          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-10-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-10-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a9b55e42f8bbcbfd33242e326f039e2955ccac81c656197bf3395e52a312c60"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 6  Overview of these rules",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "Note:\nThese rules cover a number of different sectors of the economy.  It is intended that they will be amended\nfrom time to time in the future to deal with additional sectors.\n(1) Part 1 of these rules deals with preliminary matters, such as:\n(a) definitions of terms that are used in these rules; and\n(b) the usage, in these rules, of certain terms that are defined in the Act.\nThe other provisions of these rules should be read together with these definitions\nand other interpretive provisions. Part 1 also deals with services that must be\nprovided by data holders and accredited persons that allow consumers to make\nand manage requests for CDR data.\n(2) Part 2 of these rules deals with product data requests, and should be read in\nconjunction with the relevant sector Schedule.\n(3) Part 3 of these rules deals with consumer data requests that are made by CDR\nconsumers, and should be read in conjunction with the relevant sector Schedule.\nOnly CDR consumers who are eligible to do so may make such requests. The\neligibility criteria for each sector are set out in the relevant sector Schedule.\n(4) Part 4 of these rules deals with consumer data requests that involve accredited\npersons, and should be read in conjunction with the relevant sector Schedule."
    },
    {
