      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "consumer data request:\n(a) by a CDR consumer—has the meaning given by rule 3.3; and\n(b) by an accredited person on behalf of a CDR consumer—has the meaning\ngiven by rule 4.4 or rule 4.7A.\nNote:\nThe different types of consumer data request are summarised in the following table:\nA consumer data\nrequest made under:\nis made by:\nto:\nfor disclosure of CDR\ndata to:\nrule 3.3\na CDR consumer\na data holder\nthe CDR consumer\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\nInterpretation  Division 1.3\nSection 1.7\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nA consumer data\nrequest made under:\nis made by:\nto:\nfor disclosure of CDR\ndata to:\nrule 4.4\nan accredited person on\nbehalf of a CDR\nconsumer\na data holder\nthe accredited person\nrule 4.7A\nan accredited person on\nbehalf of a CDR\nconsumer\nan accredited data\nrecipient\nthe accredited person\nconsumer experience data standards means data standards expressed to be\nconsumer experience data standards.\nExample:\nThe Data Standards Chair must make data standards about disclosure and security of\nCDR data, including consumer experience data standards for certain disclosures—see\nsubparagraphs 8.11(1)(c)(iii) to (vi).\ncurrent:\n(a) a consent is current if it has not expired in accordance with rule 4.14 or",
      "skos:definition": "consumer data request:\n(a) by a CDR consumer—has the meaning given by rule 3.3; and\n(b) by an accredited person on behalf of a CDR consumer—has the meaning\ngiven by rule 4.4 or rule 4.7A.\nNote:\nThe different types of consumer data request are summarised in the following table:\nA consumer data\nrequest made under:\nis made by:\nto:\nfor disclosure of CDR\ndata to:\nrule 3.3\na CDR consumer\na data holder\nthe CDR consumer\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\nInterpretation  Division 1.3\nSection 1.7\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nA consumer data\nrequest made under:\nis made by:\nto:\nfor disclosure of CDR\ndata to:\nrule 4.4\nan accredited person on\nbehalf of a CDR\nconsumer\na data holder\nthe accredited person\nrule 4.7A\nan accredited person on\nbehalf of a CDR\nconsumer\nan accredited data\nrecipient\nthe accredited person\nconsumer experience data standards means data standards expressed to be\nconsumer experience data standards.\nExample:\nThe Data Standards Chair must make data standards about disclosure and security of\nCDR data, including consumer experience data standards for certain disclosures—see\nsubparagraphs 8.11(1)(c)(iii) to (vi).\ncurrent:\n(a) a consent is current if it has not expired in accordance with rule 4.14 or",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "68b164b067bd7bf7a94875fc20d09035041ed402bd6a640bfd61170c68d3435e",
      "skos:note": "Consumer data request definition"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4A 13.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "consumer data request:\n(a) by a CDR consumer—has the meaning given by rule 3.3; and\n(b) by an accredited person on behalf of a CDR consumer—has the meaning\ngiven by rule 4.4 or rule 4.7A.\nNote:\nThe different types of consumer data request are summarised in the following table:\nA consumer data\nrequest made under:\nis made by:\nto:\nfor disclosure of CDR\ndata to:\nrule 3.3\na CDR consumer\na data holder\nthe CDR consumer\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\nInterpretation  Division 1.3\nSection 1.7\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nA consumer data\nrequest made under:\nis made by:\nto:\nfor disclosure of CDR\ndata to:\nrule 4.4\nan accredited person on\nbehalf of a CDR\nconsumer\na data holder\nthe accredited person\nrule 4.7A\nan accredited person on\nbehalf of a CDR\nconsumer\nan accredited data\nrecipient\nthe accredited person\nconsumer experience data standards means data standards expressed to be\nconsumer experience data standards.\nExample:\nThe Data Standards Chair must make data standards about disclosure and security of\nCDR data, including consumer experience data standards for certain disclosures—see\nsubparagraphs 8.11(1)(c)(iii) to (vi).\ncurrent:\n(a) a consent is current if it has not expired in accordance with rule 4.14 or"
    },
