      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(b) an authorisation to disclose particular CDR data is current if it has not\nexpired in accordance with rule 4.26.\nNote:\nFor paragraph (a), there are the following 3 kinds of consent:\n\ncollection consents;\n\nuse consents;\n\ndisclosure consents.\ndata holder has a meaning affected by subrule (2).\nNote:\nThe term “data holder” is defined in the Act: see subsection 56AJ of the Act. Subrule\n(2) deals with the usage of this term in these rules.\ndata minimisation principle has the meaning given by rule 1.8.\nData Standards Advisory Committee has the meaning given by rule 8.2.\nde-identification consent has the meaning given by rule 1.10A.\ndirect marketing consent has the meaning given by rule 1.10A.\ndirect or indirect OSP means a direct OSP or an indirect OSP.\ndirect OSP has the meaning given by rule 1.10.\ndirect request service has the meaning given by subrule 1.13(2).\ndisclosure consent has the meaning given by rule 1.10A.\ndisclosure option has the meaning given by rule 4A.5.\ndisclosure option management service has the meaning given by rule 4A.6.\neligible:\n(a) in relation to a particular data holder, at a particular time—has the meaning\ngiven by rule 1.10B; and",
      "skos:definition": "(b) an authorisation to disclose particular CDR data is current if it has not\nexpired in accordance with rule 4.26.\nNote:\nFor paragraph (a), there are the following 3 kinds of consent:\n\ncollection consents;\n\nuse consents;\n\ndisclosure consents.\ndata holder has a meaning affected by subrule (2).\nNote:\nThe term “data holder” is defined in the Act: see subsection 56AJ of the Act. Subrule\n(2) deals with the usage of this term in these rules.\ndata minimisation principle has the meaning given by rule 1.8.\nData Standards Advisory Committee has the meaning given by rule 8.2.\nde-identification consent has the meaning given by rule 1.10A.\ndirect marketing consent has the meaning given by rule 1.10A.\ndirect or indirect OSP means a direct OSP or an indirect OSP.\ndirect OSP has the meaning given by rule 1.10.\ndirect request service has the meaning given by subrule 1.13(2).\ndisclosure consent has the meaning given by rule 1.10A.\ndisclosure option has the meaning given by rule 4A.5.\ndisclosure option management service has the meaning given by rule 4A.6.\neligible:\n(a) in relation to a particular data holder, at a particular time—has the meaning\ngiven by rule 1.10B; and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-6-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "523198f9ab7a36c14c23685413e059c86af4bc19f61279211b0b14cdcc9b6326",
      "skos:note": "Data holder has a meaning affected by subrule (2)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20K; and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "(b) an authorisation to disclose particular CDR data is current if it has not\nexpired in accordance with rule 4.26.\nNote:\nFor paragraph (a), there are the following 3 kinds of consent:\n\ncollection consents;\n\nuse consents;\n\ndisclosure consents.\ndata holder has a meaning affected by subrule (2).\nNote:\nThe term “data holder” is defined in the Act: see subsection 56AJ of the Act. Subrule\n(2) deals with the usage of this term in these rules.\ndata minimisation principle has the meaning given by rule 1.8.\nData Standards Advisory Committee has the meaning given by rule 8.2.\nde-identification consent has the meaning given by rule 1.10A.\ndirect marketing consent has the meaning given by rule 1.10A.\ndirect or indirect OSP means a direct OSP or an indirect OSP.\ndirect OSP has the meaning given by rule 1.10.\ndirect request service has the meaning given by subrule 1.13(2).\ndisclosure consent has the meaning given by rule 1.10A.\ndisclosure option has the meaning given by rule 4A.5.\ndisclosure option management service has the meaning given by rule 4A.6.\neligible:\n(a) in relation to a particular data holder, at a particular time—has the meaning\ngiven by rule 1.10B; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-6-norm",
