    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 8  Data minimisation principle",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The collection of CDR data by an accredited person complies with the data\nminimisation principle if, when making a consumer data request on behalf of a\nCDR consumer, the accredited person does not seek to collect:\n(a) more CDR data than is reasonably needed; or\n(b) CDR data that relates to a longer time period than is reasonably needed;\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\nInterpretation  Division 1.3\nSection 1.9  Fit and proper person criteria\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nin order for it, or a relevant CDR representative, to provide the goods or services\nrequested by the CDR consumer.\n(2) The use or disclosure of CDR data by an accredited person or a CDR\nrepresentative complies with the data minimisation principle if, when providing\nthe requested goods or services, or doing any other thing that constitutes a\npermitted use or disclosure of collected CDR data, the use or disclosure of the\ncollected data, or any CDR data directly or indirectly derived from it, does not go\nbeyond what is reasonably needed in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices or to effect the permitted use or disclosure.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The collection of CDR data by an accredited person complies with the data\nminimisation principle if, when making a consumer data request on behalf of a\nCDR consumer, the accredited person does not seek to collect:\n(a) more CDR data than is reasonably needed; or\n(b) CDR data that relates to a longer time period than is reasonably needed;\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\nInterpretation  Division 1.3\nSection 1.9  Fit and proper person criteria\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nin order for it, or a relevant CDR representative, to provide the goods or services\nrequested by the CDR consumer.\n(2) The use or disclosure of CDR data by an accredited person or a CDR\nrepresentative complies with the data minimisation principle if, when providing\nthe requested goods or services, or doing any other thing that constitutes a\npermitted use or disclosure of collected CDR data, the use or disclosure of the\ncollected data, or any CDR data directly or indirectly derived from it, does not go\nbeyond what is reasonably needed in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices or to effect the permitted use or disclosure.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-13-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-13-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "15640b4389770e9b1c7af99b40cf24cc781314edf8eb1a80d67a4b72a5c5ab34"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 8  Data minimisation principle",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The collection of CDR data by an accredited person complies with the data\nminimisation principle if, when making a consumer data request on behalf of a\nCDR consumer, the accredited person does not seek to collect:\n(a) more CDR data than is reasonably needed; or\n(b) CDR data that relates to a longer time period than is reasonably needed;\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\nInterpretation  Division 1.3\nSection 1.9  Fit and proper person criteria\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nin order for it, or a relevant CDR representative, to provide the goods or services\nrequested by the CDR consumer.\n(2) The use or disclosure of CDR data by an accredited person or a CDR\nrepresentative complies with the data minimisation principle if, when providing\nthe requested goods or services, or doing any other thing that constitutes a\npermitted use or disclosure of collected CDR data, the use or disclosure of the\ncollected data, or any CDR data directly or indirectly derived from it, does not go\nbeyond what is reasonably needed in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices or to effect the permitted use or disclosure."
    },
