    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-18",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 10B  Meaning of eligible",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-18"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "Note:\nSector Schedules may add additional criteria for eligibility.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4.\n(1) A CDR consumer is eligible, in relation to a particular data holder at a particular\ntime, if, at that time:\n(a) the CDR consumer is either:\n(i) an individual who is 18 years of age or older; or\n(ii) a person who is not an individual; and\n(b) the CDR consumer is an account holder or a secondary user for an account\nwith the data holder that is open; and\n(c) any additional criteria set by the relevant sector Schedule for this subrule\nare met.\n(2) A CDR consumer is also eligible, in relation to a particular data holder at a\nparticular time, if, at that time:",
      "skos:definition": "Note:\nSector Schedules may add additional criteria for eligibility.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4.\n(1) A CDR consumer is eligible, in relation to a particular data holder at a particular\ntime, if, at that time:\n(a) the CDR consumer is either:\n(i) an individual who is 18 years of age or older; or\n(ii) a person who is not an individual; and\n(b) the CDR consumer is an account holder or a secondary user for an account\nwith the data holder that is open; and\n(c) any additional criteria set by the relevant sector Schedule for this subrule\nare met.\n(2) A CDR consumer is also eligible, in relation to a particular data holder at a\nparticular time, if, at that time:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-18-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-18-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c43b7ee8c4d493f54709d3a1a274ca37db35d8bb39146d3ae68704cdfa9c1956"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-18",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 10B  Meaning of eligible",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 35,
      "values:originalText": "Note:\nSector Schedules may add additional criteria for eligibility.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4.\n(1) A CDR consumer is eligible, in relation to a particular data holder at a particular\ntime, if, at that time:\n(a) the CDR consumer is either:\n(i) an individual who is 18 years of age or older; or\n(ii) a person who is not an individual; and\n(b) the CDR consumer is an account holder or a secondary user for an account\nwith the data holder that is open; and\n(c) any additional criteria set by the relevant sector Schedule for this subrule\nare met.\n(2) A CDR consumer is also eligible, in relation to a particular data holder at a\nparticular time, if, at that time:"
    },
