    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-20",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 10D  Meaning of sponsorship arrangement, sponsor and affiliate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-20"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A sponsorship arrangement is a written contract between a person with\nunrestricted accreditation (the sponsor) and another person (the affiliate), under\nwhich:\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\nInterpretation  Division 1.3\nSection 1.10D\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) the sponsor agrees to disclose to the affiliate, in response to a consumer\ndata request made by the affiliate in accordance with subrule 5.1B(2), CDR\ndata that it holds as an accredited data recipient; and\n(b) the affiliate undertakes to provide the sponsor with such information and\naccess to its operations as is needed for the sponsor to fulfil its obligations\nas a sponsor.\nNote:\nA person does not need to have sponsored accreditation to enter into a sponsorship\narrangement as an affiliate, but will need it to make the consumer data requests\nmentioned in paragraph (a)\n(2) A sponsorship arrangement may also provide for the sponsor to:\n(a) make consumer data requests at the request of the affiliate; or\n(b) use or disclose CDR data at the request of the affiliate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A sponsorship arrangement is a written contract between a person with\nunrestricted accreditation (the sponsor) and another person (the affiliate), under\nwhich:\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\nInterpretation  Division 1.3\nSection 1.10D\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) the sponsor agrees to disclose to the affiliate, in response to a consumer\ndata request made by the affiliate in accordance with subrule 5.1B(2), CDR\ndata that it holds as an accredited data recipient; and\n(b) the affiliate undertakes to provide the sponsor with such information and\naccess to its operations as is needed for the sponsor to fulfil its obligations\nas a sponsor.\nNote:\nA person does not need to have sponsored accreditation to enter into a sponsorship\narrangement as an affiliate, but will need it to make the consumer data requests\nmentioned in paragraph (a)\n(2) A sponsorship arrangement may also provide for the sponsor to:\n(a) make consumer data requests at the request of the affiliate; or\n(b) use or disclose CDR data at the request of the affiliate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-20-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-20-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "50018473d7943ef4c1fa3109d1589e3f48bfd7f2dedd4266655f25e1ce91e523"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-20",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 10D  Meaning of sponsorship arrangement, sponsor and affiliate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A sponsorship arrangement is a written contract between a person with\nunrestricted accreditation (the sponsor) and another person (the affiliate), under\nwhich:\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\nInterpretation  Division 1.3\nSection 1.10D\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) the sponsor agrees to disclose to the affiliate, in response to a consumer\ndata request made by the affiliate in accordance with subrule 5.1B(2), CDR\ndata that it holds as an accredited data recipient; and\n(b) the affiliate undertakes to provide the sponsor with such information and\naccess to its operations as is needed for the sponsor to fulfil its obligations\nas a sponsor.\nNote:\nA person does not need to have sponsored accreditation to enter into a sponsorship\narrangement as an affiliate, but will need it to make the consumer data requests\nmentioned in paragraph (a)\n(2) A sponsorship arrangement may also provide for the sponsor to:\n(a) make consumer data requests at the request of the affiliate; or\n(b) use or disclose CDR data at the request of the affiliate."
    },
