    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 14  Consumer dashboard—accredited person",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subrule (5), an accredited person must provide each eligible CDR\nconsumer on whose behalf the accredited person makes a consumer data request\nwith an online service that:",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subrule (5), an accredited person must provide each eligible CDR\nconsumer on whose behalf the accredited person makes a consumer data request\nwith an online service that:",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-24-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-24-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3b37d43064585fe9c7dd13c544b95ae392ac9a9cfad087358a19422d5a06e5c4",
      "skos:note": "Accredited person must provide online service to eligible consumer",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 14  Consumer dashboard—accredited person",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subrule (5), an accredited person must provide each eligible CDR\nconsumer on whose behalf the accredited person makes a consumer data request\nwith an online service that:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-24-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-24"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-24-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 15  Consumer dashboard—data holder",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a data holder receives a consumer data request from an accredited person on\nbehalf of a CDR consumer, the data holder must, in the circumstances specified\nin a sector Schedule, ensure that it provides the CDR consumer with an online\nservice that:\n(a) can be used by the CDR consumer to manage authorisations to disclose\nCDR data in response to consumer data requests; and\n(b) contains the details of each authorisation to disclose CDR data specified in\nsubrule (3); and\n(ba) contains any information in the data standards that is specified as\ninformation for the purposes of this rule; and\n(bb) contains any information on the Register of Accredited Persons that is\nspecified as information for the purposes of this rule; and\n(c) allows the CDR consumer, at any time, to withdraw a current authorisation;\nand\n(d) as part of the process of withdrawing an authorisation, displays a message,\nin accordance with the data standards, about the consequences of\nproceeding with withdrawing an authorisation; and\n(e) is simple and straightforward to use, and is no more complicated to use\nthan the process for giving the authorisation to disclose CDR data; and\n(f) is prominently displayed and readily accessible to the CDR consumer; and\n(g) contains any other details, and does anything else, required by these rules.\nNote 1:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nNote 2:\nThe circumstances are specified in the following provisions of the sector Schedules:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.3 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.3 of Schedule 4.\n(2) Such a service is the data holder’s consumer dashboard for that consumer.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a data holder receives a consumer data request from an accredited person on\nbehalf of a CDR consumer, the data holder must, in the circumstances specified\nin a sector Schedule, ensure that it provides the CDR consumer with an online\nservice that:\n(a) can be used by the CDR consumer to manage authorisations to disclose\nCDR data in response to consumer data requests; and\n(b) contains the details of each authorisation to disclose CDR data specified in\nsubrule (3); and\n(ba) contains any information in the data standards that is specified as\ninformation for the purposes of this rule; and\n(bb) contains any information on the Register of Accredited Persons that is\nspecified as information for the purposes of this rule; and\n(c) allows the CDR consumer, at any time, to withdraw a current authorisation;\nand\n(d) as part of the process of withdrawing an authorisation, displays a message,\nin accordance with the data standards, about the consequences of\nproceeding with withdrawing an authorisation; and\n(e) is simple and straightforward to use, and is no more complicated to use\nthan the process for giving the authorisation to disclose CDR data; and\n(f) is prominently displayed and readily accessible to the CDR consumer; and\n(g) contains any other details, and does anything else, required by these rules.\nNote 1:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nNote 2:\nThe circumstances are specified in the following provisions of the sector Schedules:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.3 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.3 of Schedule 4.\n(2) Such a service is the data holder’s consumer dashboard for that consumer.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-25-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-25-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dc45d278138f23d5b81b5845b42215555c5eccee2c371645c2bb96fe978336ed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 15  Consumer dashboard—data holder",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a data holder receives a consumer data request from an accredited person on\nbehalf of a CDR consumer, the data holder must, in the circumstances specified\nin a sector Schedule, ensure that it provides the CDR consumer with an online\nservice that:\n(a) can be used by the CDR consumer to manage authorisations to disclose\nCDR data in response to consumer data requests; and\n(b) contains the details of each authorisation to disclose CDR data specified in\nsubrule (3); and\n(ba) contains any information in the data standards that is specified as\ninformation for the purposes of this rule; and\n(bb) contains any information on the Register of Accredited Persons that is\nspecified as information for the purposes of this rule; and\n(c) allows the CDR consumer, at any time, to withdraw a current authorisation;\nand\n(d) as part of the process of withdrawing an authorisation, displays a message,\nin accordance with the data standards, about the consequences of\nproceeding with withdrawing an authorisation; and\n(e) is simple and straightforward to use, and is no more complicated to use\nthan the process for giving the authorisation to disclose CDR data; and\n(f) is prominently displayed and readily accessible to the CDR consumer; and\n(g) contains any other details, and does anything else, required by these rules.\nNote 1:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nNote 2:\nThe circumstances are specified in the following provisions of the sector Schedules:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.3 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.3 of Schedule 4.\n(2) Such a service is the data holder’s consumer dashboard for that consumer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-25-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
