    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 16  Obligations relating to outsourcing arrangements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "OSPs of accredited person\n(1) If an accredited person is the OSP chain principal of one or more direct or\nindirect OSPs, it must ensure that each direct and indirect OSP complies with its\nrequirements under the relevant CDR outsourcing arrangement.\n(2) The accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct OSP or indirect OSP of\nthe accredited person fails to comply with a required provision of the relevant\nCDR outsourcing arrangement.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nOSPs of CDR representative of accredited person\n(3) If an accredited person is the CDR representative principal in a CDR\nrepresentative arrangement under which it permits the CDR representative to\nengage direct or indirect OSPs, it must ensure that each such direct and indirect\nOSP complies with its requirements under the relevant CDR outsourcing\narrangement.\n(4) The accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct OSP or indirect OSP of\nthe CDR representative fails to comply with a required provision of the relevant\nCDR outsourcing arrangement.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nAccredited person acting as OSP for another accredited person\n(5) If an accredited person collects CDR data on behalf of another accredited person\n(the principal) as a direct or indirect OSP:\n(a) rules 7.4 and 7.9 apply only in relation to the principal; and\n(b) paragraph 7.10(1)(a) requires the principal to be identified.\nMeaning of required provision\n(6) For this rule, a provision of a CDR outsourcing arrangement is a required\nprovision if the arrangement would cease to be a CDR outsourcing arrangement\nunder subrule 1.10(3) if the provision were removed.",
      "skos:definition": "OSPs of accredited person\n(1) If an accredited person is the OSP chain principal of one or more direct or\nindirect OSPs, it must ensure that each direct and indirect OSP complies with its\nrequirements under the relevant CDR outsourcing arrangement.\n(2) The accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct OSP or indirect OSP of\nthe accredited person fails to comply with a required provision of the relevant\nCDR outsourcing arrangement.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nOSPs of CDR representative of accredited person\n(3) If an accredited person is the CDR representative principal in a CDR\nrepresentative arrangement under which it permits the CDR representative to\nengage direct or indirect OSPs, it must ensure that each such direct and indirect\nOSP complies with its requirements under the relevant CDR outsourcing\narrangement.\n(4) The accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct OSP or indirect OSP of\nthe CDR representative fails to comply with a required provision of the relevant\nCDR outsourcing arrangement.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nAccredited person acting as OSP for another accredited person\n(5) If an accredited person collects CDR data on behalf of another accredited person\n(the principal) as a direct or indirect OSP:\n(a) rules 7.4 and 7.9 apply only in relation to the principal; and\n(b) paragraph 7.10(1)(a) requires the principal to be identified.\nMeaning of required provision\n(6) For this rule, a provision of a CDR outsourcing arrangement is a required\nprovision if the arrangement would cease to be a CDR outsourcing arrangement\nunder subrule 1.10(3) if the provision were removed.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-26-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-26-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-26-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-26-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-26-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-26-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3eada48a14325db7ec7b9c39d655a170965485e999545815c3025a9bcc1f471e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 16  Obligations relating to outsourcing arrangements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "OSPs of accredited person\n(1) If an accredited person is the OSP chain principal of one or more direct or\nindirect OSPs, it must ensure that each direct and indirect OSP complies with its\nrequirements under the relevant CDR outsourcing arrangement.\n(2) The accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct OSP or indirect OSP of\nthe accredited person fails to comply with a required provision of the relevant\nCDR outsourcing arrangement.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nOSPs of CDR representative of accredited person\n(3) If an accredited person is the CDR representative principal in a CDR\nrepresentative arrangement under which it permits the CDR representative to\nengage direct or indirect OSPs, it must ensure that each such direct and indirect\nOSP complies with its requirements under the relevant CDR outsourcing\narrangement.\n(4) The accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct OSP or indirect OSP of\nthe CDR representative fails to comply with a required provision of the relevant\nCDR outsourcing arrangement.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nAccredited person acting as OSP for another accredited person\n(5) If an accredited person collects CDR data on behalf of another accredited person\n(the principal) as a direct or indirect OSP:\n(a) rules 7.4 and 7.9 apply only in relation to the principal; and\n(b) paragraph 7.10(1)(a) requires the principal to be identified.\nMeaning of required provision\n(6) For this rule, a provision of a CDR outsourcing arrangement is a required\nprovision if the arrangement would cease to be a CDR outsourcing arrangement\nunder subrule 1.10(3) if the provision were removed."
    },
    {
