        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-28-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9fe948cd8de6ca89a79876e7f6ecc6121c7b960bb6e5fb569c7251998b7fa491",
      "skos:note": "Delete CDR data and derived data upon impossibility of de-identification."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-28-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1(4) 17  CDR data de-identification process",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If this is not possible, the accredited data recipient must delete the relevant data\nand any CDR data directly or indirectly derived from it in accordance with the\nCDR data deletion process.\nNote:\nFor the CDR data deletion process, see rule 1.18."
    },
    {
