    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-28-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1(5) 17  CDR data de-identification process",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-28-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(5) For this rule, the DDF is The De-Identification Decision-Making Framework\npublished by the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner and Data61,\nas in force from time to time.\nNote:\nThe De-Identification Decision-Making Framework could in 2023 be downloaded from\nData61’s website (https://www.data61.csiro.au/).",
      "skos:definition": "(5) For this rule, the DDF is The De-Identification Decision-Making Framework\npublished by the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner and Data61,\nas in force from time to time.\nNote:\nThe De-Identification Decision-Making Framework could in 2023 be downloaded from\nData61’s website (https://www.data61.csiro.au/).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-28"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-28-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c46479c74b9e604be5a82ae4198464d1a23458da5ebbede684cfb3d15383fbde",
      "skos:note": "References a framework for de-identification process"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-28-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1(5) 17  CDR data de-identification process",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(5) For this rule, the DDF is The De-Identification Decision-Making Framework\npublished by the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner and Data61,\nas in force from time to time.\nNote:\nThe De-Identification Decision-Making Framework could in 2023 be downloaded from\nData61’s website (https://www.data61.csiro.au/)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-28-ss-5-norm",
