    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 17A  Identification of otherwise redundant data that is not to be deleted",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where the accredited data recipient has identified CDR data as redundant, it must\nidentify whether any of the following provisions of the Act apply to the CDR\ndata:\n(a) paragraphs 56BAA(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Act (deletion request by\nconsumer);\n(b) paragraphs 56EO(2)(b) or (c) of the Act (privacy safeguard 12).\n(2) Where one of those provisions applies, the accredited person must retain the\nCDR data while that provision applies.\n(3) For the purposes of paragraph 56BAA(2)(c) of the Act, in relation to CDR data\nof a CDR consumer, the person may:\n(a) request the CDR consumer to state whether or not proceedings of the kind\nmentioned in that paragraph are current or anticipated; and\n(b) rely on that statement.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where the accredited data recipient has identified CDR data as redundant, it must\nidentify whether any of the following provisions of the Act apply to the CDR\ndata:\n(a) paragraphs 56BAA(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Act (deletion request by\nconsumer);\n(b) paragraphs 56EO(2)(b) or (c) of the Act (privacy safeguard 12).\n(2) Where one of those provisions applies, the accredited person must retain the\nCDR data while that provision applies.\n(3) For the purposes of paragraph 56BAA(2)(c) of the Act, in relation to CDR data\nof a CDR consumer, the person may:\n(a) request the CDR consumer to state whether or not proceedings of the kind\nmentioned in that paragraph are current or anticipated; and\n(b) rely on that statement.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-29-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-29-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e77a3c78d4c7060068fa7edb76a709b3f2c4741ef22f7efa6abb65f3b3384cff"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 17A  Identification of otherwise redundant data that is not to be deleted",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where the accredited data recipient has identified CDR data as redundant, it must\nidentify whether any of the following provisions of the Act apply to the CDR\ndata:\n(a) paragraphs 56BAA(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Act (deletion request by\nconsumer);\n(b) paragraphs 56EO(2)(b) or (c) of the Act (privacy safeguard 12).\n(2) Where one of those provisions applies, the accredited person must retain the\nCDR data while that provision applies.\n(3) For the purposes of paragraph 56BAA(2)(c) of the Act, in relation to CDR data\nof a CDR consumer, the person may:\n(a) request the CDR consumer to state whether or not proceedings of the kind\nmentioned in that paragraph are current or anticipated; and\n(b) rely on that statement."
    },
