      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-30-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to delete CDR data",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-31",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 19  Eligible CDR consumers in relation to secondary data holders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-31"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "If a CDR consumer is eligible to make or initiate a consumer data request to a\nprimary data holder for SR data, the CDR consumer is not also eligible to make\nor initiate a consumer data request for that data to the secondary data holder.\nNote:\nAs a result of this rule, a secondary data holder that only holds SR data is not required\nto provide request services under rule 1.13; however, it will be required to provide a\nservice under subrule 1.20(2).",
      "skos:definition": "If a CDR consumer is eligible to make or initiate a consumer data request to a\nprimary data holder for SR data, the CDR consumer is not also eligible to make\nor initiate a consumer data request for that data to the secondary data holder.\nNote:\nAs a result of this rule, a secondary data holder that only holds SR data is not required\nto provide request services under rule 1.13; however, it will be required to provide a\nservice under subrule 1.20(2).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-31-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-31-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c6e03817fe4d849a7cf29c1359d65ddb7964829cf74792d14e7e01bcd96994fe",
      "skos:note": "Eligible CDR consumers cannot make or initiate a consumer data request for secondary data holders."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-31",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 19  Eligible CDR consumers in relation to secondary data holders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "If a CDR consumer is eligible to make or initiate a consumer data request to a\nprimary data holder for SR data, the CDR consumer is not also eligible to make\nor initiate a consumer data request for that data to the secondary data holder.\nNote:\nAs a result of this rule, a secondary data holder that only holds SR data is not required\nto provide request services under rule 1.13; however, it will be required to provide a\nservice under subrule 1.20(2)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-31-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-31"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-31-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits eligible CDR consumers from making or initiating a consumer data request for secondary data holders.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-32",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 20  Consumer data request service—primary data holders and secondary data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-32"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "holders\nPrimary data holders\n(1) Rule 1.13 (consumer data request service) applies in relation to a data holder for\nCDR data as if it were also a data holder for any SR data for which it is the\nprimary data holder.\nSecondary data holders\n(2) A secondary data holder in relation to SR data must provide an online service\nthat:\n(a) can be used by the primary data holder to request from the secondary data\nholder any SR data needed to respond to an SR data request; and\n(b) enables the requested data to be disclosed to the primary data holder in\nmachine-readable form; and\n(c) conforms with the data standards.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "holders\nPrimary data holders\n(1) Rule 1.13 (consumer data request service) applies in relation to a data holder for\nCDR data as if it were also a data holder for any SR data for which it is the\nprimary data holder.\nSecondary data holders\n(2) A secondary data holder in relation to SR data must provide an online service\nthat:\n(a) can be used by the primary data holder to request from the secondary data\nholder any SR data needed to respond to an SR data request; and\n(b) enables the requested data to be disclosed to the primary data holder in\nmachine-readable form; and\n(c) conforms with the data standards.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-32-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-32-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8aa98b2bb317ffe630850c6bdd9c965d1f49e2a53db6726fc41310d3fad6e3a3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-32",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 20  Consumer data request service—primary data holders and secondary data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "holders\nPrimary data holders\n(1) Rule 1.13 (consumer data request service) applies in relation to a data holder for\nCDR data as if it were also a data holder for any SR data for which it is the\nprimary data holder.\nSecondary data holders\n(2) A secondary data holder in relation to SR data must provide an online service\nthat:\n(a) can be used by the primary data holder to request from the secondary data\nholder any SR data needed to respond to an SR data request; and\n(b) enables the requested data to be disclosed to the primary data holder in\nmachine-readable form; and\n(c) conforms with the data standards.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
