    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-36",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 Section 1",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-36"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "24  SR data disclosed to primary data holder not to be used for other purposes\n(1) A primary data holder must not use the service mentioned in subrule 1.20(2)\nother than to request SR data that it needs to respond to an SR data request.\n(2) Where a secondary data holder provides SR data to a primary data holder in\nresponse to such a request:\n(a) the primary data holder must not use or disclose the SR data for a purpose\nother than responding to the SR data request; and\n(b) once the primary data holder has responded to the SR data request, it must\ndelete any of the SR data that it holds in accordance with the CDR data\ndeletion process.\nNote :\nSee rule 1.18 for the definition of “CDR data deletion process”.",
      "skos:definition": "24  SR data disclosed to primary data holder not to be used for other purposes\n(1) A primary data holder must not use the service mentioned in subrule 1.20(2)\nother than to request SR data that it needs to respond to an SR data request.\n(2) Where a secondary data holder provides SR data to a primary data holder in\nresponse to such a request:\n(a) the primary data holder must not use or disclose the SR data for a purpose\nother than responding to the SR data request; and\n(b) once the primary data holder has responded to the SR data request, it must\ndelete any of the SR data that it holds in accordance with the CDR data\ndeletion process.\nNote :\nSee rule 1.18 for the definition of “CDR data deletion process”.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-36-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-36-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ddc31245e0b0f16e3968e16f0a0c13ee6ac391d714930c8e158bcf50549f1299"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-36",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 Section 1",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "24  SR data disclosed to primary data holder not to be used for other purposes\n(1) A primary data holder must not use the service mentioned in subrule 1.20(2)\nother than to request SR data that it needs to respond to an SR data request.\n(2) Where a secondary data holder provides SR data to a primary data holder in\nresponse to such a request:\n(a) the primary data holder must not use or disclose the SR data for a purpose\nother than responding to the SR data request; and\n(b) once the primary data holder has responded to the SR data request, it must\ndelete any of the SR data that it holds in accordance with the CDR data\ndeletion process.\nNote :\nSee rule 1.18 for the definition of “CDR data deletion process”."
    },
