    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-3-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 5  Refusal to disclose required consumer data in response to consumer data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-3-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "request\n(1) Despite subrule 3.4(3), the data holder may refuse to disclose required consumer\ndata in response to the request:\n(a) if the data holder considers this to be necessary to prevent physical,\npsychological or financial harm or abuse; or\n(aa) in relation to an account that is blocked or suspended; or\n(b) in circumstances (if any) set out in the data standards.\n(2) The data holder must inform the CDR consumer of such a refusal in accordance\nwith the data standards.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nPreliminary  Division 4.1\nSection 4.1\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "skos:definition": "request\n(1) Despite subrule 3.4(3), the data holder may refuse to disclose required consumer\ndata in response to the request:\n(a) if the data holder considers this to be necessary to prevent physical,\npsychological or financial harm or abuse; or\n(aa) in relation to an account that is blocked or suspended; or\n(b) in circumstances (if any) set out in the data standards.\n(2) The data holder must inform the CDR consumer of such a refusal in accordance\nwith the data standards.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nPreliminary  Division 4.1\nSection 4.1\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
