      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The request ceases to be valid if the collection consent is withdrawn.\nNote:\nSo long as the use consent is not also withdrawn, the accredited person could continue\nto use CDR data it had already collected in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices. However, the notification requirement of rule 4.18A would apply.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The request ceases to be valid if the collection consent is withdrawn.\nNote:\nSo long as the use consent is not also withdrawn, the accredited person could continue\nto use CDR data it had already collected in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices. However, the notification requirement of rule 4.18A would apply.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-9"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-9-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-9-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2e78a5341dfefb990b5c82b4b45c761afed03031e6067d73ab813e9d851e1f43",
      "skos:note": "Collection consent must be withdrawn for request to cease being valid."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-9-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(4) 3  Request for accredited person to seek to collect CDR data",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The request ceases to be valid if the collection consent is withdrawn.\nNote:\nSo long as the use consent is not also withdrawn, the accredited person could continue\nto use CDR data it had already collected in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices. However, the notification requirement of rule 4.18A would apply."
    },
