      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(4) Section 4",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In giving the consents, the CDR consumer gives the CDR representative\nprincipal a valid request to seek to collect that CDR data from the CDR\nparticipant.\nNote:\nIf an accredited person seeks to collect CDR data under this Part without a valid\nrequest, it will contravene privacy safeguard 3 (a civil penalty provision under the Act):\nsee section 56EF of the Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In giving the consents, the CDR consumer gives the CDR representative\nprincipal a valid request to seek to collect that CDR data from the CDR\nparticipant.\nNote:\nIf an accredited person seeks to collect CDR data under this Part without a valid\nrequest, it will contravene privacy safeguard 3 (a civil penalty provision under the Act):\nsee section 56EF of the Act.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "28f29a2c8bb124821140f8fe30e79c2e05ef3b7becd8e54660aff94682ddcaf2",
      "skos:note": "Request to collect CDR data must be valid"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(4) Section 4",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In giving the consents, the CDR consumer gives the CDR representative\nprincipal a valid request to seek to collect that CDR data from the CDR\nparticipant.\nNote:\nIf an accredited person seeks to collect CDR data under this Part without a valid\nrequest, it will contravene privacy safeguard 3 (a civil penalty provision under the Act):\nsee section 56EF of the Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Valid request required",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(5) Section 4",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The request ceases to be valid if the collection consent is withdrawn.\nNote:\nSo long as the use consent is not also withdrawn, the CDR representative principal\ncould continue to disclose CDR data it had already collected to the CDR representative,\nand the CDR representative could use it in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices. However, the notification requirement of rule 4.20O would apply.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons to CDR participants  Division 4.2\nSection 4.3B\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The request ceases to be valid if the collection consent is withdrawn.\nNote:\nSo long as the use consent is not also withdrawn, the CDR representative principal\ncould continue to disclose CDR data it had already collected to the CDR representative,\nand the CDR representative could use it in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices. However, the notification requirement of rule 4.20O would apply.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons to CDR participants  Division 4.2\nSection 4.3B\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9c52ad0b0d2d648f8a64a85d469709897d46ae36a32d80763bab5641781f375d",
      "skos:note": "Request ceases to be valid if collection consent is withdrawn."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(5) Section 4",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The request ceases to be valid if the collection consent is withdrawn.\nNote:\nSo long as the use consent is not also withdrawn, the CDR representative principal\ncould continue to disclose CDR data it had already collected to the CDR representative,\nand the CDR representative could use it in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices. However, the notification requirement of rule 4.20O would apply.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons to CDR participants  Division 4.2\nSection 4.3B\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-10-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits request validity upon withdrawal of collection consent.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 3B  Consumer data requests by accredited persons to CDR representatives",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "Note:\nSubrule (1) allows an accredited person to make a consumer data request to a CDR representative as if\nthe latter were also an accredited person.\nSubrule (2) allows a CDR representative that receives such a consumer data request to obtain a\ndisclosure consent from the consumer. Under paragraphs 7.5(1)(i) and (j), the CDR representative is then\nable to disclose the requested data.\nApplication of rule 4.7A to CDR representative holding service data\n(1) Rule 4.7A applies in relation to a CDR representative that holds service data as\nif:\n(a) a reference to CDR data were a reference to CDR data included in the\nservice data; and\n(b) a reference to an accredited data recipient were a reference to the CDR\nrepresentative.\nApplication of rule 4.7B to CDR representative receiving request for service data\n(2) Rule 4.7B applies in relation to a CDR representative that receives, or reasonably\nanticipates receiving, a consumer data request under rule 4.7A as applied by\nsubrule (1), as if:\n(a) a reference to an accredited data recipient were a reference to the CDR\nrepresentative; and\n(b) a reference to Division 4.3 were a reference to Division 4.3A.\nSubdivision 4.2.3—Consumer data requests by accredited persons to data\nholders",
      "skos:definition": "Note:\nSubrule (1) allows an accredited person to make a consumer data request to a CDR representative as if\nthe latter were also an accredited person.\nSubrule (2) allows a CDR representative that receives such a consumer data request to obtain a\ndisclosure consent from the consumer. Under paragraphs 7.5(1)(i) and (j), the CDR representative is then\nable to disclose the requested data.\nApplication of rule 4.7A to CDR representative holding service data\n(1) Rule 4.7A applies in relation to a CDR representative that holds service data as\nif:\n(a) a reference to CDR data were a reference to CDR data included in the\nservice data; and\n(b) a reference to an accredited data recipient were a reference to the CDR\nrepresentative.\nApplication of rule 4.7B to CDR representative receiving request for service data\n(2) Rule 4.7B applies in relation to a CDR representative that receives, or reasonably\nanticipates receiving, a consumer data request under rule 4.7A as applied by\nsubrule (1), as if:\n(a) a reference to an accredited data recipient were a reference to the CDR\nrepresentative; and\n(b) a reference to Division 4.3 were a reference to Division 4.3A.\nSubdivision 4.2.3—Consumer data requests by accredited persons to data\nholders",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-11-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-11-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "32dcdcfea5ae0bcbc9b7bee236a2f8736c89d5b28d330fa5562d759762ce4ee0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 3B  Consumer data requests by accredited persons to CDR representatives",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "Note:\nSubrule (1) allows an accredited person to make a consumer data request to a CDR representative as if\nthe latter were also an accredited person.\nSubrule (2) allows a CDR representative that receives such a consumer data request to obtain a\ndisclosure consent from the consumer. Under paragraphs 7.5(1)(i) and (j), the CDR representative is then\nable to disclose the requested data.\nApplication of rule 4.7A to CDR representative holding service data\n(1) Rule 4.7A applies in relation to a CDR representative that holds service data as\nif:\n(a) a reference to CDR data were a reference to CDR data included in the\nservice data; and\n(b) a reference to an accredited data recipient were a reference to the CDR\nrepresentative.\nApplication of rule 4.7B to CDR representative receiving request for service data\n(2) Rule 4.7B applies in relation to a CDR representative that receives, or reasonably\nanticipates receiving, a consumer data request under rule 4.7A as applied by\nsubrule (1), as if:\n(a) a reference to an accredited data recipient were a reference to the CDR\nrepresentative; and\n(b) a reference to Division 4.3 were a reference to Division 4.3A.\nSubdivision 4.2.3—Consumer data requests by accredited persons to data\nholders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-11-ss-1",
