      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 3A to seek to collect CDR data from a data holder; and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "(b) the request is valid;\nthe accredited person may request the data holder to disclose, to the accredited\nperson, some or all of the CDR data that:\n(c) is the subject of the relevant collection consent, use consent and disclosure\nconsent; and\n(d) can be collected, used and disclosed in compliance with the data\nminimisation principle.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.8 for the definition of the “data minimisation principle”.\n(2) Such a request is a consumer data request by an accredited person to a data\nholder on behalf of a CDR consumer.\nNote 1:\nAn accredited person might need to make consumer data requests to several CDR\nparticipants in order to provide the goods or services requested by the CDR consumer,\nand might need to make regular consumer data requests over a period of time in order\nto provide those goods or services.\nNote 2:\nThese rules will progressively permit consumer data requests to be made in relation to\nCDR data held by a broader range of data holders within the banking sector and",
      "skos:definition": "(b) the request is valid;\nthe accredited person may request the data holder to disclose, to the accredited\nperson, some or all of the CDR data that:\n(c) is the subject of the relevant collection consent, use consent and disclosure\nconsent; and\n(d) can be collected, used and disclosed in compliance with the data\nminimisation principle.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.8 for the definition of the “data minimisation principle”.\n(2) Such a request is a consumer data request by an accredited person to a data\nholder on behalf of a CDR consumer.\nNote 1:\nAn accredited person might need to make consumer data requests to several CDR\nparticipants in order to provide the goods or services requested by the CDR consumer,\nand might need to make regular consumer data requests over a period of time in order\nto provide those goods or services.\nNote 2:\nThese rules will progressively permit consumer data requests to be made in relation to\nCDR data held by a broader range of data holders within the banking sector and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-13-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-13-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0d0c1c2db7f8134e919d267c306ec3d66fe659abc38319860116c72103ab3047",
      "skos:note": "Accredited person must request data holder to disclose CDR data in compliance with data minimisation principle.",
      "dc:description": "Data disclosure"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 3A to seek to collect CDR data from a data holder; and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "(b) the request is valid;\nthe accredited person may request the data holder to disclose, to the accredited\nperson, some or all of the CDR data that:\n(c) is the subject of the relevant collection consent, use consent and disclosure\nconsent; and\n(d) can be collected, used and disclosed in compliance with the data\nminimisation principle.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.8 for the definition of the “data minimisation principle”.\n(2) Such a request is a consumer data request by an accredited person to a data\nholder on behalf of a CDR consumer.\nNote 1:\nAn accredited person might need to make consumer data requests to several CDR\nparticipants in order to provide the goods or services requested by the CDR consumer,\nand might need to make regular consumer data requests over a period of time in order\nto provide those goods or services.\nNote 2:\nThese rules will progressively permit consumer data requests to be made in relation to\nCDR data held by a broader range of data holders within the banking sector and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-13-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-13"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-13-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Accredited person must request data holder to disclose CDR data.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-14",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 5  Data holder must ask eligible CDR consumer to authorise disclosure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-14"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) a data holder receives a consumer data request under rule 4.4; and\n(b) there is no current authorisation for the data holder to disclose the\nrequested data to the person who made the request; and\n(c) the data holder reasonably believes that the request was made by an\naccredited person on behalf of an eligible CDR consumer.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “eligible”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4.\n(2) If the data holder is considering disclosing any of the requested voluntary\nconsumer data, the data holder must ask the CDR consumer on whose behalf the\nrequest was made to authorise the disclosure:\n(a) in accordance with Division 4.4; and\n(b) in accordance with the data standards.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “voluntary consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The data holder must, subject to rule 4.7, ask the CDR consumer on whose\nbehalf the request was made to authorise the disclosure of any requested required\nconsumer data:\n(a) in accordance with Division 4.4; and\n(b) in accordance with the data standards.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “required consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) a data holder receives a consumer data request under rule 4.4; and\n(b) there is no current authorisation for the data holder to disclose the\nrequested data to the person who made the request; and\n(c) the data holder reasonably believes that the request was made by an\naccredited person on behalf of an eligible CDR consumer.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “eligible”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4.\n(2) If the data holder is considering disclosing any of the requested voluntary\nconsumer data, the data holder must ask the CDR consumer on whose behalf the\nrequest was made to authorise the disclosure:\n(a) in accordance with Division 4.4; and\n(b) in accordance with the data standards.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “voluntary consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The data holder must, subject to rule 4.7, ask the CDR consumer on whose\nbehalf the request was made to authorise the disclosure of any requested required\nconsumer data:\n(a) in accordance with Division 4.4; and\n(b) in accordance with the data standards.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “required consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-14-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-14-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-14-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "06bc75abdf1af3dde2da19772a387bad86f299cd136cc60e60bd619e10937197"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-14",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 5  Data holder must ask eligible CDR consumer to authorise disclosure",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) a data holder receives a consumer data request under rule 4.4; and\n(b) there is no current authorisation for the data holder to disclose the\nrequested data to the person who made the request; and\n(c) the data holder reasonably believes that the request was made by an\naccredited person on behalf of an eligible CDR consumer.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “eligible”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4.\n(2) If the data holder is considering disclosing any of the requested voluntary\nconsumer data, the data holder must ask the CDR consumer on whose behalf the\nrequest was made to authorise the disclosure:\n(a) in accordance with Division 4.4; and\n(b) in accordance with the data standards.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “voluntary consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The data holder must, subject to rule 4.7, ask the CDR consumer on whose\nbehalf the request was made to authorise the disclosure of any requested required\nconsumer data:\n(a) in accordance with Division 4.4; and\n(b) in accordance with the data standards.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “required consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
