      "skos:note": "Must ask eligible CDR consumer to authorise disclosure of requested data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-14-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(3) 5  Data holder must ask eligible CDR consumer to authorise disclosure",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The data holder must, subject to rule 4.7, ask the CDR consumer on whose\nbehalf the request was made to authorise the disclosure of any requested required\nconsumer data:\n(a) in accordance with Division 4.4; and\n(b) in accordance with the data standards.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “required consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
    {
