      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The data holder may, subject to rule 4.6A, disclose, to the person who made the\nrequest, any of the requested voluntary consumer data that it is authorised to\ndisclose.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “voluntary consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nFor requests that relate to joint accounts, additional requirements need to be met in\norder for the data holder to be authorised to disclose requested CDR data that relates to\nthe joint account: see Part 4A.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The data holder may, subject to rule 4.6A, disclose, to the person who made the\nrequest, any of the requested voluntary consumer data that it is authorised to\ndisclose.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “voluntary consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nFor requests that relate to joint accounts, additional requirements need to be met in\norder for the data holder to be authorised to disclose requested CDR data that relates to\nthe joint account: see Part 4A.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-15"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-15-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c7e2d48248c9f2cf1b17d5367f89bf0e914199537204e45e956116663cf013be",
      "skos:note": "Data holder may disclose requested voluntary consumer data under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-15-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(2) 6  Disclosing consumer data in response to a consumer data request",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The data holder may, subject to rule 4.6A, disclose, to the person who made the\nrequest, any of the requested voluntary consumer data that it is authorised to\ndisclose.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “voluntary consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nFor requests that relate to joint accounts, additional requirements need to be met in\norder for the data holder to be authorised to disclose requested CDR data that relates to\nthe joint account: see Part 4A."
    },
