      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-15-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(4) 6  Disclosing consumer data in response to a consumer data request",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-15-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The data holder must, subject to rule 4.6A and rule 4.7, disclose, to the person\nwho made the request, the requested required consumer data that it is authorised\nto disclose:\n(a) through its accredited person request service; and\n(b) in accordance with the data standards.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “required consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nFor requests that relate to joint accounts, additional requirements need to be met in\norder for the data holder to be authorised to disclose requested CDR data that relates to\nthe joint account: see Part 4A.\nNote 3:\nA fee cannot be charged for the disclosure of required consumer data: see section 56BU\nof the Act.\nNote 4:\nRule 7.4 (which deals with privacy safeguard 5, paragraph 56EH(a) of the Act) requires\nthe accredited person to update its consumer dashboard for the CDR consumer on\nwhose behalf the request was made to indicate the CDR data that was collected.\nNote 5:\nRule 7.9 (which deals with privacy safeguard 10, paragraph 56EM(1)(a) of the Act)\nrequires the data holder to update its consumer dashboard for the CDR consumer on\nwhose behalf the request was made to indicate the CDR data that was disclosed.\nNote 6:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The data holder must, subject to rule 4.6A and rule 4.7, disclose, to the person\nwho made the request, the requested required consumer data that it is authorised\nto disclose:\n(a) through its accredited person request service; and\n(b) in accordance with the data standards.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “required consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nFor requests that relate to joint accounts, additional requirements need to be met in\norder for the data holder to be authorised to disclose requested CDR data that relates to\nthe joint account: see Part 4A.\nNote 3:\nA fee cannot be charged for the disclosure of required consumer data: see section 56BU\nof the Act.\nNote 4:\nRule 7.4 (which deals with privacy safeguard 5, paragraph 56EH(a) of the Act) requires\nthe accredited person to update its consumer dashboard for the CDR consumer on\nwhose behalf the request was made to indicate the CDR data that was collected.\nNote 5:\nRule 7.9 (which deals with privacy safeguard 10, paragraph 56EM(1)(a) of the Act)\nrequires the data holder to update its consumer dashboard for the CDR consumer on\nwhose behalf the request was made to indicate the CDR data that was disclosed.\nNote 6:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-15"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-15-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-15-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e9d3c8b992396084cbef3b2a09b6715cff2bd3e40ddf53ea679cdd82271f6ad3",
      "skos:note": "Data holder must disclose required consumer data to the person who made the request.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-15-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(4) 6  Disclosing consumer data in response to a consumer data request",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The data holder must, subject to rule 4.6A and rule 4.7, disclose, to the person\nwho made the request, the requested required consumer data that it is authorised\nto disclose:\n(a) through its accredited person request service; and\n(b) in accordance with the data standards.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “required consumer data”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 3.2 of Schedule 4.\nNote 2:\nFor requests that relate to joint accounts, additional requirements need to be met in\norder for the data holder to be authorised to disclose requested CDR data that relates to\nthe joint account: see Part 4A.\nNote 3:\nA fee cannot be charged for the disclosure of required consumer data: see section 56BU\nof the Act.\nNote 4:\nRule 7.4 (which deals with privacy safeguard 5, paragraph 56EH(a) of the Act) requires\nthe accredited person to update its consumer dashboard for the CDR consumer on\nwhose behalf the request was made to indicate the CDR data that was collected.\nNote 5:\nRule 7.9 (which deals with privacy safeguard 10, paragraph 56EM(1)(a) of the Act)\nrequires the data holder to update its consumer dashboard for the CDR consumer on\nwhose behalf the request was made to indicate the CDR data that was disclosed.\nNote 6:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-15-ss-4-norm",
