    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-16",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Section 4",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-16"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "6A  Disclosure of CDR data relating to account not permitted if not approved\nby account holder\nDespite subrules 4.6(2) and (4), the data holder must not disclose requested CDR\ndata that relates to a particular account to the person who made the request if:\n(a) both of the following are satisfied:\n(i) the request was made on behalf of a secondary user of the account;\n(ii) the account holder has indicated, through their consumer dashboard,\nthat they no longer approve CDR data relating to that account being\ndisclosed to that accredited person in response to consumer data\nrequests made by that secondary user; or",
      "skos:definition": "6A  Disclosure of CDR data relating to account not permitted if not approved\nby account holder\nDespite subrules 4.6(2) and (4), the data holder must not disclose requested CDR\ndata that relates to a particular account to the person who made the request if:\n(a) both of the following are satisfied:\n(i) the request was made on behalf of a secondary user of the account;\n(ii) the account holder has indicated, through their consumer dashboard,\nthat they no longer approve CDR data relating to that account being\ndisclosed to that accredited person in response to consumer data\nrequests made by that secondary user; or",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-16-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-16-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "288ec0da35cb7dc15d3e7371f93df8256d0bba0a73e52545b05bacfcf511a1d3",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of CDR data is not permitted without account holder's approval."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-16",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Section 4",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "6A  Disclosure of CDR data relating to account not permitted if not approved\nby account holder\nDespite subrules 4.6(2) and (4), the data holder must not disclose requested CDR\ndata that relates to a particular account to the person who made the request if:\n(a) both of the following are satisfied:\n(i) the request was made on behalf of a secondary user of the account;\n(ii) the account holder has indicated, through their consumer dashboard,\nthat they no longer approve CDR data relating to that account being\ndisclosed to that accredited person in response to consumer data\nrequests made by that secondary user; or"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-16-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-16"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-16-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Account holder's approval is required."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 7  Refusal to disclose required consumer data in response to consumer data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "request\n(1) Despite subrules 4.5(3), 4.6(4) and 4.22A(1), a data holder may refuse to ask for\nan authorisation in relation to the relevant CDR data, to invite a CDR consumer\nto amend the authorisation, or to disclose required consumer data in response to\nthe request:\n(a) if the data holder considers this to be necessary to prevent physical,\npsychological or financial harm or abuse; or\n(b) if the data holder has reasonable grounds to believe that disclosure of some\nor all of that data would adversely impact the security, integrity or stability\nof:\n(i) the Register of Accredited Persons; or\n(ii) the data holder’s information and communication technology systems;\nor\n(c) in relation to an account that is blocked or suspended; or\n(d) in circumstances (if any) set out in the data standards; or\n(e) if the disclosure of some or all of that CDR data would not be permitted\nbecause of another provision of these rules.\n(3) The data holder must inform the accredited person of such a refusal in\naccordance with the data standards.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\nSubdivision 4.2.4—Consumer data requests by accredited persons to\naccredited data recipients",
      "skos:definition": "request\n(1) Despite subrules 4.5(3), 4.6(4) and 4.22A(1), a data holder may refuse to ask for\nan authorisation in relation to the relevant CDR data, to invite a CDR consumer\nto amend the authorisation, or to disclose required consumer data in response to\nthe request:\n(a) if the data holder considers this to be necessary to prevent physical,\npsychological or financial harm or abuse; or\n(b) if the data holder has reasonable grounds to believe that disclosure of some\nor all of that data would adversely impact the security, integrity or stability\nof:\n(i) the Register of Accredited Persons; or\n(ii) the data holder’s information and communication technology systems;\nor\n(c) in relation to an account that is blocked or suspended; or\n(d) in circumstances (if any) set out in the data standards; or\n(e) if the disclosure of some or all of that CDR data would not be permitted\nbecause of another provision of these rules.\n(3) The data holder must inform the accredited person of such a refusal in\naccordance with the data standards.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\nSubdivision 4.2.4—Consumer data requests by accredited persons to\naccredited data recipients",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-17-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1f58b9145b24d108d7ac38887338b3ea3229833b9c1e418250343f907bfd1047"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 7  Refusal to disclose required consumer data in response to consumer data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "request\n(1) Despite subrules 4.5(3), 4.6(4) and 4.22A(1), a data holder may refuse to ask for\nan authorisation in relation to the relevant CDR data, to invite a CDR consumer\nto amend the authorisation, or to disclose required consumer data in response to\nthe request:\n(a) if the data holder considers this to be necessary to prevent physical,\npsychological or financial harm or abuse; or\n(b) if the data holder has reasonable grounds to believe that disclosure of some\nor all of that data would adversely impact the security, integrity or stability\nof:\n(i) the Register of Accredited Persons; or\n(ii) the data holder’s information and communication technology systems;\nor\n(c) in relation to an account that is blocked or suspended; or\n(d) in circumstances (if any) set out in the data standards; or\n(e) if the disclosure of some or all of that CDR data would not be permitted\nbecause of another provision of these rules.\n(3) The data holder must inform the accredited person of such a refusal in\naccordance with the data standards.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\nSubdivision 4.2.4—Consumer data requests by accredited persons to\naccredited data recipients"
    },
