    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-19",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Section 4",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-19"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "3A to seek to collect CDR data from an accredited data recipient; and\n(b) the request is valid;\nthe accredited person may request the accredited data recipient to disclose, to the\naccredited person, some or all of the CDR data that:\n(c) is the subject of the relevant collection consent, use consent and disclosure\nconsent; and\n(d) can be collected, used and disclosed in compliance with the data\nminimisation principle.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.8 for the definition of the “data minimisation principle”.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons to CDR participants  Division 4.2\nSection 4.7A\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(2) Such a request is a consumer data request by an accredited person to an\naccredited data recipient on behalf of a CDR consumer.\nNote:\nAn accredited person might need to make consumer data requests to several CDR\nparticipants in order to provide the goods or services requested by the CDR consumer,\nand might need to make regular consumer data requests over a period of time in order\nto provide those goods or services.",
      "skos:definition": "3A to seek to collect CDR data from an accredited data recipient; and\n(b) the request is valid;\nthe accredited person may request the accredited data recipient to disclose, to the\naccredited person, some or all of the CDR data that:\n(c) is the subject of the relevant collection consent, use consent and disclosure\nconsent; and\n(d) can be collected, used and disclosed in compliance with the data\nminimisation principle.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.8 for the definition of the “data minimisation principle”.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons to CDR participants  Division 4.2\nSection 4.7A\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(2) Such a request is a consumer data request by an accredited person to an\naccredited data recipient on behalf of a CDR consumer.\nNote:\nAn accredited person might need to make consumer data requests to several CDR\nparticipants in order to provide the goods or services requested by the CDR consumer,\nand might need to make regular consumer data requests over a period of time in order\nto provide those goods or services.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-19-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-19-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2467f518fdbf159e166cfae47685b7ce589614a773cd63b87915bb3c862c89bd",
      "skos:note": "Accredited person must request CDR data from accredited data recipient."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-19",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Section 4",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "3A to seek to collect CDR data from an accredited data recipient; and\n(b) the request is valid;\nthe accredited person may request the accredited data recipient to disclose, to the\naccredited person, some or all of the CDR data that:\n(c) is the subject of the relevant collection consent, use consent and disclosure\nconsent; and\n(d) can be collected, used and disclosed in compliance with the data\nminimisation principle.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.8 for the definition of the “data minimisation principle”.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons to CDR participants  Division 4.2\nSection 4.7A\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(2) Such a request is a consumer data request by an accredited person to an\naccredited data recipient on behalf of a CDR consumer.\nNote:\nAn accredited person might need to make consumer data requests to several CDR\nparticipants in order to provide the goods or services requested by the CDR consumer,\nand might need to make regular consumer data requests over a period of time in order\nto provide those goods or services."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-19-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-19"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-19-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Accredited person must request CDR data.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-20",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 7B  Accredited data recipient may ask eligible CDR consumer for AP",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-20"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.67",
      "values:originalText": "disclosure consent\n(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) an accredited data recipient receives, or reasonably anticipates receiving, a\nconsumer data request under rule 4.7A; and\n(b) there is no current AP disclosure consent for the accredited data recipient\nto disclose the requested data to the person who made the request; and\n(c) the accredited data recipient reasonably believes that the request was or\nwill be made by an accredited person on behalf of an eligible CDR\nconsumer.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “eligible”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4.\n(2) The accredited data recipient may, in accordance with Division 4.3, ask the CDR\nconsumer for such an AP disclosure consent.\nNote:\nIf the CDR consumer consents to the disclosure, the accredited data recipient is\nauthorised (but not required) to disclose the requested CDR data to the accredited\nperson: see paragraph 7.5(1)(h) and rules 7.6, 7.7 and 7.8.\n(3) If an accredited data recipient asks for an AP disclosure consent for the purposes\nof subrule (2), it must do so in accordance with Division 4.3.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "disclosure consent\n(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) an accredited data recipient receives, or reasonably anticipates receiving, a\nconsumer data request under rule 4.7A; and\n(b) there is no current AP disclosure consent for the accredited data recipient\nto disclose the requested data to the person who made the request; and\n(c) the accredited data recipient reasonably believes that the request was or\nwill be made by an accredited person on behalf of an eligible CDR\nconsumer.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “eligible”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4.\n(2) The accredited data recipient may, in accordance with Division 4.3, ask the CDR\nconsumer for such an AP disclosure consent.\nNote:\nIf the CDR consumer consents to the disclosure, the accredited data recipient is\nauthorised (but not required) to disclose the requested CDR data to the accredited\nperson: see paragraph 7.5(1)(h) and rules 7.6, 7.7 and 7.8.\n(3) If an accredited data recipient asks for an AP disclosure consent for the purposes\nof subrule (2), it must do so in accordance with Division 4.3.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-20-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-20-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-20-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f27659200be540601251fddeb8d374fd8f5ab09f72886a96414f6aacd206f6be"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-20",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 7B  Accredited data recipient may ask eligible CDR consumer for AP",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 67,
      "values:originalText": "disclosure consent\n(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) an accredited data recipient receives, or reasonably anticipates receiving, a\nconsumer data request under rule 4.7A; and\n(b) there is no current AP disclosure consent for the accredited data recipient\nto disclose the requested data to the person who made the request; and\n(c) the accredited data recipient reasonably believes that the request was or\nwill be made by an accredited person on behalf of an eligible CDR\nconsumer.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “eligible”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4.\n(2) The accredited data recipient may, in accordance with Division 4.3, ask the CDR\nconsumer for such an AP disclosure consent.\nNote:\nIf the CDR consumer consents to the disclosure, the accredited data recipient is\nauthorised (but not required) to disclose the requested CDR data to the accredited\nperson: see paragraph 7.5(1)(h) and rules 7.6, 7.7 and 7.8.\n(3) If an accredited data recipient asks for an AP disclosure consent for the purposes\nof subrule (2), it must do so in accordance with Division 4.3.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
    {
