        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-20-ss-1-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7826bf6d5fd1b9cef9bd1c06a891e91e156715917791b68339771c92a65a17c4",
      "skos:note": "Accredited data recipient must disclose AP to eligible CDR consumer if requested.",
      "dc:description": "AP disclosure consent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-20-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(1) 7B  Accredited data recipient may ask eligible CDR consumer for AP",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 67,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) an accredited data recipient receives, or reasonably anticipates receiving, a\nconsumer data request under rule 4.7A; and\n(b) there is no current AP disclosure consent for the accredited data recipient\nto disclose the requested data to the person who made the request; and\n(c) the accredited data recipient reasonably believes that the request was or\nwill be made by an accredited person on behalf of an eligible CDR\nconsumer.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “eligible”.  See also:\n•\nfor the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3;\n•\nfor the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4."
    },
    {
