    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 8  Purpose of Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "This Division deals with:\n(a) giving collection consents, use consents and disclosure consents to\naccredited persons; and\n(b) amending such consents; and\n(c) related matters.\nNote:\nThis Division does not cover collection consents for accredited persons to collect CDR\ndata on behalf of CDR representatives; since those consents are given to the CDR\nrepresentatives, they are covered by Division 4.3A.",
      "skos:definition": "This Division deals with:\n(a) giving collection consents, use consents and disclosure consents to\naccredited persons; and\n(b) amending such consents; and\n(c) related matters.\nNote:\nThis Division does not cover collection consents for accredited persons to collect CDR\ndata on behalf of CDR representatives; since those consents are given to the CDR\nrepresentatives, they are covered by Division 4.3A.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-21-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-21-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "75885c13060171a5221e742854adc34f3ae8a265c510b3226de72d531ccb5bbe",
      "skos:note": "Provides collection consents, use consents and disclosure consents to accredited persons."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 8  Purpose of Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "This Division deals with:\n(a) giving collection consents, use consents and disclosure consents to\naccredited persons; and\n(b) amending such consents; and\n(c) related matters.\nNote:\nThis Division does not cover collection consents for accredited persons to collect CDR\ndata on behalf of CDR representatives; since those consents are given to the CDR\nrepresentatives, they are covered by Division 4.3A."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-21-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-21"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-21-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines the scope of collection consents.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-22",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 9  Object",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-22"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "The object of this Division is to ensure that a consent is:\n(a) voluntary; and\n(b) express; and\n(c) informed; and\n(d) specific as to purpose; and\n(e) time limited; and\n(f) easily withdrawn.\nSubdivision 4.3.2—Giving consents\nNote:\nUnder rule 4.3, if an accredited person asks a CDR consumer for their consent to collect and use their\nCDR data, it must do so in accordance with this Division, and in particular, rules 4.10, 4.11 and 4.12. A\nfailure to do so could contravene one or more civil penalty provisions: see section 56EF of the Act and\nrule 4.3.",
      "skos:definition": "The object of this Division is to ensure that a consent is:\n(a) voluntary; and\n(b) express; and\n(c) informed; and\n(d) specific as to purpose; and\n(e) time limited; and\n(f) easily withdrawn.\nSubdivision 4.3.2—Giving consents\nNote:\nUnder rule 4.3, if an accredited person asks a CDR consumer for their consent to collect and use their\nCDR data, it must do so in accordance with this Division, and in particular, rules 4.10, 4.11 and 4.12. A\nfailure to do so could contravene one or more civil penalty provisions: see section 56EF of the Act and\nrule 4.3.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-22-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-22-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-22-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "56a5999208577e05394ba1cd33f71223e0f4f109b1bb0a837aceaf1e0ae56b11",
      "skos:note": "Consent must be voluntary, express, informed, specific, time limited, and easily withdrawable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-22",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 9  Object",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "The object of this Division is to ensure that a consent is:\n(a) voluntary; and\n(b) express; and\n(c) informed; and\n(d) specific as to purpose; and\n(e) time limited; and\n(f) easily withdrawn.\nSubdivision 4.3.2—Giving consents\nNote:\nUnder rule 4.3, if an accredited person asks a CDR consumer for their consent to collect and use their\nCDR data, it must do so in accordance with this Division, and in particular, rules 4.10, 4.11 and 4.12. A\nfailure to do so could contravene one or more civil penalty provisions: see section 56EF of the Act and\nrule 4.3."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-22-norm",
