    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-22-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must be voluntary, express, informed, specific, time limited, and easily withdrawable.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-22-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "CONTAINS",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Consent must contain a temporal interval that is time limited.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-23",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 10  Requirements relating to seeking consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-23"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "A request by an accredited person for a CDR consumer to give or amend a\nconsent:\n(a) must comply with any relevant data standards; and\n(b) having regard to any consumer experience guidelines made by the Data\nStandards Body—must be reasonably easy to understand, including by use\nof plain concise language and, where appropriate, visual aids; and\n(c) must not include or refer to the accredited person’s CDR policy or other\ndocuments in a way that reduces understandability; and\n(d) must not be combined with other requests except for a consent under these\nrules (other than a request for direct marketing or de-identification\nconsent).",
      "skos:definition": "A request by an accredited person for a CDR consumer to give or amend a\nconsent:\n(a) must comply with any relevant data standards; and\n(b) having regard to any consumer experience guidelines made by the Data\nStandards Body—must be reasonably easy to understand, including by use\nof plain concise language and, where appropriate, visual aids; and\n(c) must not include or refer to the accredited person’s CDR policy or other\ndocuments in a way that reduces understandability; and\n(d) must not be combined with other requests except for a consent under these\nrules (other than a request for direct marketing or de-identification\nconsent).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-23-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-23-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "87686f55a4e2325f27eff01284c4b21195342e9c6ffa96e23feedbfa9cbec2c8",
      "skos:note": "Request for consent must comply with data standards and be easy to understand.",
      "dc:description": "Reasonable ease of understanding"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-23",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 10  Requirements relating to seeking consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "A request by an accredited person for a CDR consumer to give or amend a\nconsent:\n(a) must comply with any relevant data standards; and\n(b) having regard to any consumer experience guidelines made by the Data\nStandards Body—must be reasonably easy to understand, including by use\nof plain concise language and, where appropriate, visual aids; and\n(c) must not include or refer to the accredited person’s CDR policy or other\ndocuments in a way that reduces understandability; and\n(d) must not be combined with other requests except for a consent under these\nrules (other than a request for direct marketing or de-identification\nconsent)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-23-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-23"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-23-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Request must comply with data standards",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 11  Asking CDR consumer to give consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "(1) When asking a CDR consumer to give a consent, an accredited person must:\n(a) in the case of a collection consent or a disclosure consent—either:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3\nSection 4.11\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the particular types of CDR data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the particular types of CDR\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(aa) in the case of a use consent—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the specific uses of collected data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the specific uses of collected\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(b) in relation to the period of the collection consent, use consent, or disclosure\nconsent (as appropriate)—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the period of consent; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the period of consent (as\npresented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will apply;\nwhere the period of consent is either:\n(iii) a single occasion; or\n(iv) a specified period of time; and\n(ba) in the case of a disclosure consent―either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the persons to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the persons (as presented to\nthe CDR consumer) to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; and\n(bb) where the accredited person proposes, or is offering, to deal with a person\nin their capacity as a CDR business consumer in relation to a consent of a\nkind mentioned in paragraph 1.10A(10)(a)―invite the CDR business\nconsumer to provide the business consumer statement; and\n(c) seek the CDR consumer’s express consent to the matters referred to in\nparagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (ba) for each relevant category of consents;\nand\n(d) if the accredited person intends to charge a fee for disclosure of CDR data,\nor pass on to the CDR consumer a fee charged by a data holder or\naccredited data recipient for disclosure of CDR data—clearly distinguish\nbetween the CDR data for which a fee will, and will not, be charged or\npassed on, and either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate whether they consent to the collection or disclosure, as\nappropriate, of the CDR data for which a fee will be charged or\npassed on; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the collection or disclosure, as\nappropriate, of the CDR data for which a fee will be charged or\npassed on (as presented to the CDR consumer); and\n(e) allow the CDR consumer to make an election in relation to deletion of\nredundant data in accordance with rule 4.16.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) When asking a CDR consumer to give a consent, an accredited person must:\n(a) in the case of a collection consent or a disclosure consent—either:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3\nSection 4.11\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the particular types of CDR data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the particular types of CDR\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(aa) in the case of a use consent—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the specific uses of collected data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the specific uses of collected\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(b) in relation to the period of the collection consent, use consent, or disclosure\nconsent (as appropriate)—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the period of consent; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the period of consent (as\npresented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will apply;\nwhere the period of consent is either:\n(iii) a single occasion; or\n(iv) a specified period of time; and\n(ba) in the case of a disclosure consent―either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the persons to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the persons (as presented to\nthe CDR consumer) to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; and\n(bb) where the accredited person proposes, or is offering, to deal with a person\nin their capacity as a CDR business consumer in relation to a consent of a\nkind mentioned in paragraph 1.10A(10)(a)―invite the CDR business\nconsumer to provide the business consum",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-24-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-24-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-24-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bec8acf5147a736ee5b51948b545ce26f1d54a8306f4671246ec3698039a32ee",
      "skos:note": "Accredited person must seek CDR consumer's consent for collection, use, disclosure, and deletion of data.",
      "dc:description": "Express consent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 11  Asking CDR consumer to give consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "(1) When asking a CDR consumer to give a consent, an accredited person must:\n(a) in the case of a collection consent or a disclosure consent—either:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3\nSection 4.11\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the particular types of CDR data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the particular types of CDR\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(aa) in the case of a use consent—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the specific uses of collected data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the specific uses of collected\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(b) in relation to the period of the collection consent, use consent, or disclosure\nconsent (as appropriate)—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the period of consent; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the period of consent (as\npresented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will apply;\nwhere the period of consent is either:\n(iii) a single occasion; or\n(iv) a specified period of time; and\n(ba) in the case of a disclosure consent―either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the persons to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the persons (as presented to\nthe CDR consumer) to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; and\n(bb) where the accredited person proposes, or is offering, to deal with a person\nin their capacity as a CDR business consumer in relation to a consent of a\nkind mentioned in paragraph 1.10A(10)(a)―invite the CDR business\nconsumer to provide the business consumer statement; and\n(c) seek the CDR consumer’s express consent to the matters referred to in\nparagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (ba) for each relevant category of consents;\nand\n(d) if the accredited person intends to charge a fee for disclosure of CDR data,\nor pass on to the CDR consumer a fee charged by a data holder or\naccredited data recipient for disclosure of CDR data—clearly distinguish\nbetween the CDR data for which a fee will, and will not, be charged or\npassed on, and either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate whether they consent to the collection or disclosure, as\nappropriate, of the CDR data for which a fee will be charged or\npassed on; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the collection or disclosure, as\nappropriate, of the CDR data for which a fee will be charged or\npassed on (as presented to the CDR consumer); and\n(e) allow the CDR consumer to make an election in relation to deletion of\nredundant data in accordance with rule 4.16."
    },
