    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 12  Restrictions on seeking consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.71",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subrule (1A), an accredited person must not specify a period of time\nfor the purposes of paragraph 4.11(1)(b) that is more than 12 months.\n(1A) In the case of a consent given by a CDR business consumer that includes a\nbusiness consumer statement, an accredited person must:\n(a) not specify a period of time that is more than 7 years; and\n(b) if specifying a period of time of more than 12 months, give the CDR\nbusiness consumer the option of choosing a period for the consent of 12\nmonths or less.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subrule (1A), an accredited person must not specify a period of time\nfor the purposes of paragraph 4.11(1)(b) that is more than 12 months.\n(1A) In the case of a consent given by a CDR business consumer that includes a\nbusiness consumer statement, an accredited person must:\n(a) not specify a period of time that is more than 7 years; and\n(b) if specifying a period of time of more than 12 months, give the CDR\nbusiness consumer the option of choosing a period for the consent of 12\nmonths or less.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-25-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-25-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dc815c958324e8719456cee4529360915988ecc93f94c5a13f0b25973f99fee3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 12  Restrictions on seeking consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 71,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subrule (1A), an accredited person must not specify a period of time\nfor the purposes of paragraph 4.11(1)(b) that is more than 12 months.\n(1A) In the case of a consent given by a CDR business consumer that includes a\nbusiness consumer statement, an accredited person must:\n(a) not specify a period of time that is more than 7 years; and\n(b) if specifying a period of time of more than 12 months, give the CDR\nbusiness consumer the option of choosing a period for the consent of 12\nmonths or less."
    },
