    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-25-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(1A) 12  Restrictions on seeking consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-25-ss-1a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.71",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) In the case of a consent given by a CDR business consumer that includes a\nbusiness consumer statement, an accredited person must:\n(a) not specify a period of time that is more than 7 years; and\n(b) if specifying a period of time of more than 12 months, give the CDR\nbusiness consumer the option of choosing a period for the consent of 12\nmonths or less.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) In the case of a consent given by a CDR business consumer that includes a\nbusiness consumer statement, an accredited person must:\n(a) not specify a period of time that is more than 7 years; and\n(b) if specifying a period of time of more than 12 months, give the CDR\nbusiness consumer the option of choosing a period for the consent of 12\nmonths or less.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-25"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-25-ss-1a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-25-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-25-ss-1a-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a6424f4d922fdf4ad5d21a7c42302476fc9bf63ada90cc8775c62bb33aea8551",
      "skos:note": "Accredited person must not specify a period of time more than 7 years and give the CDR business consumer an option to choose a period of 12 months or less."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-25-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(1A) 12  Restrictions on seeking consent",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 71,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) In the case of a consent given by a CDR business consumer that includes a\nbusiness consumer statement, an accredited person must:\n(a) not specify a period of time that is more than 7 years; and\n(b) if specifying a period of time of more than 12 months, give the CDR\nbusiness consumer the option of choosing a period for the consent of 12\nmonths or less."
    },
