    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-27",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 12B  Inviting CDR consumer to amend consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-27"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An accredited person may invite a CDR consumer to amend a consent given in\naccordance with this Division only in accordance with this rule.\n(2) The accredited person may give the invitation:\n(a) if its consumer dashboard allows a consent amendment in accordance with\nsubrule 1.14(2A)―via its consumer dashboard; or\n(b) in writing directly to the CDR consumer.\n(3) The accredited person may invite a CDR consumer to amend a current consent if:\n(a) the amendment would better enable the accredited person to provide the\ngoods or services referred to in paragraph 4.3(1)(a); or\n(b) the amendment would:\n(i) be consequential to an agreement between the accredited person and\nthe CDR consumer to modify those goods or services; and\n(ii) enable the accredited person to provide the modified goods or\nservices.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3\nSection 4.12C\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(4) The accredited person must not, for an invitation to amend the period referred to\nin paragraph 4.11(1)(b):\n(a) give the invitation any earlier than a reasonable period before the current\nconsent is expected to expire; or\n(b) give more than a reasonable number of such invitations within this period.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An accredited person may invite a CDR consumer to amend a consent given in\naccordance with this Division only in accordance with this rule.\n(2) The accredited person may give the invitation:\n(a) if its consumer dashboard allows a consent amendment in accordance with\nsubrule 1.14(2A)―via its consumer dashboard; or\n(b) in writing directly to the CDR consumer.\n(3) The accredited person may invite a CDR consumer to amend a current consent if:\n(a) the amendment would better enable the accredited person to provide the\ngoods or services referred to in paragraph 4.3(1)(a); or\n(b) the amendment would:\n(i) be consequential to an agreement between the accredited person and\nthe CDR consumer to modify those goods or services; and\n(ii) enable the accredited person to provide the modified goods or\nservices.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3\nSection 4.12C\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(4) The accredited person must not, for an invitation to amend the period referred to\nin paragraph 4.11(1)(b):\n(a) give the invitation any earlier than a reasonable period before the current\nconsent is expected to expire; or\n(b) give more than a reasonable number of such invitations within this period.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-27-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-27-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-27-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-27-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0187aac15d365a6e1414d6a67bdf2aa56be857b486ef4389bacd50f67a55e48e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-27",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 12B  Inviting CDR consumer to amend consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An accredited person may invite a CDR consumer to amend a consent given in\naccordance with this Division only in accordance with this rule.\n(2) The accredited person may give the invitation:\n(a) if its consumer dashboard allows a consent amendment in accordance with\nsubrule 1.14(2A)―via its consumer dashboard; or\n(b) in writing directly to the CDR consumer.\n(3) The accredited person may invite a CDR consumer to amend a current consent if:\n(a) the amendment would better enable the accredited person to provide the\ngoods or services referred to in paragraph 4.3(1)(a); or\n(b) the amendment would:\n(i) be consequential to an agreement between the accredited person and\nthe CDR consumer to modify those goods or services; and\n(ii) enable the accredited person to provide the modified goods or\nservices.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3\nSection 4.12C\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(4) The accredited person must not, for an invitation to amend the period referred to\nin paragraph 4.11(1)(b):\n(a) give the invitation any earlier than a reasonable period before the current\nconsent is expected to expire; or\n(b) give more than a reasonable number of such invitations within this period."
    },
