      "cml:premiseText": "(6) If an accredited person’s accreditation is revoked or surrendered in accordance with rule 5.17, all of the accredited person’s consents expire when the revocation or surrender takes effect.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Accreditation revocation/surrender implies consent expiration."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-32",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 15  Additional information relating to de-identification of CDR data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-32"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "For paragraph 4.11(3)(e), the additional information the accredited person must\ngive the CDR consumer when seeking a de-identification consent is the\nfollowing:\n(a) what the CDR data de-identification process is;\n(b) if it would disclose (by sale or otherwise) the de-identified data to one or\nmore other persons;\n(i) that fact; and\n(ii) the classes of persons to which it would disclose that data;\n(iii) why it would so disclose that data;\n(c) if the accredited person would use the de-identified data for general\nresearch―that fact, together with a link to a description in the accredited\nperson’s CDR policy of:\n(i) the research to be conducted; and\n(ii) any additional benefit to be provided to the CDR consumer for\nconsenting to the use;\n(e) that the CDR consumer would not be able to elect, in accordance with rule",
      "skos:definition": "For paragraph 4.11(3)(e), the additional information the accredited person must\ngive the CDR consumer when seeking a de-identification consent is the\nfollowing:\n(a) what the CDR data de-identification process is;\n(b) if it would disclose (by sale or otherwise) the de-identified data to one or\nmore other persons;\n(i) that fact; and\n(ii) the classes of persons to which it would disclose that data;\n(iii) why it would so disclose that data;\n(c) if the accredited person would use the de-identified data for general\nresearch―that fact, together with a link to a description in the accredited\nperson’s CDR policy of:\n(i) the research to be conducted; and\n(ii) any additional benefit to be provided to the CDR consumer for\nconsenting to the use;\n(e) that the CDR consumer would not be able to elect, in accordance with rule",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-32-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-32-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2e7bfe25978daca7a8b31b928c8f3a8ce331e7748583710cf657d81d7efbfbed",
      "skos:note": "Accredited person must provide de-identification consent information to CDR consumer",
      "dc:description": "Additional information about de-identification process, disclosure, and research use"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-32",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 15  Additional information relating to de-identification of CDR data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "For paragraph 4.11(3)(e), the additional information the accredited person must\ngive the CDR consumer when seeking a de-identification consent is the\nfollowing:\n(a) what the CDR data de-identification process is;\n(b) if it would disclose (by sale or otherwise) the de-identified data to one or\nmore other persons;\n(i) that fact; and\n(ii) the classes of persons to which it would disclose that data;\n(iii) why it would so disclose that data;\n(c) if the accredited person would use the de-identified data for general\nresearch―that fact, together with a link to a description in the accredited\nperson’s CDR policy of:\n(i) the research to be conducted; and\n(ii) any additional benefit to be provided to the CDR consumer for\nconsenting to the use;\n(e) that the CDR consumer would not be able to elect, in accordance with rule"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-32-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
