      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "16, to have the de-identified data deleted once it becomes redundant data.\nSubdivision 4.3.4—Election to delete redundant data",
      "skos:definition": "16, to have the de-identified data deleted once it becomes redundant data.\nSubdivision 4.3.4—Election to delete redundant data",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-33-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "79b480e20cfa4470669f406b7ff44687f114da880916bf9ec2d05c6b2f7a0749",
      "skos:note": "Delete redundant data after a certain period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-33",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Section 4",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "16, to have the de-identified data deleted once it becomes redundant data.\nSubdivision 4.3.4—Election to delete redundant data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-33-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-33"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-34",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 16  Election to delete redundant data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-34"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR consumer who has given a consent relating to particular CDR data may:\n(a) when giving the consent; or\n(b) at any other time before the consent expires;\nelect that the collected data, and any CDR data directly or indirectly derived\nfrom it, be deleted when it becomes redundant data.\nNote 1:\nSee rules 7.12 and 7.13 for the effect of an election.\nNote 2:\nCDR data might become redundant data even before a consent expires.\n(2) The CDR consumer may make the election:\n(a) by communicating it to the accredited person in writing; or\n(b) by using the accredited person’s consumer dashboard.\n(3) This rule does not apply if the accredited person:\n(a) has a general policy of deleting redundant data; and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A CDR consumer who has given a consent relating to particular CDR data may:\n(a) when giving the consent; or\n(b) at any other time before the consent expires;\nelect that the collected data, and any CDR data directly or indirectly derived\nfrom it, be deleted when it becomes redundant data.\nNote 1:\nSee rules 7.12 and 7.13 for the effect of an election.\nNote 2:\nCDR data might become redundant data even before a consent expires.\n(2) The CDR consumer may make the election:\n(a) by communicating it to the accredited person in writing; or\n(b) by using the accredited person’s consumer dashboard.\n(3) This rule does not apply if the accredited person:\n(a) has a general policy of deleting redundant data; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-34-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-34-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-34-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8bc53b2180b34847cb3d7ee020dbf8dc9f7c6f88c616de0e23cb5cf1430dc859"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-34",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 16  Election to delete redundant data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR consumer who has given a consent relating to particular CDR data may:\n(a) when giving the consent; or\n(b) at any other time before the consent expires;\nelect that the collected data, and any CDR data directly or indirectly derived\nfrom it, be deleted when it becomes redundant data.\nNote 1:\nSee rules 7.12 and 7.13 for the effect of an election.\nNote 2:\nCDR data might become redundant data even before a consent expires.\n(2) The CDR consumer may make the election:\n(a) by communicating it to the accredited person in writing; or\n(b) by using the accredited person’s consumer dashboard.\n(3) This rule does not apply if the accredited person:\n(a) has a general policy of deleting redundant data; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-34-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(1) 16  Election to delete redundant data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-34-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
