      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR consumer who has given a consent relating to particular CDR data may:\n(a) when giving the consent; or\n(b) at any other time before the consent expires;\nelect that the collected data, and any CDR data directly or indirectly derived\nfrom it, be deleted when it becomes redundant data.\nNote 1:\nSee rules 7.12 and 7.13 for the effect of an election.\nNote 2:\nCDR data might become redundant data even before a consent expires.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A CDR consumer who has given a consent relating to particular CDR data may:\n(a) when giving the consent; or\n(b) at any other time before the consent expires;\nelect that the collected data, and any CDR data directly or indirectly derived\nfrom it, be deleted when it becomes redundant data.\nNote 1:\nSee rules 7.12 and 7.13 for the effect of an election.\nNote 2:\nCDR data might become redundant data even before a consent expires.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-34"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-34-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-34-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "35ef66660f2cd48533e62d9bbea1b5f653141e2dcc55ab0db3c508925009a26d",
      "skos:note": "Allow CDR consumer to delete data when it becomes redundant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-34-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(1) 16  Election to delete redundant data",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR consumer who has given a consent relating to particular CDR data may:\n(a) when giving the consent; or\n(b) at any other time before the consent expires;\nelect that the collected data, and any CDR data directly or indirectly derived\nfrom it, be deleted when it becomes redundant data.\nNote 1:\nSee rules 7.12 and 7.13 for the effect of an election.\nNote 2:\nCDR data might become redundant data even before a consent expires."
    },
