      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies if:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3\nSection 4.18A\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request to a CDR\nparticipant, based on a collection consent given under this Division relating\nto particular CDR data and that CDR participant; and\n(b) the request has not been completely resolved; and\n(c) the consent expires for any reason.",
