        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-38",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 18A  Notification of CDR consumer if collection consent expires",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-38"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.77",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if, in relation to particular goods or services an accredited\nperson is providing as referred to in subrule 4.3(1):\n(a) the collection consent expires; but\n(b) the use consent, or any disclosure consent, is current.\n(2) The accredited person must notify the CDR consumer as soon as practicable after\nthe collection consent expires that, at any time, they:\n(a) may withdraw the use consent or disclosure consent; and\n(b) may make the election to delete redundant data in respect of that CDR data\nunder rule 4.16.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The notification must be given in writing otherwise than through the CDR\nconsumer’s consumer dashboard.\n(4) The notification may also be included in the CDR consumer’s consumer\ndashboard.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies if, in relation to particular goods or services an accredited\nperson is providing as referred to in subrule 4.3(1):\n(a) the collection consent expires; but\n(b) the use consent, or any disclosure consent, is current.\n(2) The accredited person must notify the CDR consumer as soon as practicable after\nthe collection consent expires that, at any time, they:\n(a) may withdraw the use consent or disclosure consent; and\n(b) may make the election to delete redundant data in respect of that CDR data\nunder rule 4.16.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The notification must be given in writing otherwise than through the CDR\nconsumer’s consumer dashboard.\n(4) The notification may also be included in the CDR consumer’s consumer\ndashboard.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-38-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-38-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-38-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-38-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a1a377d5c2b45a50b7792e66282979c9f428a2f04951b0581fc0e1c3bb205d32"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-38",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 18A  Notification of CDR consumer if collection consent expires",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 77,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if, in relation to particular goods or services an accredited\nperson is providing as referred to in subrule 4.3(1):\n(a) the collection consent expires; but\n(b) the use consent, or any disclosure consent, is current.\n(2) The accredited person must notify the CDR consumer as soon as practicable after\nthe collection consent expires that, at any time, they:\n(a) may withdraw the use consent or disclosure consent; and\n(b) may make the election to delete redundant data in respect of that CDR data\nunder rule 4.16.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The notification must be given in writing otherwise than through the CDR\nconsumer’s consumer dashboard.\n(4) The notification may also be included in the CDR consumer’s consumer\ndashboard."
    },
