    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-39",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 18B  Notification if collection consent or AP disclosure consent expires",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-39"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.77",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request to an accredited\ndata recipient on behalf of a CDR representative, based on a collection\nconsent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and that\naccredited data recipient; and\n(b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent relating to that\nCDR data; and\n(c) the request has not been completely resolved.\n(2) If the collection consent expires in accordance with these rules, the accredited\nperson must notify the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable of the\nexpiry.\nNote 1:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nNote 2:\nThe AP disclosure consent that the accredited data recipient has expires when the\nnotification is received—see subrule 4.14(4).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request to an accredited\ndata recipient on behalf of a CDR representative, based on a collection\nconsent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and that\naccredited data recipient; and\n(b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent relating to that\nCDR data; and\n(c) the request has not been completely resolved.\n(2) If the collection consent expires in accordance with these rules, the accredited\nperson must notify the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable of the\nexpiry.\nNote 1:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nNote 2:\nThe AP disclosure consent that the accredited data recipient has expires when the\nnotification is received—see subrule 4.14(4).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-39-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-39-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b6a7b1e89d716dca089398a6ff6b2737df274b8dc4402e1c7d7d8a1db370bda6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-39",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 18B  Notification if collection consent or AP disclosure consent expires",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 77,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request to an accredited\ndata recipient on behalf of a CDR representative, based on a collection\nconsent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and that\naccredited data recipient; and\n(b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent relating to that\nCDR data; and\n(c) the request has not been completely resolved.\n(2) If the collection consent expires in accordance with these rules, the accredited\nperson must notify the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable of the\nexpiry.\nNote 1:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nNote 2:\nThe AP disclosure consent that the accredited data recipient has expires when the\nnotification is received—see subrule 4.14(4)."
    },
    {
