          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-39-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "76f1b525b0e0d0cb35fa7dfeca79b4d339d42e3c15c66de1ce25a33bff27c8bc",
      "skos:note": "Notify accredited data recipient of expired collection consent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-39-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(2) 18B  Notification if collection consent or AP disclosure consent expires",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 77,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the collection consent expires in accordance with these rules, the accredited\nperson must notify the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable of the\nexpiry.\nNote 1:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nNote 2:\nThe AP disclosure consent that the accredited data recipient has expires when the\nnotification is received—see subrule 4.14(4)."
    },
