    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-41",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 19  Updating consumer dashboard",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-41"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An accredited person must update a CDR consumer’s consumer dashboard as\nsoon as practicable after the information required to be contained on the\ndashboard changes.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) Where a CDR representative provides the consumer dashboard on behalf of a\nCDR representative principal (see subrule 1.14(5)), the CDR representative\nprincipal may arrange for the CDR representative to update the consumer\ndashboard on the CDR representative principal’s behalf.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An accredited person must update a CDR consumer’s consumer dashboard as\nsoon as practicable after the information required to be contained on the\ndashboard changes.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) Where a CDR representative provides the consumer dashboard on behalf of a\nCDR representative principal (see subrule 1.14(5)), the CDR representative\nprincipal may arrange for the CDR representative to update the consumer\ndashboard on the CDR representative principal’s behalf.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-41-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-41-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b41213d871e253d4ccd425739dce069546f937de8294f7d19f2dcf6c00c27d0f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-41",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 19  Updating consumer dashboard",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An accredited person must update a CDR consumer’s consumer dashboard as\nsoon as practicable after the information required to be contained on the\ndashboard changes.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) Where a CDR representative provides the consumer dashboard on behalf of a\nCDR representative principal (see subrule 1.14(5)), the CDR representative\nprincipal may arrange for the CDR representative to update the consumer\ndashboard on the CDR representative principal’s behalf."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-41-ss-1",
