      "cml:logicSummary": "May arrange for CDR representative to update consumer dashboard.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-42",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20  Ongoing notification requirement—current consents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-42"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure\nconsent given under this Division if:\n(a) the consent is current; and\n(b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following:\n(i) the CDR consumer gave the consent;\n(ia) the CDR consumer last amended the consent;\n(ii) the CDR consumer last used their consumer dashboard;\n(iii) the accredited person last notified the CDR consumer that the consent\nis still current.\n(2) The accredited person must notify the CDR consumer, in relation to each consent\ngiven by the CDR consumer that is still current, that the consent is still current.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3\nSection 4.20A\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The notification must be given in accordance with the data standards.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure\nconsent given under this Division if:\n(a) the consent is current; and\n(b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following:\n(i) the CDR consumer gave the consent;\n(ia) the CDR consumer last amended the consent;\n(ii) the CDR consumer last used their consumer dashboard;\n(iii) the accredited person last notified the CDR consumer that the consent\nis still current.\n(2) The accredited person must notify the CDR consumer, in relation to each consent\ngiven by the CDR consumer that is still current, that the consent is still current.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3\nSection 4.20A\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The notification must be given in accordance with the data standards.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-42-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-42-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-42-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f2238d420ceac42bb912f0e329421df61f57ff687c28291a14364b7c749ad3b2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-42",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20  Ongoing notification requirement—current consents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure\nconsent given under this Division if:\n(a) the consent is current; and\n(b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following:\n(i) the CDR consumer gave the consent;\n(ia) the CDR consumer last amended the consent;\n(ii) the CDR consumer last used their consumer dashboard;\n(iii) the accredited person last notified the CDR consumer that the consent\nis still current.\n(2) The accredited person must notify the CDR consumer, in relation to each consent\ngiven by the CDR consumer that is still current, that the consent is still current.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3\nSection 4.20A\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The notification must be given in accordance with the data standards.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
