    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-45",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20C  Object",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-45"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "The object of this Division is to ensure that a consent is:\n(a) voluntary; and\n(b) express; and\n(c) informed; and\n(d) specific as to purpose; and\n(e) time limited; and\n(f) easily withdrawn.\nSubdivision 4.3A.2—Giving consents\nNote:\nUnder rule 4.3A, if a CDR representative asks a CDR consumer for their consent to collect and use their\nCDR data, it must do so in accordance with this Division, and in particular, rules 4.20D, 4.20E and",
      "skos:definition": "The object of this Division is to ensure that a consent is:\n(a) voluntary; and\n(b) express; and\n(c) informed; and\n(d) specific as to purpose; and\n(e) time limited; and\n(f) easily withdrawn.\nSubdivision 4.3A.2—Giving consents\nNote:\nUnder rule 4.3A, if a CDR representative asks a CDR consumer for their consent to collect and use their\nCDR data, it must do so in accordance with this Division, and in particular, rules 4.20D, 4.20E and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-45-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-45-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "12fff1f34cc35a0ef53f72a384a42e8a39821554babbc445f628ac2657b5e3f5",
      "skos:note": "Consent requirements"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-45",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20C  Object",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "The object of this Division is to ensure that a consent is:\n(a) voluntary; and\n(b) express; and\n(c) informed; and\n(d) specific as to purpose; and\n(e) time limited; and\n(f) easily withdrawn.\nSubdivision 4.3A.2—Giving consents\nNote:\nUnder rule 4.3A, if a CDR representative asks a CDR consumer for their consent to collect and use their\nCDR data, it must do so in accordance with this Division, and in particular, rules 4.20D, 4.20E and"
    },
    {
