    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-47",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20D  Requirements relating to seeking consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-47"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "A request by a CDR representative for a CDR consumer to give or amend a\nconsent:\n(a) must comply with any relevant data standards; and\n(b) having regard to any consumer experience guidelines developed by the\nData Standards Body—must be reasonably easy to understand, including\nby use of plain concise language and, where appropriate, visual aids; and\n(c) must not include or refer to the CDR representative principal’s CDR policy\nor other documents in a way that reduces understandability; and\n(d) must not be combined with other requests except for a consent under these\nrules (other than a request for direct marketing or de-identification\nconsent).",
      "skos:definition": "A request by a CDR representative for a CDR consumer to give or amend a\nconsent:\n(a) must comply with any relevant data standards; and\n(b) having regard to any consumer experience guidelines developed by the\nData Standards Body—must be reasonably easy to understand, including\nby use of plain concise language and, where appropriate, visual aids; and\n(c) must not include or refer to the CDR representative principal’s CDR policy\nor other documents in a way that reduces understandability; and\n(d) must not be combined with other requests except for a consent under these\nrules (other than a request for direct marketing or de-identification\nconsent).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-47-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-47-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "354df254df855926f530d3080e71301f93c3ced3cdbf2e5d494519441e0eaddb",
      "skos:note": "Request for consent must comply with data standards and be easy to understand.",
      "dc:description": "Reasonable ease of understanding"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-47",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20D  Requirements relating to seeking consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "A request by a CDR representative for a CDR consumer to give or amend a\nconsent:\n(a) must comply with any relevant data standards; and\n(b) having regard to any consumer experience guidelines developed by the\nData Standards Body—must be reasonably easy to understand, including\nby use of plain concise language and, where appropriate, visual aids; and\n(c) must not include or refer to the CDR representative principal’s CDR policy\nor other documents in a way that reduces understandability; and\n(d) must not be combined with other requests except for a consent under these\nrules (other than a request for direct marketing or de-identification\nconsent)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-47-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-47"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-47-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to comply with data standards",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-48",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20E  Asking CDR consumer to give consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-48"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(1) When asking a CDR consumer to give a consent, a CDR representative must:\n(a) in the case of a collection consent or a disclosure consent—either:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20E\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the particular types of CDR data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the particular types of CDR\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(aa) in the case of a use consent—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the specific uses of collected data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the specific uses of collected\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(b) in relation to the period of the collection consent, use consent, or disclosure\nconsent (as appropriate)—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the period of consent; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the period of consent (as\npresented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will apply;\nwhere the period of consent is either:\n(iii) a single occasion; or\n(iv) a specified period of time; and\n(c) in the case of a disclosure consent―either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the person to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the persons (as presented to\nthe CDR consumer) to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; and\n(d) seek the CDR consumer’s express consent to the matters referred to in\nparagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (c) for each relevant category of consents; and\n(e) if the CDR representative intends to charge a fee for disclosure of CDR\ndata, or pass on to the CDR consumer a fee charged by a data holder or\naccredited person for disclosure of CDR data—clearly distinguish between\nthe CDR data for which a fee will, and will not, be charged or passed on,\nand either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate whether they consent to the collection or disclosure, as\nappropriate, of the CDR data for which a fee will be charged or\npassed on; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the collection or disclosure, as\nappropriate, of the CDR data for which a fee will be charged or\npassed on (as presented to the CDR consumer); and\n(f) allow the CDR consumer to make an election in relation to deletion of\nredundant data in accordance with rule 4.20M.\nNote 1:\nA CDR representative cannot infer consent, or seek to rely on an implied consent.\nNote 2:\nFor paragraph (b), the specified period may not be more than 12 months: see subrule",
      "skos:definition": "(1) When asking a CDR consumer to give a consent, a CDR representative must:\n(a) in the case of a collection consent or a disclosure consent—either:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20E\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the particular types of CDR data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the particular types of CDR\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(aa) in the case of a use consent—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the specific uses of collected data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the specific uses of collected\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(b) in relation to the period of the collection consent, use consent, or disclosure\nconsent (as appropriate)—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the period of consent; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the period of consent (as\npresented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will apply;\nwhere the period of consent is either:\n(iii) a single occasion; or\n(iv) a specified period of time; and\n(c) in the case of a disclosure consent―either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the person to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the persons (as presented to\nthe CDR consumer) to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; and\n(d) seek the CDR consumer’s express consent to the matters referred to in\nparagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (c) for each relevant category of consents; and\n(e) if the CDR representative intends to charge a fee for disclosure of CDR\ndata, or pass on to the CDR con",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-48-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-48-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-48-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c8ead7751730abfd455a926198c0591039ad08e52e7d8cc9c2095e6a599d9255",
      "skos:note": "Must provide consent for data collection, use, and disclosure",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-48",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20E  Asking CDR consumer to give consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "(1) When asking a CDR consumer to give a consent, a CDR representative must:\n(a) in the case of a collection consent or a disclosure consent—either:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20E\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the particular types of CDR data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the particular types of CDR\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(aa) in the case of a use consent—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the specific uses of collected data to which the consent will\napply; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the specific uses of collected\ndata (as presented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will\napply; and\n(b) in relation to the period of the collection consent, use consent, or disclosure\nconsent (as appropriate)—either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the period of consent; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the period of consent (as\npresented to the CDR consumer) to which the consent will apply;\nwhere the period of consent is either:\n(iii) a single occasion; or\n(iv) a specified period of time; and\n(c) in the case of a disclosure consent―either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate the person to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the persons (as presented to\nthe CDR consumer) to whom the CDR data may be disclosed; and\n(d) seek the CDR consumer’s express consent to the matters referred to in\nparagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (c) for each relevant category of consents; and\n(e) if the CDR representative intends to charge a fee for disclosure of CDR\ndata, or pass on to the CDR consumer a fee charged by a data holder or\naccredited person for disclosure of CDR data—clearly distinguish between\nthe CDR data for which a fee will, and will not, be charged or passed on,\nand either:\n(i) allow the CDR consumer to actively select or otherwise clearly\nindicate whether they consent to the collection or disclosure, as\nappropriate, of the CDR data for which a fee will be charged or\npassed on; or\n(ii) seek the CDR consumer’s agreement to the collection or disclosure, as\nappropriate, of the CDR data for which a fee will be charged or\npassed on (as presented to the CDR consumer); and\n(f) allow the CDR consumer to make an election in relation to deletion of\nredundant data in accordance with rule 4.20M.\nNote 1:\nA CDR representative cannot infer consent, or seek to rely on an implied consent.\nNote 2:\nFor paragraph (b), the specified period may not be more than 12 months: see subrule"
    },
