        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-50",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20F  Restrictions on seeking consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-50"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.83",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR representative must not specify a period of time for the purposes of\nparagraph 4.11(1)(b) that is more than 12 months.\n(2) A CDR representative must not ask for a collection consent, a use consent or a\ndisclosure consent unless the consent would comply with the data minimisation\nprinciple in respect of that collection or those uses or disclosures.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.8 for the definition of “data minimisation principle”.\n\n(3) A CDR representative must not ask for a consent:\n(a) that is not in a category of consents; or\n(b) subject to subrule (4), for using the CDR data, including by aggregating the\ndata, for the purpose of:\n(i) identifying; or\n(ii) compiling insights in relation to; or\n(iii) building a profile in relation to;\nany identifiable person who is not the CDR consumer who made the\nconsumer data request.\n(4) Paragraph (3)(b) does not apply in relation to a person whose identity is readily\napparent from the CDR data, if the CDR representative is seeking consent to:\n(a) derive, from that CDR data, CDR data about that person’s interactions with\nthe CDR consumer; and\n(b) use that derived CDR data in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A CDR representative must not specify a period of time for the purposes of\nparagraph 4.11(1)(b) that is more than 12 months.\n(2) A CDR representative must not ask for a collection consent, a use consent or a\ndisclosure consent unless the consent would comply with the data minimisation\nprinciple in respect of that collection or those uses or disclosures.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.8 for the definition of “data minimisation principle”.\n\n(3) A CDR representative must not ask for a consent:\n(a) that is not in a category of consents; or\n(b) subject to subrule (4), for using the CDR data, including by aggregating the\ndata, for the purpose of:\n(i) identifying; or\n(ii) compiling insights in relation to; or\n(iii) building a profile in relation to;\nany identifiable person who is not the CDR consumer who made the\nconsumer data request.\n(4) Paragraph (3)(b) does not apply in relation to a person whose identity is readily\napparent from the CDR data, if the CDR representative is seeking consent to:\n(a) derive, from that CDR data, CDR data about that person’s interactions with\nthe CDR consumer; and\n(b) use that derived CDR data in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-50-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-50-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-50-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-50-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4a720697cec19dc1814d6097d31e2bd6b9ee6459049e868dc41548aa916e8aa1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-50",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20F  Restrictions on seeking consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 83,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR representative must not specify a period of time for the purposes of\nparagraph 4.11(1)(b) that is more than 12 months.\n(2) A CDR representative must not ask for a collection consent, a use consent or a\ndisclosure consent unless the consent would comply with the data minimisation\nprinciple in respect of that collection or those uses or disclosures.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.8 for the definition of “data minimisation principle”.\n\n(3) A CDR representative must not ask for a consent:\n(a) that is not in a category of consents; or\n(b) subject to subrule (4), for using the CDR data, including by aggregating the\ndata, for the purpose of:\n(i) identifying; or\n(ii) compiling insights in relation to; or\n(iii) building a profile in relation to;\nany identifiable person who is not the CDR consumer who made the\nconsumer data request.\n(4) Paragraph (3)(b) does not apply in relation to a person whose identity is readily\napparent from the CDR data, if the CDR representative is seeking consent to:\n(a) derive, from that CDR data, CDR data about that person’s interactions with\nthe CDR consumer; and\n(b) use that derived CDR data in order to provide the requested goods or\nservices."
    },
