        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to derive and use CDR data",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) Paragraph (3)(b) does not apply..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-51",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20G  Amendment of consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-51"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "An amendment of a consent takes effect when the CDR consumer amends the\nconsent.\nNote:\nIt is not possible for the CDR consumer to specify a different day or time.",
      "skos:definition": "An amendment of a consent takes effect when the CDR consumer amends the\nconsent.\nNote:\nIt is not possible for the CDR consumer to specify a different day or time.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-51-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "84d5c864bc1ac678c6e9dd288645ee2a7f37c472aca57767d283d3ce4323d6ba",
      "skos:note": "Amendment of consent takes effect when the CDR consumer amends the consent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-51",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20G  Amendment of consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "An amendment of a consent takes effect when the CDR consumer amends the\nconsent.\nNote:\nIt is not possible for the CDR consumer to specify a different day or time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-51-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-51"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-52",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20H  Inviting CDR consumer to amend consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-52"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR representative may invite a CDR consumer to amend a consent given in\naccordance with this Division only in accordance with this rule.\n(2) The CDR representative may give the invitation:\n(a) if the CDR representative principal’s consumer dashboard allows an\namendment to a consent in accordance with subrule 1.14(2A)―via the\nconsumer dashboard; or\n(b) in writing directly to the CDR consumer.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\n(3) The CDR representative may invite a CDR consumer to amend a current consent\nif:\n(a) the amendment would better enable the CDR representative to provide the\ngoods or services referred to in paragraph 4.3A(1)(a); or\n(b) the amendment would:\n(i) be consequential to an agreement between the CDR representative and\nthe CDR consumer to modify those goods or services; and\n(ii) enable the CDR representative to provide the modified goods or\nservices.\n(4) The CDR representative must not, for an invitation to amend the period referred\nto in paragraph 4.20E(1)(b):\n(a) give the invitation any earlier than a reasonable period before the current\nconsent is expected to expire; or\n(b) give more than a reasonable number of such invitations within this period.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A CDR representative may invite a CDR consumer to amend a consent given in\naccordance with this Division only in accordance with this rule.\n(2) The CDR representative may give the invitation:\n(a) if the CDR representative principal’s consumer dashboard allows an\namendment to a consent in accordance with subrule 1.14(2A)―via the\nconsumer dashboard; or\n(b) in writing directly to the CDR consumer.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\n(3) The CDR representative may invite a CDR consumer to amend a current consent\nif:\n(a) the amendment would better enable the CDR representative to provide the\ngoods or services referred to in paragraph 4.3A(1)(a); or\n(b) the amendment would:\n(i) be consequential to an agreement between the CDR representative and\nthe CDR consumer to modify those goods or services; and\n(ii) enable the CDR representative to provide the modified goods or\nservices.\n(4) The CDR representative must not, for an invitation to amend the period referred\nto in paragraph 4.20E(1)(b):\n(a) give the invitation any earlier than a reasonable period before the current\nconsent is expected to expire; or\n(b) give more than a reasonable number of such invitations within this period.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-52-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-52-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-52-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-52-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "19b96bb50354ad52bf227ec98011912f0b570ef4644cb0adcb938774938583b2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-52",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20H  Inviting CDR consumer to amend consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR representative may invite a CDR consumer to amend a consent given in\naccordance with this Division only in accordance with this rule.\n(2) The CDR representative may give the invitation:\n(a) if the CDR representative principal’s consumer dashboard allows an\namendment to a consent in accordance with subrule 1.14(2A)―via the\nconsumer dashboard; or\n(b) in writing directly to the CDR consumer.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\n(3) The CDR representative may invite a CDR consumer to amend a current consent\nif:\n(a) the amendment would better enable the CDR representative to provide the\ngoods or services referred to in paragraph 4.3A(1)(a); or\n(b) the amendment would:\n(i) be consequential to an agreement between the CDR representative and\nthe CDR consumer to modify those goods or services; and\n(ii) enable the CDR representative to provide the modified goods or\nservices.\n(4) The CDR representative must not, for an invitation to amend the period referred\nto in paragraph 4.20E(1)(b):\n(a) give the invitation any earlier than a reasonable period before the current\nconsent is expected to expire; or\n(b) give more than a reasonable number of such invitations within this period."
    },
