    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-53",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20I  Process for amending consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-53"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this rule, if a CDR representative allows CDR consumers to amend\nconsents, it must allow them to do so in the same manner that it asks for CDR\nconsumers to give consents.\n(3) In the case of an amendment to a consent, in addition to the information referred\nto in subrule 4.20E(3), the CDR representative must give the CDR consumer:\n(a) a statement that indicates the consequences of amending a consent; and\n(b) a statement that the CDR representative will be able to continue to use any\nCDR data that has already been disclosed to it to the extent allowed by the\namended consent.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20J\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nSubdivision 4.3A.4—Withdrawing consents",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to this rule, if a CDR representative allows CDR consumers to amend\nconsents, it must allow them to do so in the same manner that it asks for CDR\nconsumers to give consents.\n(3) In the case of an amendment to a consent, in addition to the information referred\nto in subrule 4.20E(3), the CDR representative must give the CDR consumer:\n(a) a statement that indicates the consequences of amending a consent; and\n(b) a statement that the CDR representative will be able to continue to use any\nCDR data that has already been disclosed to it to the extent allowed by the\namended consent.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20J\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nSubdivision 4.3A.4—Withdrawing consents",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-53-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-53-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1a11404729b905dc77042bbc00a4d605aa549af5dbc564057aaa1147d92e03af"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20I  Process for amending consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this rule, if a CDR representative allows CDR consumers to amend\nconsents, it must allow them to do so in the same manner that it asks for CDR\nconsumers to give consents.\n(3) In the case of an amendment to a consent, in addition to the information referred\nto in subrule 4.20E(3), the CDR representative must give the CDR consumer:\n(a) a statement that indicates the consequences of amending a consent; and\n(b) a statement that the CDR representative will be able to continue to use any\nCDR data that has already been disclosed to it to the extent allowed by the\namended consent.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20J\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nSubdivision 4.3A.4—Withdrawing consents"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-53-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(1) 20I  Process for amending consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-53-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
