      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this rule, if a CDR representative allows CDR consumers to amend\nconsents, it must allow them to do so in the same manner that it asks for CDR\nconsumers to give consents.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to this rule, if a CDR representative allows CDR consumers to amend\nconsents, it must allow them to do so in the same manner that it asks for CDR\nconsumers to give consents.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-53"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-53-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-53-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "361cbe71da544fb8ef3b35b94f531540358e95aa3c37f9ea10dc828bb108ce72",
      "skos:note": "Must allow consumers to amend consents in the same manner as it asks for them."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-53-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(1) 20I  Process for amending consent",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this rule, if a CDR representative allows CDR consumers to amend\nconsents, it must allow them to do so in the same manner that it asks for CDR\nconsumers to give consents."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-53-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
