      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.85",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The CDR representative principal must make available a simple method of\ncommunication for the withdrawal of consent, as an alternative to using the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s consumer dashboard.\nNote 1:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The CDR representative principal must make available a simple method of\ncommunication for the withdrawal of consent, as an alternative to using the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s consumer dashboard.\nNote 1:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
