      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-56-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits withdrawal of consent",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) if the consent is withdrawn in accordance with paragraph 4.20J(1)(b)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-56-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits withdrawal of consent after a certain period",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) the end of the period of 12 months after the later of the following:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-56-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits withdrawal of consent if it would affect another provision",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(e) if the consent expires as a result of the operation of another provision of these rules that references this paragraph—when the consent expires."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-57",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 26A, of the withdrawal of an authorisation to disclose CDR data that",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-57"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "relates to a collection consent given under this Division; and\n(b) the collection consent has not expired in accordance with subrule (1);\nthe collection consent expires when the CDR representative principal receives\nthat notification.\nNote:\nThis would not result in the use consent relating to any CDR data that had already been\ncollected expiring, so it may continue to be used by the CDR representative in\naccordance with those consents. However, see the notification requirement of rule",
      "skos:definition": "relates to a collection consent given under this Division; and\n(b) the collection consent has not expired in accordance with subrule (1);\nthe collection consent expires when the CDR representative principal receives\nthat notification.\nNote:\nThis would not result in the use consent relating to any CDR data that had already been\ncollected expiring, so it may continue to be used by the CDR representative in\naccordance with those consents. However, see the notification requirement of rule",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-57-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-57-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9a83dde62170ec0e1ed87e5f0bc31a8acb9d27667b409adef0d69d5acb949c2e",
      "skos:note": "Collection consent expires when notified"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-57",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 26A, of the withdrawal of an authorisation to disclose CDR data that",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "relates to a collection consent given under this Division; and\n(b) the collection consent has not expired in accordance with subrule (1);\nthe collection consent expires when the CDR representative principal receives\nthat notification.\nNote:\nThis would not result in the use consent relating to any CDR data that had already been\ncollected expiring, so it may continue to be used by the CDR representative in\naccordance with those consents. However, see the notification requirement of rule"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-57-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-57"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-57-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes an obligation on the CDR representative principal",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:conclusionText": "The collection consent expires when notified"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-58",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20Q.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-58"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n(a) a CDR representative principal has a collection consent given under this\nDivision to collect particular CDR data from a particular accredited data\nrecipient; and\n(b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent to disclose that\nCDR data to that CDR representative principal;\nthen if one of those consents expires, the other expires when the CDR\nrepresentative principal or accredited data recipient is notified of the\nfirst-mentioned expiry.\nNote:\nThe notification is required by rule 4.18B.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20L\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(4) If a CDR representative principal’s accreditation is revoked or surrendered in\naccordance with rule 5.17, all of the consents of any of the CDR representative\nprincipal’s CDR representatives expire when the revocation or surrender takes\neffect.\nSubdivision 4.3A.6—Information relating to de-identification of CDR data",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If:\n(a) a CDR representative principal has a collection consent given under this\nDivision to collect particular CDR data from a particular accredited data\nrecipient; and\n(b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent to disclose that\nCDR data to that CDR representative principal;\nthen if one of those consents expires, the other expires when the CDR\nrepresentative principal or accredited data recipient is notified of the\nfirst-mentioned expiry.\nNote:\nThe notification is required by rule 4.18B.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20L\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(4) If a CDR representative principal’s accreditation is revoked or surrendered in\naccordance with rule 5.17, all of the consents of any of the CDR representative\nprincipal’s CDR representatives expire when the revocation or surrender takes\neffect.\nSubdivision 4.3A.6—Information relating to de-identification of CDR data",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-58-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-58-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e10d5a88004ed57c95ea39d04396b8600ba5df0e62335937777b4127584f4d00"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-58",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20Q.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n(a) a CDR representative principal has a collection consent given under this\nDivision to collect particular CDR data from a particular accredited data\nrecipient; and\n(b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent to disclose that\nCDR data to that CDR representative principal;\nthen if one of those consents expires, the other expires when the CDR\nrepresentative principal or accredited data recipient is notified of the\nfirst-mentioned expiry.\nNote:\nThe notification is required by rule 4.18B.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20L\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(4) If a CDR representative principal’s accreditation is revoked or surrendered in\naccordance with rule 5.17, all of the consents of any of the CDR representative\nprincipal’s CDR representatives expire when the revocation or surrender takes\neffect.\nSubdivision 4.3A.6—Information relating to de-identification of CDR data"
    },
