      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n(a) a CDR representative principal has a collection consent given under this\nDivision to collect particular CDR data from a particular accredited data\nrecipient; and\n(b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent to disclose that\nCDR data to that CDR representative principal;\nthen if one of those consents expires, the other expires when the CDR\nrepresentative principal or accredited data recipient is notified of the\nfirst-mentioned expiry.\nNote:\nThe notification is required by rule 4.18B.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20L\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If:\n(a) a CDR representative principal has a collection consent given under this\nDivision to collect particular CDR data from a particular accredited data\nrecipient; and\n(b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent to disclose that\nCDR data to that CDR representative principal;\nthen if one of those consents expires, the other expires when the CDR\nrepresentative principal or accredited data recipient is notified of the\nfirst-mentioned expiry.\nNote:\nThe notification is required by rule 4.18B.\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20L\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "values:partOf": {
