    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-58-ss-4-logic-argumentation-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Imply",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Implies expiration of consents upon accreditation revocation/surrender.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) If a CDR representative principal’s accreditation is revoked or surrendered...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...all of the consents of any of the CDR representative principal’s CDR representatives expire when the revocation or surrender takes effect."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-59",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20L  Additional information relating to de-identification of CDR data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-59"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.87",
      "values:originalText": "For paragraph 4.20E(3)(i), the additional information relating to de-identification\nis the following:\n(a) what the CDR data de-identification process is;\n(b) if it would disclose (by sale or otherwise) the de-identified data to one or\nmore other persons;\n(i) that fact; and\n(ii) the classes of persons to which it would disclose that data; and\n(iii) why it would so disclose that data;\n(c) if the CDR representative would use the de-identified data for general\nresearch―that fact, together with a link to a description in the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s CDR policy of:\n(i) the research to be conducted; and\n(ii) any additional benefit to be provided to the CDR consumer for\nconsenting to the use;\n(e) that the CDR consumer would not be able to elect, in accordance with rule",
      "skos:definition": "For paragraph 4.20E(3)(i), the additional information relating to de-identification\nis the following:\n(a) what the CDR data de-identification process is;\n(b) if it would disclose (by sale or otherwise) the de-identified data to one or\nmore other persons;\n(i) that fact; and\n(ii) the classes of persons to which it would disclose that data; and\n(iii) why it would so disclose that data;\n(c) if the CDR representative would use the de-identified data for general\nresearch―that fact, together with a link to a description in the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s CDR policy of:\n(i) the research to be conducted; and\n(ii) any additional benefit to be provided to the CDR consumer for\nconsenting to the use;\n(e) that the CDR consumer would not be able to elect, in accordance with rule",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-59-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd33acf5104e66cfe8ee1935b3c0778bfe918f91fb0adb9afe8869d8f0a22c4d",
      "skos:note": "Provides additional information about de-identification of CDR data",
      "dc:description": "Additional information relating to de-identification of CDR data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-59",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20L  Additional information relating to de-identification of CDR data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 87,
      "values:originalText": "For paragraph 4.20E(3)(i), the additional information relating to de-identification\nis the following:\n(a) what the CDR data de-identification process is;\n(b) if it would disclose (by sale or otherwise) the de-identified data to one or\nmore other persons;\n(i) that fact; and\n(ii) the classes of persons to which it would disclose that data; and\n(iii) why it would so disclose that data;\n(c) if the CDR representative would use the de-identified data for general\nresearch―that fact, together with a link to a description in the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s CDR policy of:\n(i) the research to be conducted; and\n(ii) any additional benefit to be provided to the CDR consumer for\nconsenting to the use;\n(e) that the CDR consumer would not be able to elect, in accordance with rule"
    },
