    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-65",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20P  Notification of data holder or accredited data recipient if collection",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-65"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "consent expires\n(1) This rule applies if:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20Q\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request on behalf of a CDR\nrepresentative to a CDR participant based on a collection consent given\nunder this Division relating to particular CDR data and a particular CDR\nparticipant; and\n(b) the request has not been completely resolved; and\n(c) the consent expires for any reason.\n(2) The accredited person must notify:\n(a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with\nthe data standards, that the consent has expired; and\n(b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data\nrecipient as soon as practicable that the consent has expired.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "consent expires\n(1) This rule applies if:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20Q\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request on behalf of a CDR\nrepresentative to a CDR participant based on a collection consent given\nunder this Division relating to particular CDR data and a particular CDR\nparticipant; and\n(b) the request has not been completely resolved; and\n(c) the consent expires for any reason.\n(2) The accredited person must notify:\n(a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with\nthe data standards, that the consent has expired; and\n(b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data\nrecipient as soon as practicable that the consent has expired.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
