    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-66",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20Q  Notification of consumer if collection consent expires",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-66"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if, in relation to particular goods or services a CDR\nrepresentative is providing as referred to in subrule 4.3A(1):\n(a) the collection consent expires; but\n(b) the use consent, or any disclosure consent, is current.\n(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer as soon as practicable\nafter the collection consent expires that, at any time, they:\n(a) may withdraw the use consent or disclosure consent; and\n(b) may make the election to delete redundant data in respect of that CDR data\nunder rule 4.20M.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A).\n(3) The notification must be given in writing otherwise than through the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s consumer dashboard.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\n(4) The notification may also be included in the CDR representative principal’s\nconsumer dashboard.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies if, in relation to particular goods or services a CDR\nrepresentative is providing as referred to in subrule 4.3A(1):\n(a) the collection consent expires; but\n(b) the use consent, or any disclosure consent, is current.\n(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer as soon as practicable\nafter the collection consent expires that, at any time, they:\n(a) may withdraw the use consent or disclosure consent; and\n(b) may make the election to delete redundant data in respect of that CDR data\nunder rule 4.20M.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A).\n(3) The notification must be given in writing otherwise than through the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s consumer dashboard.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\n(4) The notification may also be included in the CDR representative principal’s\nconsumer dashboard.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-66-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-66-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-66-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-66-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a349a771ee691a2b14d21570e372b591cd1eeab71333d0c2ea9cd235ca4f091f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-66",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20Q  Notification of consumer if collection consent expires",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if, in relation to particular goods or services a CDR\nrepresentative is providing as referred to in subrule 4.3A(1):\n(a) the collection consent expires; but\n(b) the use consent, or any disclosure consent, is current.\n(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer as soon as practicable\nafter the collection consent expires that, at any time, they:\n(a) may withdraw the use consent or disclosure consent; and\n(b) may make the election to delete redundant data in respect of that CDR data\nunder rule 4.20M.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A).\n(3) The notification must be given in writing otherwise than through the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s consumer dashboard.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\n(4) The notification may also be included in the CDR representative principal’s\nconsumer dashboard.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5)."
    },
