    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-66-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(2) 20Q  Notification of consumer if collection consent expires",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-66-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer as soon as practicable\nafter the collection consent expires that, at any time, they:\n(a) may withdraw the use consent or disclosure consent; and\n(b) may make the election to delete redundant data in respect of that CDR data\nunder rule 4.20M.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer as soon as practicable\nafter the collection consent expires that, at any time, they:\n(a) may withdraw the use consent or disclosure consent; and\n(b) may make the election to delete redundant data in respect of that CDR data\nunder rule 4.20M.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-66"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-66-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-66-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "726a48d067122aea7847255bb5d43b3158b0d308e4edd6ab005744b4f220fe28",
      "skos:note": "Notify CDR consumer of expired collection consent",
      "dc:description": "Notification"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-66-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(2) 20Q  Notification of consumer if collection consent expires",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer as soon as practicable\nafter the collection consent expires that, at any time, they:\n(a) may withdraw the use consent or disclosure consent; and\n(b) may make the election to delete redundant data in respect of that CDR data\nunder rule 4.20M.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A)."
    },
