    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-68",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20S  Notification if collection consent is amended",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-68"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) a CDR representative principal has made a consumer data request to a\nCDR participant on behalf of a CDR representative, based on a collection\nconsent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and a\nparticular CDR participant; and\n(b) the request has not been completely resolved; and\n(c) the CDR consumer amends the consent.\n(2) The CDR representative principal must notify:\n(a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with\nthe data standards, that the consent has been amended; and\n(b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data\nrecipient as soon as practicable that the consent has been amended.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) a CDR representative principal has made a consumer data request to a\nCDR participant on behalf of a CDR representative, based on a collection\nconsent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and a\nparticular CDR participant; and\n(b) the request has not been completely resolved; and\n(c) the CDR consumer amends the consent.\n(2) The CDR representative principal must notify:\n(a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with\nthe data standards, that the consent has been amended; and\n(b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data\nrecipient as soon as practicable that the consent has been amended.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "965723d47737023e8412777000df1dd0f5e47133875ebd9cc3bdcc8a42df59fd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-68",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20S  Notification if collection consent is amended",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) a CDR representative principal has made a consumer data request to a\nCDR participant on behalf of a CDR representative, based on a collection\nconsent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and a\nparticular CDR participant; and\n(b) the request has not been completely resolved; and\n(c) the CDR consumer amends the consent.\n(2) The CDR representative principal must notify:\n(a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with\nthe data standards, that the consent has been amended; and\n(b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data\nrecipient as soon as practicable that the consent has been amended.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
