    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(2) 20S  Notification if collection consent is amended",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The CDR representative principal must notify:\n(a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with\nthe data standards, that the consent has been amended; and\n(b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data\nrecipient as soon as practicable that the consent has been amended.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The CDR representative principal must notify:\n(a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with\nthe data standards, that the consent has been amended; and\n(b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data\nrecipient as soon as practicable that the consent has been amended.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-68"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c046f06d63791d7f5fe97fcca696f550405573af438ee39f8753023d8041a368",
      "skos:note": "Notify data holder and accredited data recipient of amended consent",
      "dc:description": "Notification"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(2) 20S  Notification if collection consent is amended",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The CDR representative principal must notify:\n(a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with\nthe data standards, that the consent has been amended; and\n(b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data\nrecipient as soon as practicable that the consent has been amended.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-2-norm",
