    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-69",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20T  Updating consumer dashboard",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-69"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR representative must inform the CDR representative principal as soon as\npracticable after the information required to be contained on the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s consumer dashboard changes.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\n(2) The CDR representative principal must, as soon as practicable, make those\nchanges.\nNote 1:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nNote 2:\nThe CDR representative principal could arrange for the CDR representative to update\nthe consumer dashboard on the CDR representative principal’s behalf: see subrule",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A CDR representative must inform the CDR representative principal as soon as\npracticable after the information required to be contained on the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s consumer dashboard changes.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\n(2) The CDR representative principal must, as soon as practicable, make those\nchanges.\nNote 1:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nNote 2:\nThe CDR representative principal could arrange for the CDR representative to update\nthe consumer dashboard on the CDR representative principal’s behalf: see subrule",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-69-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-69-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d278870767f013b38b4d05b69ed5d8ebfe076bd7c686ba97b037aaf45770851b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-69",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20T  Updating consumer dashboard",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR representative must inform the CDR representative principal as soon as\npracticable after the information required to be contained on the CDR\nrepresentative principal’s consumer dashboard changes.\nNote:\nThe CDR representative principal may allow the CDR representative to provide the\nconsumer dashboard on its behalf—see subrule 1.14(5).\n(2) The CDR representative principal must, as soon as practicable, make those\nchanges.\nNote 1:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\nNote 2:\nThe CDR representative principal could arrange for the CDR representative to update\nthe consumer dashboard on the CDR representative principal’s behalf: see subrule"
    },
