    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-71",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 20U  Ongoing notification requirement—current consents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-71"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure\nconsent given under this Division if:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20U\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) the consent is current; and\n(b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following:\n(i) the CDR consumer gave the consent;\n(ii) the CDR consumer last amended the consent;\n(iii) the CDR consumer last used the CDR representative principal’s\nconsumer dashboard;\n(iv) the CDR representative or the CDR representative principal last\nnotified the CDR consumer that the consent is still current.\n(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer, in relation to each\nconsent given by the CDR consumer that is still current, that the consent is still\ncurrent.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A).\n(3) The notification must be given in accordance with the data standards.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure\nconsent given under this Division if:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20U\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) the consent is current; and\n(b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following:\n(i) the CDR consumer gave the consent;\n(ii) the CDR consumer last amended the consent;\n(iii) the CDR consumer last used the CDR representative principal’s\nconsumer dashboard;\n(iv) the CDR representative or the CDR representative principal last\nnotified the CDR consumer that the consent is still current.\n(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer, in relation to each\nconsent given by the CDR consumer that is still current, that the consent is still\ncurrent.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A).\n(3) The notification must be given in accordance with the data standards.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-71-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-71-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-71-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b373337c97810df53c0122166a8822af6e67cad650a93b10fc629aa5ce630ef5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-71",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 20U  Ongoing notification requirement—current consents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure\nconsent given under this Division if:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20U\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) the consent is current; and\n(b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following:\n(i) the CDR consumer gave the consent;\n(ii) the CDR consumer last amended the consent;\n(iii) the CDR consumer last used the CDR representative principal’s\nconsumer dashboard;\n(iv) the CDR representative or the CDR representative principal last\nnotified the CDR consumer that the consent is still current.\n(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer, in relation to each\nconsent given by the CDR consumer that is still current, that the consent is still\ncurrent.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A).\n(3) The notification must be given in accordance with the data standards.\nNote:\nA failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil\npenalty (see rule 1.16A)."
    },
