      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure\nconsent given under this Division if:\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nGiving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A\nSection 4.20U\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) the consent is current; and\n(b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following:\n(i) the CDR consumer gave the consent;\n(ii) the CDR consumer last amended the consent;\n(iii) the CDR consumer last used the CDR representative principal’s\nconsumer dashboard;\n(iv) the CDR representative or the CDR representative principal last\nnotified the CDR consumer that the consent is still current.",
