    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-75",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 23  Asking CDR consumer to give authorisation to disclose CDR data or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-75"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.92",
      "values:originalText": "inviting CDR consumer to amend a current authorisation\n(1) When asking a CDR consumer to authorise the disclosure of CDR data, or\namend a current authorisation, a data holder must give the CDR consumer the\nfollowing information about the authorisation or amendment:\n(a) subject to subrule (2), the name of the accredited person that made the\nrequest;\n(b) the period of time to which the CDR data that was the subject of the\nrequest relates;\n(c) the types of CDR data for which the data holder is seeking an authorisation\nto disclose;\n(d) whether the authorisation is being sought for:\n(i) disclosure of CDR data on a single occasion; or\n(ii) disclosure of CDR data over a period of time of not more than 12\nmonths;\n(e) if authorisation is being sought for disclosure over a period of time―what\nthat period is;\n(f) a statement that, at any time, the authorisation can be withdrawn;\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nAuthorisations to disclose CDR data  Division 4.4\nSection 4.24\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(g) instructions for how the authorisation can be withdrawn.\nNote:\nWhile certain consents by a CDR business consumer can have a period of 7 years, a\ncorresponding authorisation cannot be for more than 12 months before renewal under\nsubparagraph (1)(d)(ii).\n(2) The data holder must also give the CDR consumer any information that the\nRegister of Accredited Persons holds in relation to the accredited person that is\nspecified as information for the purposes of this rule.",
      "skos:definition": "inviting CDR consumer to amend a current authorisation\n(1) When asking a CDR consumer to authorise the disclosure of CDR data, or\namend a current authorisation, a data holder must give the CDR consumer the\nfollowing information about the authorisation or amendment:\n(a) subject to subrule (2), the name of the accredited person that made the\nrequest;\n(b) the period of time to which the CDR data that was the subject of the\nrequest relates;\n(c) the types of CDR data for which the data holder is seeking an authorisation\nto disclose;\n(d) whether the authorisation is being sought for:\n(i) disclosure of CDR data on a single occasion; or\n(ii) disclosure of CDR data over a period of time of not more than 12\nmonths;\n(e) if authorisation is being sought for disclosure over a period of time―what\nthat period is;\n(f) a statement that, at any time, the authorisation can be withdrawn;\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nAuthorisations to disclose CDR data  Division 4.4\nSection 4.24\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(g) instructions for how the authorisation can be withdrawn.\nNote:\nWhile certain consents by a CDR business consumer can have a period of 7 years, a\ncorresponding authorisation cannot be for more than 12 months before renewal under\nsubparagraph (1)(d)(ii).\n(2) The data holder must also give the CDR consumer any information that the\nRegister of Accredited Persons holds in relation to the accredited person that is\nspecified as information for the purposes of this rule.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-75-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-75-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2a4cac803d6d656b2636647c92f97eaf0053e14ab9728d22fd528dc8f8265d5d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-75",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 23  Asking CDR consumer to give authorisation to disclose CDR data or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 92,
      "values:originalText": "inviting CDR consumer to amend a current authorisation\n(1) When asking a CDR consumer to authorise the disclosure of CDR data, or\namend a current authorisation, a data holder must give the CDR consumer the\nfollowing information about the authorisation or amendment:\n(a) subject to subrule (2), the name of the accredited person that made the\nrequest;\n(b) the period of time to which the CDR data that was the subject of the\nrequest relates;\n(c) the types of CDR data for which the data holder is seeking an authorisation\nto disclose;\n(d) whether the authorisation is being sought for:\n(i) disclosure of CDR data on a single occasion; or\n(ii) disclosure of CDR data over a period of time of not more than 12\nmonths;\n(e) if authorisation is being sought for disclosure over a period of time―what\nthat period is;\n(f) a statement that, at any time, the authorisation can be withdrawn;\n\n\nConsumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4\nAuthorisations to disclose CDR data  Division 4.4\nSection 4.24\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(g) instructions for how the authorisation can be withdrawn.\nNote:\nWhile certain consents by a CDR business consumer can have a period of 7 years, a\ncorresponding authorisation cannot be for more than 12 months before renewal under\nsubparagraph (1)(d)(ii).\n(2) The data holder must also give the CDR consumer any information that the\nRegister of Accredited Persons holds in relation to the accredited person that is\nspecified as information for the purposes of this rule."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-75-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(1) 23  Asking CDR consumer to give authorisation to disclose CDR data or",
