    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-76",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 24  Restrictions when asking CDR consumer to authorise disclosure of CDR",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-76"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.93",
      "values:originalText": "data\nWhen asking a CDR consumer to authorise the disclosure of CDR data or to\namend a current authorisation, the data holder must not do any of the following:\n(a) add any requirements to the authorisation process beyond those specified in\nthe data standards and these rules;\n(b) provide or request additional information during the authorisation process\nbeyond that specified in the data standards and these rules;\n(c) offer additional or alternative services as part of the authorisation process;\n(d) include or refer to other documents.",
      "skos:definition": "data\nWhen asking a CDR consumer to authorise the disclosure of CDR data or to\namend a current authorisation, the data holder must not do any of the following:\n(a) add any requirements to the authorisation process beyond those specified in\nthe data standards and these rules;\n(b) provide or request additional information during the authorisation process\nbeyond that specified in the data standards and these rules;\n(c) offer additional or alternative services as part of the authorisation process;\n(d) include or refer to other documents.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-76-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-76-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9472900f58317b5568f0033f638fbcb1268695aa553c101485a15b57b6282f40",
      "skos:note": "Restrictions on disclosure of CDR data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-76",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 24  Restrictions when asking CDR consumer to authorise disclosure of CDR",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 93,
      "values:originalText": "data\nWhen asking a CDR consumer to authorise the disclosure of CDR data or to\namend a current authorisation, the data holder must not do any of the following:\n(a) add any requirements to the authorisation process beyond those specified in\nthe data standards and these rules;\n(b) provide or request additional information during the authorisation process\nbeyond that specified in the data standards and these rules;\n(c) offer additional or alternative services as part of the authorisation process;\n(d) include or refer to other documents."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-76-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-76"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-76-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "forbid",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-77",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 25  Withdrawal of authorisation to disclose CDR data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-77"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.93",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR consumer who has given an authorisation to a data holder to disclose\nparticular CDR data to an accredited person may withdraw the authorisation at\nany time:\n(a) by using the data holder’s consumer dashboard; or\n(b) by using a simple alternative method of communication to be made\navailable by the data holder for that purpose.\n(2) If the withdrawal was in accordance with paragraph (1)(b), the data holder must\ngive effect to the withdrawal as soon as practicable, and in any case within 2\nbusiness days after receiving the communication.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A CDR consumer who has given an authorisation to a data holder to disclose\nparticular CDR data to an accredited person may withdraw the authorisation at\nany time:\n(a) by using the data holder’s consumer dashboard; or\n(b) by using a simple alternative method of communication to be made\navailable by the data holder for that purpose.\n(2) If the withdrawal was in accordance with paragraph (1)(b), the data holder must\ngive effect to the withdrawal as soon as practicable, and in any case within 2\nbusiness days after receiving the communication.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-77-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-77-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d998acae9d8f52add32c2e2422c664390a144419890975fdf1947bb87304401c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4-77",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 25  Withdrawal of authorisation to disclose CDR data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 93,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR consumer who has given an authorisation to a data holder to disclose\nparticular CDR data to an accredited person may withdraw the authorisation at\nany time:\n(a) by using the data holder’s consumer dashboard; or\n(b) by using a simple alternative method of communication to be made\navailable by the data holder for that purpose.\n(2) If the withdrawal was in accordance with paragraph (1)(b), the data holder must\ngive effect to the withdrawal as soon as practicable, and in any case within 2\nbusiness days after receiving the communication.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
