    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4A 1  Purpose of Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.95",
      "values:originalText": "Special rules apply in relation to consumer data requests under Part 4 under\nwhich there is a request for disclosure of CDR data that relates to one or more\njoint accounts. This Part sets out those rules.",
      "skos:definition": "Special rules apply in relation to consumer data requests under Part 4 under\nwhich there is a request for disclosure of CDR data that relates to one or more\njoint accounts. This Part sets out those rules.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e38e82e558aa324d272bb218a9fe8d5ac473bec2507be6fc9761daba5e028122",
      "skos:note": "Special rules apply for joint accounts in consumer data requests."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4A 1  Purpose of Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 95,
      "values:originalText": "Special rules apply in relation to consumer data requests under Part 4 under\nwhich there is a request for disclosure of CDR data that relates to one or more\njoint accounts. This Part sets out those rules."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4A 2  Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.95",
      "values:originalText": "CDR data that relates to a joint account can be disclosed under these rules only in\naccordance with the disclosure option that applies to the account. Division 4A.2\nsets out:\n•\nthe three disclosure options, with the default option being the\npre-approval option; and\n•\nan obligation for data holders to provide a service (a disclosure option\nmanagement service) for all joint accounts to which this Part applies\nthrough which joint account holders can change the disclosure option\nthat applies to the account, or propose a change to the other account\nholders; and\n•\nwhen one joint account holder proposes to change the disclosure\noption―a process by which the other joint account holders can either\nagree with or reject the proposal; and\n•\nsome associated notification requirements.\nAny joint account holder can choose that the non-disclosure option will apply.\nIf the pre-approval option applies, any joint account holder can choose that the\nco-approval option will apply.\nA change from the non-disclosure option to another option, or a change from the\nco-approval option to the pre-approval option, requires the agreement of all the\njoint account holders.\nWhen an accredited person makes a consumer data request under Part 4 on\nbehalf of a CDR consumer, and the request includes CDR data relating to one or\nmore joint accounts of which the CDR consumer is a joint account holder,",
      "skos:definition": "CDR data that relates to a joint account can be disclosed under these rules only in\naccordance with the disclosure option that applies to the account. Division 4A.2\nsets out:\n•\nthe three disclosure options, with the default option being the\npre-approval option; and\n•\nan obligation for data holders to provide a service (a disclosure option\nmanagement service) for all joint accounts to which this Part applies\nthrough which joint account holders can change the disclosure option\nthat applies to the account, or propose a change to the other account\nholders; and\n•\nwhen one joint account holder proposes to change the disclosure\noption―a process by which the other joint account holders can either\nagree with or reject the proposal; and\n•\nsome associated notification requirements.\nAny joint account holder can choose that the non-disclosure option will apply.\nIf the pre-approval option applies, any joint account holder can choose that the\nco-approval option will apply.\nA change from the non-disclosure option to another option, or a change from the\nco-approval option to the pre-approval option, requires the agreement of all the\njoint account holders.\nWhen an accredited person makes a consumer data request under Part 4 on\nbehalf of a CDR consumer, and the request includes CDR data relating to one or\nmore joint accounts of which the CDR consumer is a joint account holder,",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0ca00929c7734a1b2ad3164e5f68974b57202e11fb3eb5fbd720d5fa56ac4527",
      "skos:note": "Joint account holders must agree on changes to disclosure options."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4A 2  Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 95,
      "values:originalText": "CDR data that relates to a joint account can be disclosed under these rules only in\naccordance with the disclosure option that applies to the account. Division 4A.2\nsets out:\n•\nthe three disclosure options, with the default option being the\npre-approval option; and\n•\nan obligation for data holders to provide a service (a disclosure option\nmanagement service) for all joint accounts to which this Part applies\nthrough which joint account holders can change the disclosure option\nthat applies to the account, or propose a change to the other account\nholders; and\n•\nwhen one joint account holder proposes to change the disclosure\noption―a process by which the other joint account holders can either\nagree with or reject the proposal; and\n•\nsome associated notification requirements.\nAny joint account holder can choose that the non-disclosure option will apply.\nIf the pre-approval option applies, any joint account holder can choose that the\nco-approval option will apply.\nA change from the non-disclosure option to another option, or a change from the\nco-approval option to the pre-approval option, requires the agreement of all the\njoint account holders.\nWhen an accredited person makes a consumer data request under Part 4 on\nbehalf of a CDR consumer, and the request includes CDR data relating to one or\nmore joint accounts of which the CDR consumer is a joint account holder,"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Joint account holders have an obligation to agree on changes.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "ClassInclusion",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The disclosure options are defined in Division 4A.2.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4A 3  Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "For this Part, in relation to a consumer data request to a data holder under Part 4\nwhere the CDR data requested includes CDR data that relates to a joint account:\n(a) the requester is the person on whose behalf the consumer data request was\nmade; and\n(b) the relevant account holders are:\n(i) if the requester is a secondary user―all joint account holders; and\n(ii) if the requester is a joint account holder―the other joint account\nholders; and\n(c) the joint account data is the CDR data relating to the joint account that\nwas the subject of the request.\nNote:\nThe CDR data that can be requested on behalf a  CDR consumer is governed by the\nrelevant general provisions in the sector Schedules, so that, for example, customer data\nthat relates to another joint account holder cannot be covered by a consumer data\nrequest (see paragraphs 3.2(3)(b) of Schedule 3 and 3.2(3)(b) of Schedule 4).\n\n\nJoint accounts  Part 4A\nDisclosure options  Division 4A.2\nSection 4A.4\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "skos:definition": "For this Part, in relation to a consumer data request to a data holder under Part 4\nwhere the CDR data requested includes CDR data that relates to a joint account:\n(a) the requester is the person on whose behalf the consumer data request was\nmade; and\n(b) the relevant account holders are:\n(i) if the requester is a secondary user―all joint account holders; and\n(ii) if the requester is a joint account holder―the other joint account\nholders; and\n(c) the joint account data is the CDR data relating to the joint account that\nwas the subject of the request.\nNote:\nThe CDR data that can be requested on behalf a  CDR consumer is governed by the\nrelevant general provisions in the sector Schedules, so that, for example, customer data\nthat relates to another joint account holder cannot be covered by a consumer data\nrequest (see paragraphs 3.2(3)(b) of Schedule 3 and 3.2(3)(b) of Schedule 4).\n\n\nJoint accounts  Part 4A\nDisclosure options  Division 4A.2\nSection 4A.4\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-4-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-4-logic-descriptionlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-4-logic-descriptionlogic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a677575ba89fee5a4edf746b53828f0361570c008ee0ac2cd796da98c3165450",
      "skos:note": "Defines who is the requester and relevant account holders in a joint account for consumer data requests."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4A 3  Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "For this Part, in relation to a consumer data request to a data holder under Part 4\nwhere the CDR data requested includes CDR data that relates to a joint account:\n(a) the requester is the person on whose behalf the consumer data request was\nmade; and\n(b) the relevant account holders are:\n(i) if the requester is a secondary user―all joint account holders; and\n(ii) if the requester is a joint account holder―the other joint account\nholders; and\n(c) the joint account data is the CDR data relating to the joint account that\nwas the subject of the request.\nNote:\nThe CDR data that can be requested on behalf a  CDR consumer is governed by the\nrelevant general provisions in the sector Schedules, so that, for example, customer data\nthat relates to another joint account holder cannot be covered by a consumer data\nrequest (see paragraphs 3.2(3)(b) of Schedule 3 and 3.2(3)(b) of Schedule 4).\n\n\nJoint accounts  Part 4A\nDisclosure options  Division 4A.2\nSection 4A.4\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-4-norm",
