    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4A 6  Obligation to provide disclosure option management service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.98",
      "values:originalText": "Obligation to provide disclosure option management service\n(1) For each joint account to which this Part applies, the data holder must provide a\nservice to each joint account holder that allows the joint account holder to:\n(a) change the disclosure option that applies to the account in accordance with\nrule 4A.7; and\n(b) propose a change in the disclosure option to the other joint account holders\nin accordance with rule 4A.8; and\n(c) respond to a proposal by another joint account holder to change the\ndisclosure option.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) Such a service is a disclosure option management service.\nRequirements for disclosure option management service\n(3) The service must be provided online and, if there is a data holder’s consumer\ndashboard for a joint account holder, may be included in the dashboard.\n(4) The service may, but need not, also be provided other than online.\n(5) The service must give effect to a change in the disclosure option as soon as\npracticable.\n(6) The service must not do any of the following in relation to the processes that it\nprovides for changing or proposing to change the disclosure option that applies\nto the joint account, or responding to such a proposal (the processes):\n\n\nJoint accounts  Part 4A\nDisclosure options  Division 4A.2\nSection 4A.7\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) add any requirements to the processes beyond those specified in the data\nstandards and these rules;\n(b) offer additional or alternative services as part of the processes;\n(c) include or refer to other documents, or provide any other information, so as\nto reduce comprehensibility;\n(d) offer any pre-selected options.\n(7) The service must indicate to the joint account holder which disclosure option\ncurrently applies.\n(8) The service must be in accordance with the data standards.",
      "skos:definition": "Obligation to provide disclosure option management service\n(1) For each joint account to which this Part applies, the data holder must provide a\nservice to each joint account holder that allows the joint account holder to:\n(a) change the disclosure option that applies to the account in accordance with\nrule 4A.7; and\n(b) propose a change in the disclosure option to the other joint account holders\nin accordance with rule 4A.8; and\n(c) respond to a proposal by another joint account holder to change the\ndisclosure option.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) Such a service is a disclosure option management service.\nRequirements for disclosure option management service\n(3) The service must be provided online and, if there is a data holder’s consumer\ndashboard for a joint account holder, may be included in the dashboard.\n(4) The service may, but need not, also be provided other than online.\n(5) The service must give effect to a change in the disclosure option as soon as\npracticable.\n(6) The service must not do any of the following in relation to the processes that it\nprovides for changing or proposing to change the disclosure option that applies\nto the joint account, or responding to such a proposal (the processes):\n\n\nJoint accounts  Part 4A\nDisclosure options  Division 4A.2\nSection 4A.7\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) add any requirements to the processes beyond those specified in the data\nstandards and these rules;\n(b) offer additional or alternative services as part of the processes;\n(c) include or refer to other documents, or provide any other information, so as\nto reduce comprehensibility;\n(d) offer any pre-selected options.\n(7) The service must indicate to the joint account holder which disclosure option\ncurrently applies.\n(8) The service must be in accordance with the data standards.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-7-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-7-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-7-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-7-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-7-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-7-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-7-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-7-ss-8"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6fc9ffaf96aa1a508447773a1711fd3016ba47913a690a675f000f893590a15f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4A 6  Obligation to provide disclosure option management service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 98,
      "values:originalText": "Obligation to provide disclosure option management service\n(1) For each joint account to which this Part applies, the data holder must provide a\nservice to each joint account holder that allows the joint account holder to:\n(a) change the disclosure option that applies to the account in accordance with\nrule 4A.7; and\n(b) propose a change in the disclosure option to the other joint account holders\nin accordance with rule 4A.8; and\n(c) respond to a proposal by another joint account holder to change the\ndisclosure option.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) Such a service is a disclosure option management service.\nRequirements for disclosure option management service\n(3) The service must be provided online and, if there is a data holder’s consumer\ndashboard for a joint account holder, may be included in the dashboard.\n(4) The service may, but need not, also be provided other than online.\n(5) The service must give effect to a change in the disclosure option as soon as\npracticable.\n(6) The service must not do any of the following in relation to the processes that it\nprovides for changing or proposing to change the disclosure option that applies\nto the joint account, or responding to such a proposal (the processes):\n\n\nJoint accounts  Part 4A\nDisclosure options  Division 4A.2\nSection 4A.7\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) add any requirements to the processes beyond those specified in the data\nstandards and these rules;\n(b) offer additional or alternative services as part of the processes;\n(c) include or refer to other documents, or provide any other information, so as\nto reduce comprehensibility;\n(d) offer any pre-selected options.\n(7) The service must indicate to the joint account holder which disclosure option\ncurrently applies.\n(8) The service must be in accordance with the data standards."
    },
    {
