      "skos:note": "Joint account holders must be provided with a service to change disclosure options.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-7-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4A(1) 6  Obligation to provide disclosure option management service",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 98,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For each joint account to which this Part applies, the data holder must provide a\nservice to each joint account holder that allows the joint account holder to:\n(a) change the disclosure option that applies to the account in accordance with\nrule 4A.7; and\n(b) propose a change in the disclosure option to the other joint account holders\nin accordance with rule 4A.8; and\n(c) respond to a proposal by another joint account holder to change the\ndisclosure option.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-7-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
