    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-18",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4A 11(e); or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-18"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.104",
      "values:originalText": "(ii) a relevant account holder has withdrawn an approval previously\ngiven;\nin accordance with the data standards.\n(2) The data holder must make the appropriate approval notification to a joint\naccount holder in relation to an event mentioned in subrule (1):\n(a) as soon as practicable after the event occurs, unless the joint account holder\nhas selected an alternative schedule of notifications; and\n(b) through its ordinary means of contacting the joint account holders.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The data holder must, in accordance with any relevant data standards:\n(a) provide for alternative notification schedules (including reducing the\nfrequency of notifications or not receiving notifications); and\n(b) give each joint account holder a means of selecting such an alternative, and\nof changing a selection.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(ii) a relevant account holder has withdrawn an approval previously\ngiven;\nin accordance with the data standards.\n(2) The data holder must make the appropriate approval notification to a joint\naccount holder in relation to an event mentioned in subrule (1):\n(a) as soon as practicable after the event occurs, unless the joint account holder\nhas selected an alternative schedule of notifications; and\n(b) through its ordinary means of contacting the joint account holders.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The data holder must, in accordance with any relevant data standards:\n(a) provide for alternative notification schedules (including reducing the\nfrequency of notifications or not receiving notifications); and\n(b) give each joint account holder a means of selecting such an alternative, and\nof changing a selection.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-18-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4a-18-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3aa9ce029a210bcce001c029edff285bde22be99cca7c8c4cde8bdc491f86cea"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-4a-18",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4A 11(e); or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 104,
      "values:originalText": "(ii) a relevant account holder has withdrawn an approval previously\ngiven;\nin accordance with the data standards.\n(2) The data holder must make the appropriate approval notification to a joint\naccount holder in relation to an event mentioned in subrule (1):\n(a) as soon as practicable after the event occurs, unless the joint account holder\nhas selected an alternative schedule of notifications; and\n(b) through its ordinary means of contacting the joint account holders.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(3) The data holder must, in accordance with any relevant data standards:\n(a) provide for alternative notification schedules (including reducing the\nfrequency of notifications or not receiving notifications); and\n(b) give each joint account holder a means of selecting such an alternative, and\nof changing a selection.\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
