      "cml:premiseText": "(a) in writing; or (b) in an interview with the CDR Accreditor; or (c) by phone, email, videoconferencing or any other form of electronic communication."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-8-ss-2-logic-argumentation-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "May",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Request for further information as a basis for accreditation decision",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "If the accreditation applicant does not provide the further information as requested under this rule, the CDR Accreditor might not be in a position to be satisfied, under section 56CA of the Act, that the applicant meets the criteria for accreditation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 4  CDR Accreditor may consult",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "(1) When making a decision under this Part, the Data Recipient Accreditor may\nconsult with:\n(a) other Commonwealth, State or Territory authorities as relevant, including,\nbut not limited to:\n(i) the Information Commissioner; and\n(ii) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission; and\n(iii) the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority; and\n(iv) the Australian Financial Complaints Authority Limited; and\n(b) similar authorities of foreign jurisdictions; and\n(c) an authority specified for the purposes of this rule in a sector Schedule.\n(2) The functions of the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority include\nproviding the Data Recipient Accreditor with advice or assistance if consulted in\naccordance with this rule.\n(3) The Australian Securities and Investments Commission may disclose\ninformation as reasonably necessary in order to provide the Data Recipient\nAccreditor with advice or assistance if consulted in accordance with this rule.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) When making a decision under this Part, the Data Recipient Accreditor may\nconsult with:\n(a) other Commonwealth, State or Territory authorities as relevant, including,\nbut not limited to:\n(i) the Information Commissioner; and\n(ii) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission; and\n(iii) the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority; and\n(iv) the Australian Financial Complaints Authority Limited; and\n(b) similar authorities of foreign jurisdictions; and\n(c) an authority specified for the purposes of this rule in a sector Schedule.\n(2) The functions of the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority include\nproviding the Data Recipient Accreditor with advice or assistance if consulted in\naccordance with this rule.\n(3) The Australian Securities and Investments Commission may disclose\ninformation as reasonably necessary in order to provide the Data Recipient\nAccreditor with advice or assistance if consulted in accordance with this rule.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-9-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-9-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-9-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "605b7f5812ec69248f24cf13278fe11981920e4a6a1e0c26d1dfe986b52b87f0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 4  CDR Accreditor may consult",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 108,
      "values:originalText": "(1) When making a decision under this Part, the Data Recipient Accreditor may\nconsult with:\n(a) other Commonwealth, State or Territory authorities as relevant, including,\nbut not limited to:\n(i) the Information Commissioner; and\n(ii) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission; and\n(iii) the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority; and\n(iv) the Australian Financial Complaints Authority Limited; and\n(b) similar authorities of foreign jurisdictions; and\n(c) an authority specified for the purposes of this rule in a sector Schedule.\n(2) The functions of the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority include\nproviding the Data Recipient Accreditor with advice or assistance if consulted in\naccordance with this rule.\n(3) The Australian Securities and Investments Commission may disclose\ninformation as reasonably necessary in order to provide the Data Recipient\nAccreditor with advice or assistance if consulted in accordance with this rule."
    },
