    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 7  Accreditation decision—notifying accreditation applicant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR Accreditor must notify an accreditation applicant, in writing, as soon\nas practicable after making a decision to accredit, or refuse to accredit, the\napplicant under subsection56CA(1) of the Act.\n(2) If the Accreditor decided to accredit the applicant, the notice must include the\nfollowing:\n(a) that fact;\n(b) the level of accreditation;\n(c) any conditions that were imposed when the accreditation decision was\nmade;\n(d) their accreditation number.\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to accreditation process  Division 5.2\nSection 5.8\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote:\nFor paragraph (c), for conditions on accreditations, see rule 5.10.\n(3) If the Accreditor decided not to accredit the applicant, the notice must include\nthe following:\n(a) that fact;\n(b) the applicant’s rights to have the decision to refuse reviewed by the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The CDR Accreditor must notify an accreditation applicant, in writing, as soon\nas practicable after making a decision to accredit, or refuse to accredit, the\napplicant under subsection56CA(1) of the Act.\n(2) If the Accreditor decided to accredit the applicant, the notice must include the\nfollowing:\n(a) that fact;\n(b) the level of accreditation;\n(c) any conditions that were imposed when the accreditation decision was\nmade;\n(d) their accreditation number.\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to accreditation process  Division 5.2\nSection 5.8\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote:\nFor paragraph (c), for conditions on accreditations, see rule 5.10.\n(3) If the Accreditor decided not to accredit the applicant, the notice must include\nthe following:\n(a) that fact;\n(b) the applicant’s rights to have the decision to refuse reviewed by the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-13-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-13-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-13-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1006223a97fc1756bf09865abc192cf0da9deb59ffde3f0bf3fbf8a08388187c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 7  Accreditation decision—notifying accreditation applicant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 108,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR Accreditor must notify an accreditation applicant, in writing, as soon\nas practicable after making a decision to accredit, or refuse to accredit, the\napplicant under subsection56CA(1) of the Act.\n(2) If the Accreditor decided to accredit the applicant, the notice must include the\nfollowing:\n(a) that fact;\n(b) the level of accreditation;\n(c) any conditions that were imposed when the accreditation decision was\nmade;\n(d) their accreditation number.\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to accreditation process  Division 5.2\nSection 5.8\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote:\nFor paragraph (c), for conditions on accreditations, see rule 5.10.\n(3) If the Accreditor decided not to accredit the applicant, the notice must include\nthe following:\n(a) that fact;\n(b) the applicant’s rights to have the decision to refuse reviewed by the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal."
    },
