      "skos:note": "Inform and hear accreditation applicant before exercising power",
      "dc:description": "(a) inform, (b) give reasonable opportunity to be heard"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-16-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(2) 10  Other conditions on accreditation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 109,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Before exercising a power under this rule, the Accreditor must:\n(a) inform the accreditation applicant or accredited person, as appropriate, of\nthe proposed imposition or variation; and\n(b) give the accreditation applicant or accredited person, as appropriate, a\nreasonable opportunity to be heard in relation to the proposal.\nNote 1:\nContravention of a condition could lead to suspension or revocation of accreditation:\nsee items 6 and 7 of the table to rule 5.17.\nNote 2:\nApplications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal to review a decision\nunder this rule: see paragraph 9.2(a)."
    },
    {
