    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-16-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5(3) 10  Other conditions on accreditation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-16-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.109",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the reasons for imposing or varying a condition on an existing accreditation are\nsuch that, in the opinion of the CDR Accreditor, complying with subrule (2)\nwould create a real risk of:\n(a) harm or abuse to an individual; or\n(b) adversely impacting the security, integrity or stability of:\n(i) the Register of Accredited Persons; or\n(ii) information and communication technology systems that are used by\nCDR participants to disclose or collect CDR data;\nthe Accreditor may impose or vary the condition without complying with that\nsubrule, but must, as soon as practicable, give the accredited person a reasonable\nopportunity to be heard in relation to the imposition or variation.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If the reasons for imposing or varying a condition on an existing accreditation are\nsuch that, in the opinion of the CDR Accreditor, complying with subrule (2)\nwould create a real risk of:\n(a) harm or abuse to an individual; or\n(b) adversely impacting the security, integrity or stability of:\n(i) the Register of Accredited Persons; or\n(ii) information and communication technology systems that are used by\nCDR participants to disclose or collect CDR data;\nthe Accreditor may impose or vary the condition without complying with that\nsubrule, but must, as soon as practicable, give the accredited person a reasonable\nopportunity to be heard in relation to the imposition or variation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-16"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
