      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "205522551ea6e7272378e9b8dee8284cea2e7da0e9688e6436d3442fcb11ee54",
      "skos:note": "Accreditor may impose or vary condition without complying with subrule (2) if it creates a real risk of harm or abuse to an individual."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-16-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(3) 10  Other conditions on accreditation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 109,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the reasons for imposing or varying a condition on an existing accreditation are\nsuch that, in the opinion of the CDR Accreditor, complying with subrule (2)\nwould create a real risk of:\n(a) harm or abuse to an individual; or\n(b) adversely impacting the security, integrity or stability of:\n(i) the Register of Accredited Persons; or\n(ii) information and communication technology systems that are used by\nCDR participants to disclose or collect CDR data;\nthe Accreditor may impose or vary the condition without complying with that\nsubrule, but must, as soon as practicable, give the accredited person a reasonable\nopportunity to be heard in relation to the imposition or variation."
    },
