    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 11  Notification to accredited person relating to conditions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR Accreditor must notify the accredited person, in writing, as soon as\npracticable after the imposition, variation or removal of a condition on an\naccreditation under rule 5.10.\n(2) The notice must include the following:\n(a) if a condition is imposed or varied:\n(i) the condition or the condition as varied;\n(ii) if applicable—the applicant’s rights to have the decision reviewed by\nthe Administrative Appeals Tribunal; and\n(b) if a condition is removed—that fact.\nSubdivision 5.2.3—Obligations of accredited person",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The CDR Accreditor must notify the accredited person, in writing, as soon as\npracticable after the imposition, variation or removal of a condition on an\naccreditation under rule 5.10.\n(2) The notice must include the following:\n(a) if a condition is imposed or varied:\n(i) the condition or the condition as varied;\n(ii) if applicable—the applicant’s rights to have the decision reviewed by\nthe Administrative Appeals Tribunal; and\n(b) if a condition is removed—that fact.\nSubdivision 5.2.3—Obligations of accredited person",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-17-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1656d2bb586843ee1f7e7a3b7d5587668e7fec951d81bfb814475273fcdc4445"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 11  Notification to accredited person relating to conditions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR Accreditor must notify the accredited person, in writing, as soon as\npracticable after the imposition, variation or removal of a condition on an\naccreditation under rule 5.10.\n(2) The notice must include the following:\n(a) if a condition is imposed or varied:\n(i) the condition or the condition as varied;\n(ii) if applicable—the applicant’s rights to have the decision reviewed by\nthe Administrative Appeals Tribunal; and\n(b) if a condition is removed—that fact.\nSubdivision 5.2.3—Obligations of accredited person"
    },
