    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-23",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 17  Revocation, suspension, or surrender of accreditation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-23"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The table has effect:\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to accreditation process  Division 5.2\nSection 5.17\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nGrounds for revocation, suspension and surrender of accreditation as accredited\nperson\nIf:\nthe CDR Accreditor:\nan accredited person applies to the CDR Accreditor,\nin writing, to surrender their accreditation;\nmust, in writing, accept that\nsurrender.\nthe CDR Accreditor is satisfied that an accredited\nperson’s accreditation was granted as the result of\nstatements or other information, by the accreditation\napplicant or by any other person, that were false or\nmisleading in a material particular;\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe person’s accreditation, as\nappropriate.\nsubject to items 6 and 7, the CDR Accreditor is\nsatisfied that the accredited person or an associated\nperson of the accredited person has been found to\nhave contravened a law relevant to the management\nof CDR data;\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “associated\nperson” and “law relevant to the management of\nCDR data”.\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe accredited person’s\naccreditation, as appropriate.\nthe CDR Accreditor reasonably believes that\nrevocation or suspension is necessary in order to:\n(a) protect consumers; or\n(b) protect the security, integrity and stability of:\n(i) the Register of Accredited Persons or the\nassociated database; or\n(ii) information and communication\ntechnology systems that are used by CDR\nparticipants to disclose or collect CDR\ndata;\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “law relevant to\nthe management of CDR data”.\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe person’s accreditation, as\nappropriate.\nthe following are satisfied:\n(a) the accredited person, at the time of the\naccreditation, satisfied a condition that is\nrelevant to a designated sector and is specified\nfor this item in the sector Schedule;\n(b) the accredited person no longer satisfies the\ncondition;\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe person’s accreditation, as\nappropriate.\nthe CDR Accreditor reasonably believes that the\naccredited person has or may have contravened:\n(a) an offence provision of the Act or a civil penalty\nprovision of the Act or these rules; or\n(b) one or more data standards;\nmay, in writing, suspend the\nperson’s accreditation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The table has effect:\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to accreditation process  Division 5.2\nSection 5.17\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nGrounds for revocation, suspension and surrender of accreditation as accredited\nperson\nIf:\nthe CDR Accreditor:\nan accredited person applies to the CDR Accreditor,\nin writing, to surrender their accreditation;\nmust, in writing, accept that\nsurrender.\nthe CDR Accreditor is satisfied that an accredited\nperson’s accreditation was granted as the result of\nstatements or other information, by the accreditation\napplicant or by any other person, that were false or\nmisleading in a material particular;\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe person’s accreditation, as\nappropriate.\nsubject to items 6 and 7, the CDR Accreditor is\nsatisfied that the accredited person or an associated\nperson of the accredited person has been found to\nhave contravened a law relevant to the management\nof CDR data;\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “associated\nperson” and “law relevant to the management of\nCDR data”.\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe accredited person’s\naccreditation, as appropriate.\nthe CDR Accreditor reasonably believes that\nrevocation or suspension is necessary in order to:\n(a) protect consumers; or\n(b) protect the security, integrity and stability of:\n(i) the Register of Accredited Persons or the\nassociated database; or\n(ii) information and communication\ntechnology systems that are used by CDR\nparticipants to disclose or collect CDR\ndata;\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “law relevant to\nthe management of CDR data”.\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe person’s accreditation, as\nappropriate.\nthe following are satisfied:\n(a) the accredited person, at the time of the\naccreditation, satisfied a condition that is\nrelevant to a designated sector and is specified\nfor this item in the sector Schedule;\n(b) the accredited person no longer satisfies t",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-23-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-23-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d4ef935d3aa4e95619089c4d181ffaafeec1c40f0e97863f4ca7341414caec5f",
      "skos:note": "Revocation, suspension or surrender of accreditation is prohibited without written acceptance."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-23",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 17  Revocation, suspension, or surrender of accreditation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The table has effect:\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to accreditation process  Division 5.2\nSection 5.17\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nGrounds for revocation, suspension and surrender of accreditation as accredited\nperson\nIf:\nthe CDR Accreditor:\nan accredited person applies to the CDR Accreditor,\nin writing, to surrender their accreditation;\nmust, in writing, accept that\nsurrender.\nthe CDR Accreditor is satisfied that an accredited\nperson’s accreditation was granted as the result of\nstatements or other information, by the accreditation\napplicant or by any other person, that were false or\nmisleading in a material particular;\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe person’s accreditation, as\nappropriate.\nsubject to items 6 and 7, the CDR Accreditor is\nsatisfied that the accredited person or an associated\nperson of the accredited person has been found to\nhave contravened a law relevant to the management\nof CDR data;\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “associated\nperson” and “law relevant to the management of\nCDR data”.\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe accredited person’s\naccreditation, as appropriate.\nthe CDR Accreditor reasonably believes that\nrevocation or suspension is necessary in order to:\n(a) protect consumers; or\n(b) protect the security, integrity and stability of:\n(i) the Register of Accredited Persons or the\nassociated database; or\n(ii) information and communication\ntechnology systems that are used by CDR\nparticipants to disclose or collect CDR\ndata;\nNote:\nSee rule 1.7 for the meaning of “law relevant to\nthe management of CDR data”.\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe person’s accreditation, as\nappropriate.\nthe following are satisfied:\n(a) the accredited person, at the time of the\naccreditation, satisfied a condition that is\nrelevant to a designated sector and is specified\nfor this item in the sector Schedule;\n(b) the accredited person no longer satisfies the\ncondition;\nmay, in writing:\n(a) suspend; or\n(b) revoke;\nthe person’s accreditation, as\nappropriate.\nthe CDR Accreditor reasonably believes that the\naccredited person has or may have contravened:\n(a) an offence provision of the Act or a civil penalty\nprovision of the Act or these rules; or\n(b) one or more data standards;\nmay, in writing, suspend the\nperson’s accreditation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-23-norm",
