    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 18  Revocation of accreditation—process",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.115",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before revoking an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17, the CDR\nAccreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person and any associate of:\n(i) the proposed revocation; and\n(ii) when it is proposed to take effect; and\n(b) give the accredited person and any associate a reasonable opportunity to be\nheard in relation to the proposed revocation.\n(2) If the Accreditor revokes an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17,\nthe Accreditor must notify the person and any associate, in writing, of the\nrevocation.\nNote:\nThe decision to revoke an accredited person’s accreditation can be reviewed by the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal: see paragraph 9.2(b).\n(3) For this rule, each of the following is an associate of the accredited person:\n(a) any sponsor;\n(b) any affiliate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before revoking an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17, the CDR\nAccreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person and any associate of:\n(i) the proposed revocation; and\n(ii) when it is proposed to take effect; and\n(b) give the accredited person and any associate a reasonable opportunity to be\nheard in relation to the proposed revocation.\n(2) If the Accreditor revokes an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17,\nthe Accreditor must notify the person and any associate, in writing, of the\nrevocation.\nNote:\nThe decision to revoke an accredited person’s accreditation can be reviewed by the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal: see paragraph 9.2(b).\n(3) For this rule, each of the following is an associate of the accredited person:\n(a) any sponsor;\n(b) any affiliate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-24-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-24-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-24-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e7df7f6ed713f13a0b273ba06481f43166c927257b61559d41ee39346de947e5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 18  Revocation of accreditation—process",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 115,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before revoking an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17, the CDR\nAccreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person and any associate of:\n(i) the proposed revocation; and\n(ii) when it is proposed to take effect; and\n(b) give the accredited person and any associate a reasonable opportunity to be\nheard in relation to the proposed revocation.\n(2) If the Accreditor revokes an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17,\nthe Accreditor must notify the person and any associate, in writing, of the\nrevocation.\nNote:\nThe decision to revoke an accredited person’s accreditation can be reviewed by the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal: see paragraph 9.2(b).\n(3) For this rule, each of the following is an associate of the accredited person:\n(a) any sponsor;\n(b) any affiliate."
    },
    {
