    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-24-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(1) 18  Revocation of accreditation—process",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 115,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before revoking an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17, the CDR\nAccreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person and any associate of:\n(i) the proposed revocation; and\n(ii) when it is proposed to take effect; and\n(b) give the accredited person and any associate a reasonable opportunity to be\nheard in relation to the proposed revocation."
    },
