    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 20  General process for suspension of accreditation or extension of suspension",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.115",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies subject to rule 5.21.\n(2) Before suspending an accreditation under rule 5.17, or extending a suspension,\nthe CDR Accreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person of:\n(i) the proposed suspension or extension (including the proposed\nduration); and\n(ii) in the case of a suspension—when it is proposed to take effect; and\n(b) give the accredited person a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation\nto the proposed suspension or extension.\n(3) If the Accreditor suspends an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17,\nthe Accreditor must notify the person, in writing, of the suspension and the\nperiod of the suspension.\nNote:\nThe decision to suspend an accredited person’s accreditation can be reviewed by the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal: see paragraph 9.2(b).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies subject to rule 5.21.\n(2) Before suspending an accreditation under rule 5.17, or extending a suspension,\nthe CDR Accreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person of:\n(i) the proposed suspension or extension (including the proposed\nduration); and\n(ii) in the case of a suspension—when it is proposed to take effect; and\n(b) give the accredited person a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation\nto the proposed suspension or extension.\n(3) If the Accreditor suspends an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17,\nthe Accreditor must notify the person, in writing, of the suspension and the\nperiod of the suspension.\nNote:\nThe decision to suspend an accredited person’s accreditation can be reviewed by the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal: see paragraph 9.2(b).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-26-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-26-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-26-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5397747b841a63a4c9a300f0bebe47f4c044bcea77b3c19b4d365293c0ffb5f7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 20  General process for suspension of accreditation or extension of suspension",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 115,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies subject to rule 5.21.\n(2) Before suspending an accreditation under rule 5.17, or extending a suspension,\nthe CDR Accreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person of:\n(i) the proposed suspension or extension (including the proposed\nduration); and\n(ii) in the case of a suspension—when it is proposed to take effect; and\n(b) give the accredited person a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation\nto the proposed suspension or extension.\n(3) If the Accreditor suspends an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17,\nthe Accreditor must notify the person, in writing, of the suspension and the\nperiod of the suspension.\nNote:\nThe decision to suspend an accredited person’s accreditation can be reviewed by the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal: see paragraph 9.2(b)."
    },
