      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-26-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-26-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "09e147194a08f0943000c8179d4da191ae1f0a79397cc8dd8c65c190807844b0",
      "skos:note": "Inform accredited person of proposed suspension or extension and give reasonable opportunity to be heard.",
      "dc:description": "Information about proposed suspension or extension"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-26-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(2) 20  General process for suspension of accreditation or extension of suspension",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 115,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Before suspending an accreditation under rule 5.17, or extending a suspension,\nthe CDR Accreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person of:\n(i) the proposed suspension or extension (including the proposed\nduration); and\n(ii) in the case of a suspension—when it is proposed to take effect; and\n(b) give the accredited person a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation\nto the proposed suspension or extension."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-26-ss-2-norm",
