      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-27",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 21  Process for urgent suspensions or extensions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-27"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) the CDR Accreditor proposes to suspend an accreditation, or extend a\nsuspension, on urgent grounds; and\n(b) in the opinion of the CDR Accreditor, because of the urgency, it is not\npossible to comply with rule 5.20 prior to the suspension or extension.\n(2) The Accreditor may suspend the accreditation, or extend the suspension, without\nfirst complying with rule 5.20.\n(3) However, as soon as practicable after suspending the accreditation or extending\nthe suspension, the Accreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person of the suspension or extension; and\n(b) give the accredited person a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation\nto whether the suspension should be removed.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) the CDR Accreditor proposes to suspend an accreditation, or extend a\nsuspension, on urgent grounds; and\n(b) in the opinion of the CDR Accreditor, because of the urgency, it is not\npossible to comply with rule 5.20 prior to the suspension or extension.\n(2) The Accreditor may suspend the accreditation, or extend the suspension, without\nfirst complying with rule 5.20.\n(3) However, as soon as practicable after suspending the accreditation or extending\nthe suspension, the Accreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person of the suspension or extension; and\n(b) give the accredited person a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation\nto whether the suspension should be removed.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-27-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-27-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-27-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b87541e80e0d9e82ffad803bac4034cf6e17c7168bd5fb1dc66be44f12f80f40"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-27",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 21  Process for urgent suspensions or extensions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This rule applies if:\n(a) the CDR Accreditor proposes to suspend an accreditation, or extend a\nsuspension, on urgent grounds; and\n(b) in the opinion of the CDR Accreditor, because of the urgency, it is not\npossible to comply with rule 5.20 prior to the suspension or extension.\n(2) The Accreditor may suspend the accreditation, or extend the suspension, without\nfirst complying with rule 5.20.\n(3) However, as soon as practicable after suspending the accreditation or extending\nthe suspension, the Accreditor must:\n(a) inform the accredited person of the suspension or extension; and\n(b) give the accredited person a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation\nto whether the suspension should be removed."
    },
