      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The person:\n(a) must not, after the revocation or surrender, or while the accreditation is\nsuspended, seek to collect any, or any further, CDR data under these rules;\nand\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to accreditation process  Division 5.2\nSection 5.23\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(b) if the person has collected any CDR data under these rules—must notify\neach person who has consented to the accredited person collecting CDR\ndata for which they are a CDR consumer:\n(i) that their accreditation has been surrendered, suspended or revoked, as\nthe case may be; and\n(ii) in the case of a suspension—of the following:\n(A) that any consents to collect and to use CDR data may be\nwithdrawn at any time; and\n(B) the effect of any such withdrawal.\nNote 1:\nIf an accredited person’s accreditation is suspended, they remain an accredited person,\nand continue to be subject to the obligations of an accredited person whose\naccreditation has not been suspended.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The person:\n(a) must not, after the revocation or surrender, or while the accreditation is\nsuspended, seek to collect any, or any further, CDR data under these rules;\nand\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to accreditation process  Division 5.2\nSection 5.23\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(b) if the person has collected any CDR data under these rules—must notify\neach person who has consented to the accredited person collecting CDR\ndata for which they are a CDR consumer:\n(i) that their accreditation has been surrendered, suspended or revoked, as\nthe case may be; and\n(ii) in the case of a suspension—of the following:\n(A) that any consents to collect and to use CDR data may be\nwithdrawn at any time; and\n(B) the effect of any such withdrawal.\nNote 1:\nIf an accredited person’s accreditation is suspended, they remain an accredited person,\nand continue to be subject to the obligations of an accredited person whose\naccreditation has not been suspended.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-29"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-29-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-29-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f43740b298f777d4024d7d41db6b1dd7102a441dce6e433e6c93cbb4f4c56d91",
      "skos:note": "Must not collect CDR data after accreditation revocation or suspension."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-29-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(3) 23  Consequences of surrender, suspension or revocation of accreditation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The person:\n(a) must not, after the revocation or surrender, or while the accreditation is\nsuspended, seek to collect any, or any further, CDR data under these rules;\nand\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to accreditation process  Division 5.2\nSection 5.23\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(b) if the person has collected any CDR data under these rules—must notify\neach person who has consented to the accredited person collecting CDR\ndata for which they are a CDR consumer:\n(i) that their accreditation has been surrendered, suspended or revoked, as\nthe case may be; and\n(ii) in the case of a suspension—of the following:\n(A) that any consents to collect and to use CDR data may be\nwithdrawn at any time; and\n(B) the effect of any such withdrawal.\nNote 1:\nIf an accredited person’s accreditation is suspended, they remain an accredited person,\nand continue to be subject to the obligations of an accredited person whose\naccreditation has not been suspended.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-29-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
