    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-29-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5(4) 23  Consequences of surrender, suspension or revocation of accreditation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-29-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n(a) the person’s accreditation has been surrendered or revoked; and\n(b) the person has collected CDR data under these rules; and\n(c) the person is not required to retain that CDR data by or under an Australian\nlaw or a court/tribunal order; and\n(d) the CDR data does not relate to any current or anticipated:\n(i) legal proceedings; or\n(ii) dispute resolution proceedings;\nto which the person is a party; and\n(e) where there is a CDR consumer for the CDR data, the CDR data does not\nrelate to any current or anticipated:\n(i) legal proceedings; or\n(ii) dispute resolution proceedings;\nto which the CDR consumer is a party;\nthe person must delete or de-identify that data by taking the steps specified in\nrule 7.12 or 7.13, as appropriate.\nNote 1:\nIn addition:\n•\nif an accreditation is revoked or surrendered:\n-\nany consents to collect and use CDR data expire: see subrules 4.14(6) and",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If:\n(a) the person’s accreditation has been surrendered or revoked; and\n(b) the person has collected CDR data under these rules; and\n(c) the person is not required to retain that CDR data by or under an Australian\nlaw or a court/tribunal order; and\n(d) the CDR data does not relate to any current or anticipated:\n(i) legal proceedings; or\n(ii) dispute resolution proceedings;\nto which the person is a party; and\n(e) where there is a CDR consumer for the CDR data, the CDR data does not\nrelate to any current or anticipated:\n(i) legal proceedings; or\n(ii) dispute resolution proceedings;\nto which the CDR consumer is a party;\nthe person must delete or de-identify that data by taking the steps specified in\nrule 7.12 or 7.13, as appropriate.\nNote 1:\nIn addition:\n•\nif an accreditation is revoked or surrendered:\n-\nany consents to collect and use CDR data expire: see subrules 4.14(6) and",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-29"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-29-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-29-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "82a41d1ad27dab7225ab5a536728a5b17db325204e1824c02cbefff149be9bb5",
      "skos:note": "Delete or de-identify CDR data if not required by law or court order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-29-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(4) 23  Consequences of surrender, suspension or revocation of accreditation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n(a) the person’s accreditation has been surrendered or revoked; and\n(b) the person has collected CDR data under these rules; and\n(c) the person is not required to retain that CDR data by or under an Australian\nlaw or a court/tribunal order; and\n(d) the CDR data does not relate to any current or anticipated:\n(i) legal proceedings; or\n(ii) dispute resolution proceedings;\nto which the person is a party; and\n(e) where there is a CDR consumer for the CDR data, the CDR data does not\nrelate to any current or anticipated:\n(i) legal proceedings; or\n(ii) dispute resolution proceedings;\nto which the CDR consumer is a party;\nthe person must delete or de-identify that data by taking the steps specified in\nrule 7.12 or 7.13, as appropriate.\nNote 1:\nIn addition:\n•\nif an accreditation is revoked or surrendered:\n-\nany consents to collect and use CDR data expire: see subrules 4.14(6) and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-29-ss-4-norm",
