    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-30",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 24  Maintaining the Register of Accredited Persons",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-30"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "The Accreditation Registrar must enter the following details on the Register of\nAccredited Persons:\n(a) the following details about the accredited person:\n(i) the accredited person’s name;\n(ii) the accredited person’s accreditation number;\n(iii) the accredited person’s addresses for service;\n(iv) if the accredited person is a foreign entity—the name and addresses\nfor service of the accredited person’s local agent;\n(b) the level of the person’s accreditation;\n(ba) for a person with sponsored accreditation—any sponsor;\n(bb) for a sponsor—each affiliate;\n(bc) the name, ABN and business address of any CDR representative;\n(c) either:\n(i) any conditions on the accreditation; or\n(ii) if the CDR Accreditor so directs—a description of the effect of any\nsuch conditions;\n(d) if the accreditation has been revoked—that fact and the date of the\nrevocation;\n(e) if the accreditation has been suspended—that fact and the period of the\nsuspension;\n(f) if a decision to suspend an accreditation has been revoked, or the\nsuspension otherwise is no longer in effect:\n(i) that fact; and\n(ii) the date from which the accreditation is once more in effect;\n(g) if the accreditation is surrendered—that fact and the date of the surrender;\n(h) each brand name under which the accredited person provides goods or\nservices where, in order to provide the good or service, the accredited\nperson needs to access a CDR consumer’s CDR data;\n(i) a hyperlink to each of the following:\n(i) the relevant web site address of the accredited person;\n(ii) the accredited person’s CDR policy;\n(iii) if the accredited person has a CDR policy for a brand name under\nwhich the accredited person provides goods or services where, in\norder to provide the good or service, the accredited person needs to\naccess a CDR consumer’s CDR data―that policy.\nNote 1:\nFor paragraphs (a), see rule 1.7 for the meaning of “addresses for service”.\nNote 3:\nFor paragraphs (a) to (g), see rule 5.15.",
      "skos:definition": "The Accreditation Registrar must enter the following details on the Register of\nAccredited Persons:\n(a) the following details about the accredited person:\n(i) the accredited person’s name;\n(ii) the accredited person’s accreditation number;\n(iii) the accredited person’s addresses for service;\n(iv) if the accredited person is a foreign entity—the name and addresses\nfor service of the accredited person’s local agent;\n(b) the level of the person’s accreditation;\n(ba) for a person with sponsored accreditation—any sponsor;\n(bb) for a sponsor—each affiliate;\n(bc) the name, ABN and business address of any CDR representative;\n(c) either:\n(i) any conditions on the accreditation; or\n(ii) if the CDR Accreditor so directs—a description of the effect of any\nsuch conditions;\n(d) if the accreditation has been revoked—that fact and the date of the\nrevocation;\n(e) if the accreditation has been suspended—that fact and the period of the\nsuspension;\n(f) if a decision to suspend an accreditation has been revoked, or the\nsuspension otherwise is no longer in effect:\n(i) that fact; and\n(ii) the date from which the accreditation is once more in effect;\n(g) if the accreditation is surrendered—that fact and the date of the surrender;\n(h) each brand name under which the accredited person provides goods or\nservices where, in order to provide the good or service, the accredited\nperson needs to access a CDR consumer’s CDR data;\n(i) a hyperlink to each of the following:\n(i) the relevant web site address of the accredited person;\n(ii) the accredited person’s CDR policy;\n(iii) if the accredited person has a CDR policy for a brand name under\nwhich the accredited person provides goods or services where, in\norder to provide the good or service, the accredited person needs to\naccess a CDR consumer’s CDR data―that policy.\nNote 1:\nFor paragraphs (a), see rule 1.7 for the meaning of “addresses for service”.\nNote 3:\nFor paragraphs (a) to (g), see rule 5.15.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-30-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-30-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "775a534f4cc3a316b8b8e88e1f801f30acc90d72056b035fd2b4f0c402bea89e",
      "skos:note": "The Accreditation Registrar must enter specific details on the Register of Accredited Persons.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-30",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 24  Maintaining the Register of Accredited Persons",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "The Accreditation Registrar must enter the following details on the Register of\nAccredited Persons:\n(a) the following details about the accredited person:\n(i) the accredited person’s name;\n(ii) the accredited person’s accreditation number;\n(iii) the accredited person’s addresses for service;\n(iv) if the accredited person is a foreign entity—the name and addresses\nfor service of the accredited person’s local agent;\n(b) the level of the person’s accreditation;\n(ba) for a person with sponsored accreditation—any sponsor;\n(bb) for a sponsor—each affiliate;\n(bc) the name, ABN and business address of any CDR representative;\n(c) either:\n(i) any conditions on the accreditation; or\n(ii) if the CDR Accreditor so directs—a description of the effect of any\nsuch conditions;\n(d) if the accreditation has been revoked—that fact and the date of the\nrevocation;\n(e) if the accreditation has been suspended—that fact and the period of the\nsuspension;\n(f) if a decision to suspend an accreditation has been revoked, or the\nsuspension otherwise is no longer in effect:\n(i) that fact; and\n(ii) the date from which the accreditation is once more in effect;\n(g) if the accreditation is surrendered—that fact and the date of the surrender;\n(h) each brand name under which the accredited person provides goods or\nservices where, in order to provide the good or service, the accredited\nperson needs to access a CDR consumer’s CDR data;\n(i) a hyperlink to each of the following:\n(i) the relevant web site address of the accredited person;\n(ii) the accredited person’s CDR policy;\n(iii) if the accredited person has a CDR policy for a brand name under\nwhich the accredited person provides goods or services where, in\norder to provide the good or service, the accredited person needs to\naccess a CDR consumer’s CDR data―that policy.\nNote 1:\nFor paragraphs (a), see rule 1.7 for the meaning of “addresses for service”.\nNote 3:\nFor paragraphs (a) to (g), see rule 5.15."
    },
    {
