      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-36",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 30  Other functions of Accreditation Registrar",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-36"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.120",
      "values:originalText": "For paragraph 56CL(1)(b) of the Act, the other functions of the Accreditation\nRegistrar include the following:\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to Register of Accredited Persons  Division 5.3\nSection 5.31\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) enabling information included in the Register of Accredited Persons and\nassociated database to be communicated to data holders and accredited\npersons to facilitate the making and processing of requests under these\nrules in accordance with these rules and the data standards;\n(b) maintaining the security, integrity and stability of the Register and\nassociated database, including undertaking or facilitating any testing by\nCDR participants for that purpose;\n(c) requesting a data holder or an accredited person to do specified things\nwhere that is necessary or convenient in order for the Accreditation\nRegistrar to perform its functions or exercise its powers;\nExample:\nThe Accreditation Registrar could request data holders or accredited persons to\nundertake and complete testing where it is necessary or convenient for the Registrar to\nperform its functions under paragraph (b).\n(d) informing the CDR Accreditor of any failure of an accredited person to\ncomply with a condition of its accreditation or to do things requested by the\nRegistrar in the performance of its functions or the exercise of its powers.\nNote:\nThe Accreditation Registrar has the power to do all things necessary or convenient to\nbe done for or in connection with the performance of its functions. See subsection\n56CL(2) of the Act.",
      "skos:definition": "For paragraph 56CL(1)(b) of the Act, the other functions of the Accreditation\nRegistrar include the following:\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to Register of Accredited Persons  Division 5.3\nSection 5.31\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) enabling information included in the Register of Accredited Persons and\nassociated database to be communicated to data holders and accredited\npersons to facilitate the making and processing of requests under these\nrules in accordance with these rules and the data standards;\n(b) maintaining the security, integrity and stability of the Register and\nassociated database, including undertaking or facilitating any testing by\nCDR participants for that purpose;\n(c) requesting a data holder or an accredited person to do specified things\nwhere that is necessary or convenient in order for the Accreditation\nRegistrar to perform its functions or exercise its powers;\nExample:\nThe Accreditation Registrar could request data holders or accredited persons to\nundertake and complete testing where it is necessary or convenient for the Registrar to\nperform its functions under paragraph (b).\n(d) informing the CDR Accreditor of any failure of an accredited person to\ncomply with a condition of its accreditation or to do things requested by the\nRegistrar in the performance of its functions or the exercise of its powers.\nNote:\nThe Accreditation Registrar has the power to do all things necessary or convenient to\nbe done for or in connection with the performance of its functions. See subsection\n56CL(2) of the Act.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-36-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-36-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-36-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b632fcbeba453245e5e31210249ff52183ae3d0df7f8227cd070892857d4d240",
      "skos:note": "The Accreditation Registrar must inform the CDR Accreditor of any failure of an accredited person to comply with a condition of its accreditation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-36",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 30  Other functions of Accreditation Registrar",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 120,
      "values:originalText": "For paragraph 56CL(1)(b) of the Act, the other functions of the Accreditation\nRegistrar include the following:\n\n\nRules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5\nRules relating to Register of Accredited Persons  Division 5.3\nSection 5.31\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(a) enabling information included in the Register of Accredited Persons and\nassociated database to be communicated to data holders and accredited\npersons to facilitate the making and processing of requests under these\nrules in accordance with these rules and the data standards;\n(b) maintaining the security, integrity and stability of the Register and\nassociated database, including undertaking or facilitating any testing by\nCDR participants for that purpose;\n(c) requesting a data holder or an accredited person to do specified things\nwhere that is necessary or convenient in order for the Accreditation\nRegistrar to perform its functions or exercise its powers;\nExample:\nThe Accreditation Registrar could request data holders or accredited persons to\nundertake and complete testing where it is necessary or convenient for the Registrar to\nperform its functions under paragraph (b).\n(d) informing the CDR Accreditor of any failure of an accredited person to\ncomply with a condition of its accreditation or to do things requested by the\nRegistrar in the performance of its functions or the exercise of its powers.\nNote:\nThe Accreditation Registrar has the power to do all things necessary or convenient to\nbe done for or in connection with the performance of its functions. See subsection\n56CL(2) of the Act."
    },
