    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-39",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Section 5",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-39"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.121",
      "values:originalText": "33  Temporary restriction on use of the Register in relation to data holder\n(1) The Accreditation Registrar may take steps to prevent the Register of Accredited\nPersons and associated database from being used to make consumer data requests\nto a data holder, for a period of up to 10 days, if the Accreditation Registrar\nreasonably believes it is necessary to do so in order to ensure the security,\nintegrity and stability of the Register or associated database.\n(2) The steps taken by the Accreditation Registrar may include amending the\ninformation in the associated database relating to a data holder that is used to\nfacilitate the making and processing of requests.\n(3) Before, or as soon as practicable after, taking steps under subrule (1), the\nAccreditation Registrar must:\n(a) inform the data holder of the steps to be taken, or that have been taken; and\n(b) give the data holder a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation to the\nmatter.",
      "skos:definition": "33  Temporary restriction on use of the Register in relation to data holder\n(1) The Accreditation Registrar may take steps to prevent the Register of Accredited\nPersons and associated database from being used to make consumer data requests\nto a data holder, for a period of up to 10 days, if the Accreditation Registrar\nreasonably believes it is necessary to do so in order to ensure the security,\nintegrity and stability of the Register or associated database.\n(2) The steps taken by the Accreditation Registrar may include amending the\ninformation in the associated database relating to a data holder that is used to\nfacilitate the making and processing of requests.\n(3) Before, or as soon as practicable after, taking steps under subrule (1), the\nAccreditation Registrar must:\n(a) inform the data holder of the steps to be taken, or that have been taken; and\n(b) give the data holder a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation to the\nmatter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-39-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-39-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-39-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ec674b432d2b17fa72cf722d7ad7fa58c92f96c1c5397b491bb70697a302f2b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-39",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Section 5",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 121,
      "values:originalText": "33  Temporary restriction on use of the Register in relation to data holder\n(1) The Accreditation Registrar may take steps to prevent the Register of Accredited\nPersons and associated database from being used to make consumer data requests\nto a data holder, for a period of up to 10 days, if the Accreditation Registrar\nreasonably believes it is necessary to do so in order to ensure the security,\nintegrity and stability of the Register or associated database.\n(2) The steps taken by the Accreditation Registrar may include amending the\ninformation in the associated database relating to a data holder that is used to\nfacilitate the making and processing of requests.\n(3) Before, or as soon as practicable after, taking steps under subrule (1), the\nAccreditation Registrar must:\n(a) inform the data holder of the steps to be taken, or that have been taken; and\n(b) give the data holder a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation to the\nmatter."
    },
