    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-40-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5(4) 34  Temporary direction to refrain from processing consumer data requests",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-40-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.122",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite anything else in these rules:\n(a) an accredited person must not make a consumer data request contrary to a\ndirection it has received under this rule; and\n(b) a data holder must not disclose CDR data in response to a consumer data\nrequest contrary to a direction it has received under this rule.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n\n\nRules relating to dispute resolution  Part 6\nRules relating to Register of Accredited Persons  Division 5.3\nSection 6.1\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Despite anything else in these rules:\n(a) an accredited person must not make a consumer data request contrary to a\ndirection it has received under this rule; and\n(b) a data holder must not disclose CDR data in response to a consumer data\nrequest contrary to a direction it has received under this rule.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n\n\nRules relating to dispute resolution  Part 6\nRules relating to Register of Accredited Persons  Division 5.3\nSection 6.1\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-40"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-40-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-40-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-40-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-40-ss-4-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "680287892b2cf5d35d75110302716cb75f355167d9e6f15c7281f57a2ef3aa00",
      "skos:note": "Accredited person must not make consumer data request contrary to direction received under this rule."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-40-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(4) 34  Temporary direction to refrain from processing consumer data requests",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 122,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite anything else in these rules:\n(a) an accredited person must not make a consumer data request contrary to a\ndirection it has received under this rule; and\n(b) a data holder must not disclose CDR data in response to a consumer data\nrequest contrary to a direction it has received under this rule.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n\n\nRules relating to dispute resolution  Part 6\nRules relating to Register of Accredited Persons  Division 5.3\nSection 6.1\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020"
    },
    {
