    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 1  Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.124",
      "values:originalText": "The privacy safeguards are an additional protection given to CDR data under\nPart IVD of the Act. The privacy safeguards apply only to CDR data for which\nthere are one or more CDR consumers (such as required consumer data and\nvoluntary consumer data); they do not apply to CDR data for which there are no\nCDR consumers (such as required product data and voluntary product data).\nSeveral of the privacy safeguards depend on matters specified in these rules for\ntheir operation. This Part sets out the rules that relate to the privacy safeguards.\nThis Part also sets out some additional civil penalty provisions that protect the\nprivacy or confidentiality of CDR consumers’ CDR data.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "skos:definition": "The privacy safeguards are an additional protection given to CDR data under\nPart IVD of the Act. The privacy safeguards apply only to CDR data for which\nthere are one or more CDR consumers (such as required consumer data and\nvoluntary consumer data); they do not apply to CDR data for which there are no\nCDR consumers (such as required product data and voluntary product data).\nSeveral of the privacy safeguards depend on matters specified in these rules for\ntheir operation. This Part sets out the rules that relate to the privacy safeguards.\nThis Part also sets out some additional civil penalty provisions that protect the\nprivacy or confidentiality of CDR consumers’ CDR data.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "58f21a5870bb1e53c4da6ad4f1ba44b06a430ed903446ec08cfd651605c00574",
      "skos:note": "Privacy safeguards apply to CDR data for which there are one or more CDR consumers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 1  Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 124,
      "values:originalText": "The privacy safeguards are an additional protection given to CDR data under\nPart IVD of the Act. The privacy safeguards apply only to CDR data for which\nthere are one or more CDR consumers (such as required consumer data and\nvoluntary consumer data); they do not apply to CDR data for which there are no\nCDR consumers (such as required product data and voluntary product data).\nSeveral of the privacy safeguards depend on matters specified in these rules for\ntheir operation. This Part sets out the rules that relate to the privacy safeguards.\nThis Part also sets out some additional civil penalty provisions that protect the\nprivacy or confidentiality of CDR consumers’ CDR data.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "holds",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Holds true for CDR data with one or more consumers.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "There are one or more CDR consumers.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Privacy safeguards apply."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 2  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 1—open and transparent management of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "CDR data\nPolicy about the management of CDR data\n(1) For paragraph 56ED(3)(b) of the Act, the Information Commissioner may\napprove a form for a CDR policy.\n(2) For paragraph 56ED(3)(b) of the Act, the CDR entity’s CDR policy must be in\nthe form of a document that is distinct from any of the CDR entity’s privacy\npolicies.\nAdditional information for CDR policy\n(3) In addition to the information referred to in subsection 56ED(4) of the Act, the\ndata holder’s CDR policy must indicate:\n(a) whether it accepts requests for:\n(i) voluntary product data; or\n(ii) voluntary consumer data; and\n(b) if so:\n(i) whether it charges fees for disclosure of such data; and\n(ii) if it does―how information about those fees can be obtained.\n(4) In addition to the information referred to in subsection 56ED(5) of the Act, the\nCDR policy of an accredited person who is or who may become an accredited\ndata recipient of CDR data must include the following:\n(a) a statement indicating the consequences to the CDR consumer if they\nwithdraw a consent to collect and use CDR data;\n(b) a list of any other accredited persons with whom the accredited person has\na sponsorship arrangement;\n(c) for each such arrangement—the nature of the services one party provides to\nthe other party;\n(d) a list of the CDR representatives of the accredited person;\n(e) for each CDR representative—the nature of the goods and services that the\nCDR representative provides to customers using CDR data;\n(f) a list of the direct and indirect OSPs of the accredited person and of any\nCDR representative (whether based in Australia or based overseas, and\nwhether or not any is an accredited person);\n(g) for each such service provider:\n(i) the nature of the services it provides;\n(ii) the CDR data or classes of CDR data that may be disclosed to it or\ncollected by it;\n(h) if the accredited person wishes to undertake general research using the\nCDR data:\n(i) a description of the research to be conducted;",
      "skos:definition": "CDR data\nPolicy about the management of CDR data\n(1) For paragraph 56ED(3)(b) of the Act, the Information Commissioner may\napprove a form for a CDR policy.\n(2) For paragraph 56ED(3)(b) of the Act, the CDR entity’s CDR policy must be in\nthe form of a document that is distinct from any of the CDR entity’s privacy\npolicies.\nAdditional information for CDR policy\n(3) In addition to the information referred to in subsection 56ED(4) of the Act, the\ndata holder’s CDR policy must indicate:\n(a) whether it accepts requests for:\n(i) voluntary product data; or\n(ii) voluntary consumer data; and\n(b) if so:\n(i) whether it charges fees for disclosure of such data; and\n(ii) if it does―how information about those fees can be obtained.\n(4) In addition to the information referred to in subsection 56ED(5) of the Act, the\nCDR policy of an accredited person who is or who may become an accredited\ndata recipient of CDR data must include the following:\n(a) a statement indicating the consequences to the CDR consumer if they\nwithdraw a consent to collect and use CDR data;\n(b) a list of any other accredited persons with whom the accredited person has\na sponsorship arrangement;\n(c) for each such arrangement—the nature of the services one party provides to\nthe other party;\n(d) a list of the CDR representatives of the accredited person;\n(e) for each CDR representative—the nature of the goods and services that the\nCDR representative provides to customers using CDR data;\n(f) a list of the direct and indirect OSPs of the accredited person and of any\nCDR representative (whether based in Australia or based overseas, and\nwhether or not any is an accredited person);\n(g) for each such service provider:\n(i) the nature of the services it provides;\n(ii) the CDR data or classes of CDR data that may be disclosed to it or\ncollected by it;\n(h) if the accredited person wishes to undertake general research using the\nCDR data:\n(i) a description of the research to be conducted;",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-3-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-3-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-3-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-3-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9158e6e0b1c121df60564e670d83ee868f3863981c4a87c5e6f68a2c4a28b0c8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 2  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 1—open and transparent management of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "CDR data\nPolicy about the management of CDR data\n(1) For paragraph 56ED(3)(b) of the Act, the Information Commissioner may\napprove a form for a CDR policy.\n(2) For paragraph 56ED(3)(b) of the Act, the CDR entity’s CDR policy must be in\nthe form of a document that is distinct from any of the CDR entity’s privacy\npolicies.\nAdditional information for CDR policy\n(3) In addition to the information referred to in subsection 56ED(4) of the Act, the\ndata holder’s CDR policy must indicate:\n(a) whether it accepts requests for:\n(i) voluntary product data; or\n(ii) voluntary consumer data; and\n(b) if so:\n(i) whether it charges fees for disclosure of such data; and\n(ii) if it does―how information about those fees can be obtained.\n(4) In addition to the information referred to in subsection 56ED(5) of the Act, the\nCDR policy of an accredited person who is or who may become an accredited\ndata recipient of CDR data must include the following:\n(a) a statement indicating the consequences to the CDR consumer if they\nwithdraw a consent to collect and use CDR data;\n(b) a list of any other accredited persons with whom the accredited person has\na sponsorship arrangement;\n(c) for each such arrangement—the nature of the services one party provides to\nthe other party;\n(d) a list of the CDR representatives of the accredited person;\n(e) for each CDR representative—the nature of the goods and services that the\nCDR representative provides to customers using CDR data;\n(f) a list of the direct and indirect OSPs of the accredited person and of any\nCDR representative (whether based in Australia or based overseas, and\nwhether or not any is an accredited person);\n(g) for each such service provider:\n(i) the nature of the services it provides;\n(ii) the CDR data or classes of CDR data that may be disclosed to it or\ncollected by it;\n(h) if the accredited person wishes to undertake general research using the\nCDR data:\n(i) a description of the research to be conducted;"
    },
