    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 3  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 2—anonymity and pseudonymity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.127",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For subsection 56EE(3) of the Act, subsection 56EE(1) of the Act does not apply\nif:\n(a) the accredited person who is or may become an accredited data recipient of\nCDR data is required or authorised by law or by a court/tribunal order to\ndeal with an identified CDR consumer in relation to particular CDR data;\nor\n(b) in relation to particular CDR data, it is impracticable for the accredited data\nrecipient to deal with a CDR consumer that has not been identified.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For subsection 56EE(3) of the Act, subsection 56EE(1) of the Act does not apply\nif:\n(a) the accredited person who is or may become an accredited data recipient of\nCDR data is required or authorised by law or by a court/tribunal order to\ndeal with an identified CDR consumer in relation to particular CDR data;\nor\n(b) in relation to particular CDR data, it is impracticable for the accredited data\nrecipient to deal with a CDR consumer that has not been identified.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-4-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-4-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-4-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4ed67adc0f5f365efaaf669c394c98b21252fdaa749c0e9e7c57ad88a5928e36",
      "skos:note": "Exemption from subsection 56EE(1) of the Act for accredited data recipients dealing with identified CDR consumers under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 3  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 2—anonymity and pseudonymity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 127,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For subsection 56EE(3) of the Act, subsection 56EE(1) of the Act does not apply\nif:\n(a) the accredited person who is or may become an accredited data recipient of\nCDR data is required or authorised by law or by a court/tribunal order to\ndeal with an identified CDR consumer in relation to particular CDR data;\nor\n(b) in relation to particular CDR data, it is impracticable for the accredited data\nrecipient to deal with a CDR consumer that has not been identified."
    },
