    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 3A  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 4—destruction of unsolicited data—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "CDR representative\n(1) A CDR representative principal breaches this subrule if its CDR representative\nfails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR\nconsumer as if;\n(a) it were an accredited person; and\n(b) it had collected the service data.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) For subrule (1), it is irrelevant whether the action of the CDR representative in\nrelation to the service data is in accordance with the CDR representative\narrangement.",
      "skos:definition": "CDR representative\n(1) A CDR representative principal breaches this subrule if its CDR representative\nfails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR\nconsumer as if;\n(a) it were an accredited person; and\n(b) it had collected the service data.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) For subrule (1), it is irrelevant whether the action of the CDR representative in\nrelation to the service data is in accordance with the CDR representative\narrangement.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-5-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1272c36667a3a4ad4a75767cf79b185d5f7154c394f04b5e31021c7b3f05083e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 3A  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 4—destruction of unsolicited data—",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 128,
      "values:originalText": "CDR representative\n(1) A CDR representative principal breaches this subrule if its CDR representative\nfails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR\nconsumer as if;\n(a) it were an accredited person; and\n(b) it had collected the service data.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) For subrule (1), it is irrelevant whether the action of the CDR representative in\nrelation to the service data is in accordance with the CDR representative\narrangement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-5-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7(1) 3A  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 4—destruction of unsolicited data—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-5-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR representative principal breaches this subrule if its CDR representative\nfails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR\nconsumer as if;\n(a) it were an accredited person; and\n(b) it had collected the service data.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A CDR representative principal breaches this subrule if its CDR representative\nfails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR\nconsumer as if;\n(a) it were an accredited person; and\n(b) it had collected the service data.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
