    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 3B  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 4—destruction of unsolicited data—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "outsourced service providers\n(1) An accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct or indirect OSP of:\n(a) the accredited person; or\n(b) a CDR representative of the accredited person;\nfails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR\nconsumer as if:\n(c) it were an accredited person; and\n(d) it had collected the service data.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10 for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR outsourcing\narrangement.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) For subrule (1), it is irrelevant whether the action of the direct or indirect OSP in\nrelation to the service data is in accordance with the CDR outsourcing\narrangement.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.4\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nSubdivision 7.2.2—Rules relating to collecting CDR data",
      "skos:definition": "outsourced service providers\n(1) An accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct or indirect OSP of:\n(a) the accredited person; or\n(b) a CDR representative of the accredited person;\nfails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR\nconsumer as if:\n(c) it were an accredited person; and\n(d) it had collected the service data.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10 for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR outsourcing\narrangement.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) For subrule (1), it is irrelevant whether the action of the direct or indirect OSP in\nrelation to the service data is in accordance with the CDR outsourcing\narrangement.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.4\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nSubdivision 7.2.2—Rules relating to collecting CDR data",
      "cml:hasPart": [
