    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 5  Meaning of permitted use or disclosure and relates to direct marketing",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "Permitted uses or disclosures that do not relate to direct marketing\n(1) For these rules, for an accredited data recipient that has collected CDR data\nunder a consumer data request under Part 4 on behalf of a CDR consumer, each\nof the following is a permitted use or disclosure:\n(a) using the CDR consumer’s CDR data to provide goods or services\nrequested by the CDR consumer (the existing goods or services):\n(i) in compliance with the data minimisation principle; and\n(ii) in accordance with a current use consent from the CDR consumer,\nother than a direct marketing consent;\n(b) in accordance with a current de-identification consent, de-identifying the\nCDR consumer’s CDR data in accordance with the CDR data\nde-identification process and:\n(i) using the de-identified data for general research; or\n(ii) disclosing (including by selling) the de-identified data;\n(c) directly or indirectly deriving CDR data from the collected CDR data in\norder to use the data in accordance with paragraph (a) or (b);\n(d) for the purpose of providing the existing goods or services—disclosing, to\nthe CDR consumer, any of their CDR data;",
      "skos:definition": "Permitted uses or disclosures that do not relate to direct marketing\n(1) For these rules, for an accredited data recipient that has collected CDR data\nunder a consumer data request under Part 4 on behalf of a CDR consumer, each\nof the following is a permitted use or disclosure:\n(a) using the CDR consumer’s CDR data to provide goods or services\nrequested by the CDR consumer (the existing goods or services):\n(i) in compliance with the data minimisation principle; and\n(ii) in accordance with a current use consent from the CDR consumer,\nother than a direct marketing consent;\n(b) in accordance with a current de-identification consent, de-identifying the\nCDR consumer’s CDR data in accordance with the CDR data\nde-identification process and:\n(i) using the de-identified data for general research; or\n(ii) disclosing (including by selling) the de-identified data;\n(c) directly or indirectly deriving CDR data from the collected CDR data in\norder to use the data in accordance with paragraph (a) or (b);\n(d) for the purpose of providing the existing goods or services—disclosing, to\nthe CDR consumer, any of their CDR data;",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ef053cb560276905a8831dc16af1a32470ebc3d65d4966edc0cd77f1ae9e941",
      "skos:note": "Permitted uses or disclosures of CDR data not related to direct marketing"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 5  Meaning of permitted use or disclosure and relates to direct marketing",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "Permitted uses or disclosures that do not relate to direct marketing\n(1) For these rules, for an accredited data recipient that has collected CDR data\nunder a consumer data request under Part 4 on behalf of a CDR consumer, each\nof the following is a permitted use or disclosure:\n(a) using the CDR consumer’s CDR data to provide goods or services\nrequested by the CDR consumer (the existing goods or services):\n(i) in compliance with the data minimisation principle; and\n(ii) in accordance with a current use consent from the CDR consumer,\nother than a direct marketing consent;\n(b) in accordance with a current de-identification consent, de-identifying the\nCDR consumer’s CDR data in accordance with the CDR data\nde-identification process and:\n(i) using the de-identified data for general research; or\n(ii) disclosing (including by selling) the de-identified data;\n(c) directly or indirectly deriving CDR data from the collected CDR data in\norder to use the data in accordance with paragraph (a) or (b);\n(d) for the purpose of providing the existing goods or services—disclosing, to\nthe CDR consumer, any of their CDR data;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-8-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-8"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-8-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permits",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Allows permitted uses or disclosures",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 5A  Limitation to disclosures of CDR data under a disclosure consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.131",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite paragraph 7.5(1)(e), disclosure of CDR data to an accredited person\nunder an AP disclosure consent is not a permitted use or disclosure until the\nearlier of the following:\n(a) 1 July 2021;\n(b) the day the Data Standards Chair makes the data standard about the matter\nreferred to in subparagraph 8.11(1)(c)(iii).\n(2) Despite paragraph 7.5(1)(e), disclosure of CDR data to a trusted adviser under a\nTA disclosure consent is not a permitted use or disclosure until the earlier of the\nfollowing:\n(a) 1 February 2022;\n(b) the day the Data Standards Chair makes the data standard about the matter\nreferred to in subparagraph 8.11(1)(c)(iv).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Despite paragraph 7.5(1)(e), disclosure of CDR data to an accredited person\nunder an AP disclosure consent is not a permitted use or disclosure until the\nearlier of the following:\n(a) 1 July 2021;\n(b) the day the Data Standards Chair makes the data standard about the matter\nreferred to in subparagraph 8.11(1)(c)(iii).\n(2) Despite paragraph 7.5(1)(e), disclosure of CDR data to a trusted adviser under a\nTA disclosure consent is not a permitted use or disclosure until the earlier of the\nfollowing:\n(a) 1 February 2022;\n(b) the day the Data Standards Chair makes the data standard about the matter\nreferred to in subparagraph 8.11(1)(c)(iv).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-9-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-9-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "040088709f87bb91d7803970bde13e4bcd4855e8c7b193da8fb111352e4f7a3a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 5A  Limitation to disclosures of CDR data under a disclosure consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 131,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite paragraph 7.5(1)(e), disclosure of CDR data to an accredited person\nunder an AP disclosure consent is not a permitted use or disclosure until the\nearlier of the following:\n(a) 1 July 2021;\n(b) the day the Data Standards Chair makes the data standard about the matter\nreferred to in subparagraph 8.11(1)(c)(iii).\n(2) Despite paragraph 7.5(1)(e), disclosure of CDR data to a trusted adviser under a\nTA disclosure consent is not a permitted use or disclosure until the earlier of the\nfollowing:\n(a) 1 February 2022;\n(b) the day the Data Standards Chair makes the data standard about the matter\nreferred to in subparagraph 8.11(1)(c)(iv)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-9-ss-1",
