    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Section 7",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "6  Use or disclosure of CDR data by accredited data recipients and related\npersons\n(1) Subject to the Act and these rules, an accredited data recipient that has collected\nCDR data under a consumer data request under Part 4 made on behalf of a CDR\nconsumer must not use or disclose it, or CDR data directly or indirectly derived\nfrom it, other than for a permitted use or disclosure (whether or not one that\nrelates to direct marketing).\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) For this rule:\n(a) any use or disclosure of service data by a direct or indirect OSP of:\n(i) an accredited data recipient; or\n(ii) a CDR representative of the accredited data recipient;\nis taken to have been by the accredited data recipient; and\n(b) it is irrelevant whether the use or disclosure is in accordance with the\nrelevant CDR outsourcing arrangement.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a direct or indirect\nOSP.\n(3) For this rule, any CDR data collected by an accredited person at the request of an\naffiliate is taken also to have been collected by the affiliate.\n(4) For this rule:\n(a) any use or disclosure of service data by a CDR representative is taken to\nhave been by the CDR representative principal; and\n(b) it is irrelevant whether the use or disclosure is in accordance with the CDR\nrepresentative arrangement.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.7\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\n(5) For this rule:\n(a) any collection of service data by a direct or indirect OSP of an accredited\nperson is taken to have been by the accredited person; and\n(b) it is irrelevant whether the collection is in accordance with the relevant\nCDR outsourcing arrangement.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR outsourcing\narrangement.",
      "skos:definition": "6  Use or disclosure of CDR data by accredited data recipients and related\npersons\n(1) Subject to the Act and these rules, an accredited data recipient that has collected\nCDR data under a consumer data request under Part 4 made on behalf of a CDR\nconsumer must not use or disclose it, or CDR data directly or indirectly derived\nfrom it, other than for a permitted use or disclosure (whether or not one that\nrelates to direct marketing).\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) For this rule:\n(a) any use or disclosure of service data by a direct or indirect OSP of:\n(i) an accredited data recipient; or\n(ii) a CDR representative of the accredited data recipient;\nis taken to have been by the accredited data recipient; and\n(b) it is irrelevant whether the use or disclosure is in accordance with the\nrelevant CDR outsourcing arrangement.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a direct or indirect\nOSP.\n(3) For this rule, any CDR data collected by an accredited person at the request of an\naffiliate is taken also to have been collected by the affiliate.\n(4) For this rule:\n(a) any use or disclosure of service data by a CDR representative is taken to\nhave been by the CDR representative principal; and\n(b) it is irrelevant whether the use or disclosure is in accordance with the CDR\nrepresentative arrangement.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.7\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\n(5) For this rule:\n(a) any collection of service data by a direct or indirect OSP of an accredited\nperson is taken to have been by the accredited person; and\n(b) it is irrelevant whether the collection is in accordance with the relevant\nCDR outsourcing arrangement.\nNote:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR out",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-10-ss-1"
        },
