      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.134",
      "values:originalText": "(2) An accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct or indirect OSP of:\n(a) the accredited person; or\n(b) a CDR representative of the accredited person;\nfails to comply with section 56EL of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR\nconsumer as if it were an accredited data recipient of the service data.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) An accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct or indirect OSP of:\n(a) the accredited person; or\n(b) a CDR representative of the accredited person;\nfails to comply with section 56EL of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR\nconsumer as if it were an accredited data recipient of the service data.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "values:partOf": {
