    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-18",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 11  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-18"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For subsection 56EO(1) of the Act, the steps are set out in Schedule 2.\nNote:\nBroadly speaking, the steps are for an accredited data recipient of CDR data to:\n•\ndefine and implement security governance in relation to CDR data; and\n•\ndefine the boundaries of the CDR data environment; and\n•\nhave and maintain an information security capability; and\n•\nimplement a formal controls assessment program; and\n•\nmanage and report security incidents.\n(2) For this rule, where an accredited data recipient is an OSP chain principal, a\nfailure by a direct or indirect OSP to comply with Schedule 2 in relation to\nservice data is taken to be a failure by the accredited data recipient.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.12\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(3) For this rule, where an accredited data recipient is a CDR representative\nprincipal, a failure by:\n(a) the CDR representative; or\n(b) any direct or indirect OSP of the CDR representative;\nto comply with Schedule 2 in relation to service data is taken to be a failure by\nthe CDR representative principal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For subsection 56EO(1) of the Act, the steps are set out in Schedule 2.\nNote:\nBroadly speaking, the steps are for an accredited data recipient of CDR data to:\n•\ndefine and implement security governance in relation to CDR data; and\n•\ndefine the boundaries of the CDR data environment; and\n•\nhave and maintain an information security capability; and\n•\nimplement a formal controls assessment program; and\n•\nmanage and report security incidents.\n(2) For this rule, where an accredited data recipient is an OSP chain principal, a\nfailure by a direct or indirect OSP to comply with Schedule 2 in relation to\nservice data is taken to be a failure by the accredited data recipient.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.12\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(3) For this rule, where an accredited data recipient is a CDR representative\nprincipal, a failure by:\n(a) the CDR representative; or\n(b) any direct or indirect OSP of the CDR representative;\nto comply with Schedule 2 in relation to service data is taken to be a failure by\nthe CDR representative principal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-18-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-18-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-18-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "feceb90a481eb3583e6891f5eff14d98ebc859d596de4c46af30f7645b0dcdd3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-18",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 11  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For subsection 56EO(1) of the Act, the steps are set out in Schedule 2.\nNote:\nBroadly speaking, the steps are for an accredited data recipient of CDR data to:\n•\ndefine and implement security governance in relation to CDR data; and\n•\ndefine the boundaries of the CDR data environment; and\n•\nhave and maintain an information security capability; and\n•\nimplement a formal controls assessment program; and\n•\nmanage and report security incidents.\n(2) For this rule, where an accredited data recipient is an OSP chain principal, a\nfailure by a direct or indirect OSP to comply with Schedule 2 in relation to\nservice data is taken to be a failure by the accredited data recipient.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.12\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(3) For this rule, where an accredited data recipient is a CDR representative\nprincipal, a failure by:\n(a) the CDR representative; or\n(b) any direct or indirect OSP of the CDR representative;\nto comply with Schedule 2 in relation to service data is taken to be a failure by\nthe CDR representative principal."
    },
    {
