      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.137",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The steps are:\n(a) to apply the CDR data de-identification process to the redundant data; and\n(b) direct any direct OSP or CDR representative of the accredited data\nrecipient (the recipient of the redundant data) that had been provided with\na copy of the redundant data:\n(i) to delete the redundant data, as well as any CDR data that has been\ndirectly or indirectly derived from it, and notify the accredited data\nrecipient of the deletion; and\n(ii) to, if the recipient of the redundant data has provided any such data to\nits own direct OSP (the further recipient), give the direction set out in\nthis paragraph to the further recipient as if the further recipient were\nitself the recipient of the redundant data.\nNote:\nIf the redundant data cannot be de-identified in accordance with the CDR data\nde-identification process, it must be deleted in accordance with the CDR data deletion\nprocess: see subrule 1.17(4).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The steps are:\n(a) to apply the CDR data de-identification process to the redundant data; and\n(b) direct any direct OSP or CDR representative of the accredited data\nrecipient (the recipient of the redundant data) that had been provided with\na copy of the redundant data:\n(i) to delete the redundant data, as well as any CDR data that has been\ndirectly or indirectly derived from it, and notify the accredited data\nrecipient of the deletion; and\n(ii) to, if the recipient of the redundant data has provided any such data to\nits own direct OSP (the further recipient), give the direction set out in\nthis paragraph to the further recipient as if the further recipient were\nitself the recipient of the redundant data.\nNote:\nIf the redundant data cannot be de-identified in accordance with the CDR data\nde-identification process, it must be deleted in accordance with the CDR data deletion\nprocess: see subrule 1.17(4).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-19"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-19-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-19-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e84ad177bc781e587b08403c840dfdabc2af18e2afb940f26e33703dc3d3e0e3",
      "skos:note": "Delete redundant data and notify recipient of deletion."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-19-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7(2) 12  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 12—de-identification of redundant data",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 137,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The steps are:\n(a) to apply the CDR data de-identification process to the redundant data; and\n(b) direct any direct OSP or CDR representative of the accredited data\nrecipient (the recipient of the redundant data) that had been provided with\na copy of the redundant data:\n(i) to delete the redundant data, as well as any CDR data that has been\ndirectly or indirectly derived from it, and notify the accredited data\nrecipient of the deletion; and\n(ii) to, if the recipient of the redundant data has provided any such data to\nits own direct OSP (the further recipient), give the direction set out in\nthis paragraph to the further recipient as if the further recipient were\nitself the recipient of the redundant data.\nNote:\nIf the redundant data cannot be de-identified in accordance with the CDR data\nde-identification process, it must be deleted in accordance with the CDR data deletion\nprocess: see subrule 1.17(4)."
    },
