    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-23",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 16  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 13—correction of data—CDR",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-23"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.138",
      "values:originalText": "representative\n(1) A CDR representative principal breaches this subrule if its CDR representative\nfails to comply with subsection 56EP(2) of the Act in relation to service data of a\nCDR consumer as if it were an accredited person.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.16\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) For subrule (1), it is irrelevant whether the action of the CDR representative in\nrelation to the service data is in accordance with the CDR representative\narrangement.",
      "skos:definition": "representative\n(1) A CDR representative principal breaches this subrule if its CDR representative\nfails to comply with subsection 56EP(2) of the Act in relation to service data of a\nCDR consumer as if it were an accredited person.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.16\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) For subrule (1), it is irrelevant whether the action of the CDR representative in\nrelation to the service data is in accordance with the CDR representative\narrangement.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-23-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-23-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "482a37dd98d937458a3d29b863e3a7362eed44601472b1155cd70a3ba2f16c8a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-7-23",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 16  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 13—correction of data—CDR",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 138,
      "values:originalText": "representative\n(1) A CDR representative principal breaches this subrule if its CDR representative\nfails to comply with subsection 56EP(2) of the Act in relation to service data of a\nCDR consumer as if it were an accredited person.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.16\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(2) For subrule (1), it is irrelevant whether the action of the CDR representative in\nrelation to the service data is in accordance with the CDR representative\narrangement."
    },
