      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.138",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CDR representative principal breaches this subrule if its CDR representative\nfails to comply with subsection 56EP(2) of the Act in relation to service data of a\nCDR consumer as if it were an accredited person.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.16\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A CDR representative principal breaches this subrule if its CDR representative\nfails to comply with subsection 56EP(2) of the Act in relation to service data of a\nCDR consumer as if it were an accredited person.\nNote 1:\nSee rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative\narrangement.\n\n\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7\nRules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2\nSection 7.16\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\nNote 2:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).",
