    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 1  Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.147",
      "values:originalText": "This Part deals with a range of miscellaneous matters, including:\n•\ndecisions that can be reviewed by the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal; and\n•\nrules relating to reporting, record-keeping and auditing; and\n•\ncivil penalty provisions of the consumer data rules, which are enforced\nunder the enforcement provisions of the Act.",
      "skos:definition": "This Part deals with a range of miscellaneous matters, including:\n•\ndecisions that can be reviewed by the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal; and\n•\nrules relating to reporting, record-keeping and auditing; and\n•\ncivil penalty provisions of the consumer data rules, which are enforced\nunder the enforcement provisions of the Act.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-6-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "447ebc59b31d4967270a4b069a28d574cc057c7acfb60addf5082d97b2667923",
      "skos:note": "Miscellaneous matters including decisions reviewable by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal and civil penalty provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 1  Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 147,
      "values:originalText": "This Part deals with a range of miscellaneous matters, including:\n•\ndecisions that can be reviewed by the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal; and\n•\nrules relating to reporting, record-keeping and auditing; and\n•\ncivil penalty provisions of the consumer data rules, which are enforced\nunder the enforcement provisions of the Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 2  Review of decisions by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.148",
      "values:originalText": "Applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal to review any\nof the following decisions:\n(a) a decision of the CDR Accreditor under rule 5.10 to:\n(i) impose a condition on an accreditation; or\n(ii) vary a condition that has been imposed;\n(b) a decision of the CDR Accreditor under rule 5.17 to:\n(i) suspend an accreditation; or\n(ii) extend a suspension; or\n(iii) revoke an accreditation.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 9\nReporting, record keeping and audit  Division 9.3\nSection 9.3\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "skos:definition": "Applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal to review any\nof the following decisions:\n(a) a decision of the CDR Accreditor under rule 5.10 to:\n(i) impose a condition on an accreditation; or\n(ii) vary a condition that has been imposed;\n(b) a decision of the CDR Accreditor under rule 5.17 to:\n(i) suspend an accreditation; or\n(ii) extend a suspension; or\n(iii) revoke an accreditation.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 9\nReporting, record keeping and audit  Division 9.3\nSection 9.3\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-7-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1c9ffcd83f783f0a016752a27bc88980cb780cfa4f4b3d0ae8f55103a0ac4b12",
      "skos:note": "Review of decisions by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 2  Review of decisions by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 148,
      "values:originalText": "Applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal to review any\nof the following decisions:\n(a) a decision of the CDR Accreditor under rule 5.10 to:\n(i) impose a condition on an accreditation; or\n(ii) vary a condition that has been imposed;\n(b) a decision of the CDR Accreditor under rule 5.17 to:\n(i) suspend an accreditation; or\n(ii) extend a suspension; or\n(iii) revoke an accreditation.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 9\nReporting, record keeping and audit  Division 9.3\nSection 9.3\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-7-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-7"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 3  Records to be kept and maintained",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.149",
      "values:originalText": "Records to be kept and maintained—data holder\n(1) A data holder must keep and maintain records that record and explain the\nfollowing:\n(a) authorisations given by CDR consumers to disclose CDR data;\n(b) amendments to or withdrawals of authorisations to disclose CDR data;\n(c) notifications of withdrawals of consents to collect CDR data;\n(ca) where the data holder is a primary data holder—any requests for SR data\nmade under subrule 1.23(4) and responses received under subrule 1.23(5)\nor (6);\n(cb) where the data holder is a secondary data holder:\n(i) any requests for SR data received under subrule 1.22(3) or 1.23(4) and\nresponses given under subrule 1.22(4) or (5) or 1.23(5) or (6); and\n(ii) where the data holder has refused to disclose requested SR data—the\nreasons relied upon to refuse to disclose the SR data, including any\nrule or data standard;\n(d) disclosures of CDR data made in response to consumer data requests;\n(da) any written agreement of a kind referred to in subrule 2.4(5) the data holder\nhas entered into;\n(db) any election by the data holder in effect under subclause 7.1A(1) of\nSchedule 3;\n(e) instances where the data holder has refused to disclose requested CDR data\nand the rule or data standard relied upon to refuse to disclose the CDR\ndata;\n(f) CDR complaint data;\n(fa) CDR consumer complaints;\n(g) the processes by which the data holder asks CDR consumers for their\nauthorisation to disclose CDR data and for an amendment to their\nauthorisation, including a video of each process.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\nRecords to be kept and maintained—accredited data recipient\n(2) An accredited data recipient must keep and maintain records that record and\nexplain the following:\n(a) all consents, including, if applicable, the uses of the CDR data that the\nCDR consumer has consented to under any use consents;\n(b) amendments to or withdrawals of consents by CDR consumers;\n(c) notifications of withdrawals of authorisations received from data holders;\n(d) CDR complaint data;",
      "skos:definition": "Records to be kept and maintained—data holder\n(1) A data holder must keep and maintain records that record and explain the\nfollowing:\n(a) authorisations given by CDR consumers to disclose CDR data;\n(b) amendments to or withdrawals of authorisations to disclose CDR data;\n(c) notifications of withdrawals of consents to collect CDR data;\n(ca) where the data holder is a primary data holder—any requests for SR data\nmade under subrule 1.23(4) and responses received under subrule 1.23(5)\nor (6);\n(cb) where the data holder is a secondary data holder:\n(i) any requests for SR data received under subrule 1.22(3) or 1.23(4) and\nresponses given under subrule 1.22(4) or (5) or 1.23(5) or (6); and\n(ii) where the data holder has refused to disclose requested SR data—the\nreasons relied upon to refuse to disclose the SR data, including any\nrule or data standard;\n(d) disclosures of CDR data made in response to consumer data requests;\n(da) any written agreement of a kind referred to in subrule 2.4(5) the data holder\nhas entered into;\n(db) any election by the data holder in effect under subclause 7.1A(1) of\nSchedule 3;\n(e) instances where the data holder has refused to disclose requested CDR data\nand the rule or data standard relied upon to refuse to disclose the CDR\ndata;\n(f) CDR complaint data;\n(fa) CDR consumer complaints;\n(g) the processes by which the data holder asks CDR consumers for their\nauthorisation to disclose CDR data and for an amendment to their\nauthorisation, including a video of each process.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\nRecords to be kept and maintained—accredited data recipient\n(2) An accredited data recipient must keep and maintain records that record and\nexplain the following:\n(a) all consents, including, if applicable, the uses of the CDR data that the\nCDR consumer has consented to under any use consents;\n(b) amendments to or withdrawals of consents by CDR consumers;\n(c) notifications of withdrawals of authori",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-8-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-8-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "daed8a751aa92cd7b9016021ed115d439f06adf445e11459e15ddda814a71b4b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 3  Records to be kept and maintained",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 149,
      "values:originalText": "Records to be kept and maintained—data holder\n(1) A data holder must keep and maintain records that record and explain the\nfollowing:\n(a) authorisations given by CDR consumers to disclose CDR data;\n(b) amendments to or withdrawals of authorisations to disclose CDR data;\n(c) notifications of withdrawals of consents to collect CDR data;\n(ca) where the data holder is a primary data holder—any requests for SR data\nmade under subrule 1.23(4) and responses received under subrule 1.23(5)\nor (6);\n(cb) where the data holder is a secondary data holder:\n(i) any requests for SR data received under subrule 1.22(3) or 1.23(4) and\nresponses given under subrule 1.22(4) or (5) or 1.23(5) or (6); and\n(ii) where the data holder has refused to disclose requested SR data—the\nreasons relied upon to refuse to disclose the SR data, including any\nrule or data standard;\n(d) disclosures of CDR data made in response to consumer data requests;\n(da) any written agreement of a kind referred to in subrule 2.4(5) the data holder\nhas entered into;\n(db) any election by the data holder in effect under subclause 7.1A(1) of\nSchedule 3;\n(e) instances where the data holder has refused to disclose requested CDR data\nand the rule or data standard relied upon to refuse to disclose the CDR\ndata;\n(f) CDR complaint data;\n(fa) CDR consumer complaints;\n(g) the processes by which the data holder asks CDR consumers for their\nauthorisation to disclose CDR data and for an amendment to their\nauthorisation, including a video of each process.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\nRecords to be kept and maintained—accredited data recipient\n(2) An accredited data recipient must keep and maintain records that record and\nexplain the following:\n(a) all consents, including, if applicable, the uses of the CDR data that the\nCDR consumer has consented to under any use consents;\n(b) amendments to or withdrawals of consents by CDR consumers;\n(c) notifications of withdrawals of authorisations received from data holders;\n(d) CDR complaint data;"
    },
