    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 4  Reporting requirements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.153",
      "values:originalText": "Reports that must be prepared—data holder\n(1) A data holder must prepare a report for each reporting period that:\n(a) is in the form approved by the Commission for the purposes of this rule;\nand\n(b) summarises the CDR complaint data that relates to that reporting period;\nand\n(c) sets out the number (if any) of:\n(i) product data requests; and\n(ii) consumer data requests made by eligible CDR consumers; and\n(iii) consumer data requests made by accredited persons on behalf of\neligible CDR consumers;\nreceived by the data holder during the reporting period; and\n(d) sets out, for each of the types of requests referred to in subparagraphs\n(c)(i), (ii) and (iii):\n(i) the number of times the data holder has refused to disclose CDR data;\nand\n(ii) the rule or data standard relied upon to refuse to disclose that data;\nand\n(iii) the number of times the data holder has relied on each of those rules\nor data standards as a ground of refusal.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of product data request see rule 2.3. For the meaning of consumer\ndata request see rule 3.3 (requests made by CDR consumers) and rules 4.4 and 4.7A\n(requests by accredited persons).\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\nReports that must be prepared—secondary data holder\n(1A) A secondary data holder must prepare a report for each reporting period that:\n(a) is in the form approved by the Commission for the purposes of this rule;\nand\n(b) sets out the number (if any) of requests for SR data under subrule 1.22(3)\nor 1.23(4) received by the data holder from the primary data holder during\nthe reporting period; and\n(c) sets out:",
      "skos:definition": "Reports that must be prepared—data holder\n(1) A data holder must prepare a report for each reporting period that:\n(a) is in the form approved by the Commission for the purposes of this rule;\nand\n(b) summarises the CDR complaint data that relates to that reporting period;\nand\n(c) sets out the number (if any) of:\n(i) product data requests; and\n(ii) consumer data requests made by eligible CDR consumers; and\n(iii) consumer data requests made by accredited persons on behalf of\neligible CDR consumers;\nreceived by the data holder during the reporting period; and\n(d) sets out, for each of the types of requests referred to in subparagraphs\n(c)(i), (ii) and (iii):\n(i) the number of times the data holder has refused to disclose CDR data;\nand\n(ii) the rule or data standard relied upon to refuse to disclose that data;\nand\n(iii) the number of times the data holder has relied on each of those rules\nor data standards as a ground of refusal.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of product data request see rule 2.3. For the meaning of consumer\ndata request see rule 3.3 (requests made by CDR consumers) and rules 4.4 and 4.7A\n(requests by accredited persons).\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\nReports that must be prepared—secondary data holder\n(1A) A secondary data holder must prepare a report for each reporting period that:\n(a) is in the form approved by the Commission for the purposes of this rule;\nand\n(b) sets out the number (if any) of requests for SR data under subrule 1.22(3)\nor 1.23(4) received by the data holder from the primary data holder during\nthe reporting period; and\n(c) sets out:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-9-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-9-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "306580c70b0f5928a6521c641f229fb2b316f2ff23e2e19f8ba2368d91b75d7f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 4  Reporting requirements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 153,
      "values:originalText": "Reports that must be prepared—data holder\n(1) A data holder must prepare a report for each reporting period that:\n(a) is in the form approved by the Commission for the purposes of this rule;\nand\n(b) summarises the CDR complaint data that relates to that reporting period;\nand\n(c) sets out the number (if any) of:\n(i) product data requests; and\n(ii) consumer data requests made by eligible CDR consumers; and\n(iii) consumer data requests made by accredited persons on behalf of\neligible CDR consumers;\nreceived by the data holder during the reporting period; and\n(d) sets out, for each of the types of requests referred to in subparagraphs\n(c)(i), (ii) and (iii):\n(i) the number of times the data holder has refused to disclose CDR data;\nand\n(ii) the rule or data standard relied upon to refuse to disclose that data;\nand\n(iii) the number of times the data holder has relied on each of those rules\nor data standards as a ground of refusal.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of product data request see rule 2.3. For the meaning of consumer\ndata request see rule 3.3 (requests made by CDR consumers) and rules 4.4 and 4.7A\n(requests by accredited persons).\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\nReports that must be prepared—secondary data holder\n(1A) A secondary data holder must prepare a report for each reporting period that:\n(a) is in the form approved by the Commission for the purposes of this rule;\nand\n(b) sets out the number (if any) of requests for SR data under subrule 1.22(3)\nor 1.23(4) received by the data holder from the primary data holder during\nthe reporting period; and\n(c) sets out:"
    },
