      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9(1A) 4  Reporting requirements",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 153,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) A secondary data holder must prepare a report for each reporting period that:\n(a) is in the form approved by the Commission for the purposes of this rule;\nand\n(b) sets out the number (if any) of requests for SR data under subrule 1.22(3)\nor 1.23(4) received by the data holder from the primary data holder during\nthe reporting period; and\n(c) sets out:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-9-ss-1a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-9-ss-1a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-9-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide a report",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-9-ss-1a-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "DURING",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Report covers a specific time period",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "during the reporting period;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-41",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 14(4); or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-41"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.155",
      "values:originalText": "(ii) previously included in a report prepared under this rule; and\n(c) in relation to any good or service that is required to be described under\nparagraph (b):\n(i) describes the CDR data that is needed in order to offer the good or\nservice to CDR consumers; and\n(ii) explains why that data is needed in order to offer the good or service\nto CDR consumers; and\n(d) describes any material changes that have been made to any goods or\nservices offered by the CDR representative since the previous reporting\nperiod, including any changes to the matters referred to in paragraph (b);\nand",
      "skos:definition": "(ii) previously included in a report prepared under this rule; and\n(c) in relation to any good or service that is required to be described under\nparagraph (b):\n(i) describes the CDR data that is needed in order to offer the good or\nservice to CDR consumers; and\n(ii) explains why that data is needed in order to offer the good or service\nto CDR consumers; and\n(d) describes any material changes that have been made to any goods or\nservices offered by the CDR representative since the previous reporting\nperiod, including any changes to the matters referred to in paragraph (b);\nand",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-41-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-41-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0c05b112de9e2a98bbc99bf93c9d8b0bbfc7f52dc49086061a2e2a2843d462a1",
      "skos:note": "Describe CDR data and changes to goods/services offered by the CDR representative.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-41",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 14(4); or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 155,
      "values:originalText": "(ii) previously included in a report prepared under this rule; and\n(c) in relation to any good or service that is required to be described under\nparagraph (b):\n(i) describes the CDR data that is needed in order to offer the good or\nservice to CDR consumers; and\n(ii) explains why that data is needed in order to offer the good or service\nto CDR consumers; and\n(d) describes any material changes that have been made to any goods or\nservices offered by the CDR representative since the previous reporting\nperiod, including any changes to the matters referred to in paragraph (b);\nand"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-41-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-41"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-41-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide information about CDR data and changes.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 5  Requests from CDR consumers for copies of records",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.157",
      "values:originalText": "Requests to data holders of CDR data\n(1) A CDR consumer may request a data holder for copies of records relating to the\ninformation referred to in paragraphs 9.3(1)(a), (b), (c), (d), (f) and (fa) that\nrelates to the CDR consumer.\nRequests to accredited data recipients\n(2) A CDR consumer may request an accredited data recipient for copies of records\nrelating to the information referred to in:\n(a) paragraphs 9.3(2)(a), (b), (c), (d), (da), (e), (ea), (eb), (ec), (ed), (ee), (ef),\n(eg), (f) and (m); and\n(b) paragraphs 9.3(2A)(d), (e), (f), (g), (ga), (h), (ha), (hb), (hc), (i) and (o);\nthat relates to the CDR consumer.\nForm for requests\n(3) A request under this rule must be in the form (if any) approved by the\nCommission for the purposes of this subrule.\nDealing with requests under this rule\n(4) A person who receives a request under this rule must provide the requested\ncopies, in the form (if any) approved by the Commission for the purposes of this\nrule, as soon as practicable, but no later than 10 business days, after receiving the\nrequest.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n(5) A data holder must not charge a fee for making or responding to a request under\nsubrule (1).\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n(6) An accredited data recipient must not charge a fee for making or responding to a\nrequest under subrule (2).\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.",
      "skos:definition": "Requests to data holders of CDR data\n(1) A CDR consumer may request a data holder for copies of records relating to the\ninformation referred to in paragraphs 9.3(1)(a), (b), (c), (d), (f) and (fa) that\nrelates to the CDR consumer.\nRequests to accredited data recipients\n(2) A CDR consumer may request an accredited data recipient for copies of records\nrelating to the information referred to in:\n(a) paragraphs 9.3(2)(a), (b), (c), (d), (da), (e), (ea), (eb), (ec), (ed), (ee), (ef),\n(eg), (f) and (m); and\n(b) paragraphs 9.3(2A)(d), (e), (f), (g), (ga), (h), (ha), (hb), (hc), (i) and (o);\nthat relates to the CDR consumer.\nForm for requests\n(3) A request under this rule must be in the form (if any) approved by the\nCommission for the purposes of this subrule.\nDealing with requests under this rule\n(4) A person who receives a request under this rule must provide the requested\ncopies, in the form (if any) approved by the Commission for the purposes of this\nrule, as soon as practicable, but no later than 10 business days, after receiving the\nrequest.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n(5) A data holder must not charge a fee for making or responding to a request under\nsubrule (1).\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n(6) An accredited data recipient must not charge a fee for making or responding to a\nrequest under subrule (2).\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-10-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-10-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-10-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-10-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-10-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-10-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c049d02afa96f7eeca08f50fdcb644d7b0264d24bf5e30c3034e158b3f218fe9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 5  Requests from CDR consumers for copies of records",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 157,
      "values:originalText": "Requests to data holders of CDR data\n(1) A CDR consumer may request a data holder for copies of records relating to the\ninformation referred to in paragraphs 9.3(1)(a), (b), (c), (d), (f) and (fa) that\nrelates to the CDR consumer.\nRequests to accredited data recipients\n(2) A CDR consumer may request an accredited data recipient for copies of records\nrelating to the information referred to in:\n(a) paragraphs 9.3(2)(a), (b), (c), (d), (da), (e), (ea), (eb), (ec), (ed), (ee), (ef),\n(eg), (f) and (m); and\n(b) paragraphs 9.3(2A)(d), (e), (f), (g), (ga), (h), (ha), (hb), (hc), (i) and (o);\nthat relates to the CDR consumer.\nForm for requests\n(3) A request under this rule must be in the form (if any) approved by the\nCommission for the purposes of this subrule.\nDealing with requests under this rule\n(4) A person who receives a request under this rule must provide the requested\ncopies, in the form (if any) approved by the Commission for the purposes of this\nrule, as soon as practicable, but no later than 10 business days, after receiving the\nrequest.\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n(5) A data holder must not charge a fee for making or responding to a request under\nsubrule (1).\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000.\n(6) An accredited data recipient must not charge a fee for making or responding to a\nrequest under subrule (2).\nCivil penalty:\n(a) for an individual―$50,000; and\n(b) for a body corporate―$250,000."
    },
