    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 7  Audits by the Data Recipient Accreditor",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR Accreditor may, at any time, audit the compliance of an accredited\ndata recipient with any or all of the following:\n(a) the obligations under rule 5.12;\n(b) any conditions imposed on their accreditation.\n(2) For the purposes of conducting an audit or otherwise monitoring the compliance\nof the accredited data recipient with the criteria and conditions mentioned in\nsubrule (1), the CDR Accreditor may give an accredited data recipient a written\nnotice that requests the accredited data recipient to produce:\n(a) copies of records that are required by this Division to be kept; or\n(b) information from such records.\n(3) The accredited data recipient must comply with a request under subrule (2).\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(4) The CDR Accreditor must provide a copy of any audit report to the Commission\nand the Information Commissioner.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 9\nCivil penalty provisions  Division 9.4\nSection 9.8\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The CDR Accreditor may, at any time, audit the compliance of an accredited\ndata recipient with any or all of the following:\n(a) the obligations under rule 5.12;\n(b) any conditions imposed on their accreditation.\n(2) For the purposes of conducting an audit or otherwise monitoring the compliance\nof the accredited data recipient with the criteria and conditions mentioned in\nsubrule (1), the CDR Accreditor may give an accredited data recipient a written\nnotice that requests the accredited data recipient to produce:\n(a) copies of records that are required by this Division to be kept; or\n(b) information from such records.\n(3) The accredited data recipient must comply with a request under subrule (2).\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(4) The CDR Accreditor must provide a copy of any audit report to the Commission\nand the Information Commissioner.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 9\nCivil penalty provisions  Division 9.4\nSection 9.8\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-12-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-12-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-12-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-12-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "798862ccd52d55c6f1bf75c9276860928dce6a917d4a2329d4dfbc303103fed7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-9-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 7  Audits by the Data Recipient Accreditor",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR Accreditor may, at any time, audit the compliance of an accredited\ndata recipient with any or all of the following:\n(a) the obligations under rule 5.12;\n(b) any conditions imposed on their accreditation.\n(2) For the purposes of conducting an audit or otherwise monitoring the compliance\nof the accredited data recipient with the criteria and conditions mentioned in\nsubrule (1), the CDR Accreditor may give an accredited data recipient a written\nnotice that requests the accredited data recipient to produce:\n(a) copies of records that are required by this Division to be kept; or\n(b) information from such records.\n(3) The accredited data recipient must comply with a request under subrule (2).\nNote:\nThis subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8).\n(4) The CDR Accreditor must provide a copy of any audit report to the Commission\nand the Information Commissioner.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 9\nCivil penalty provisions  Division 9.4\nSection 9.8\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020"
    },
