    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 2  Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-2-sec-1-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.167",
      "values:originalText": "In this Schedule:\nCDR data environment means the information technology systems used for, and\nprocesses that relate to, the management of CDR data.\ninformation security capability, of an accredited data recipient:\n(a) means the accredited data recipient’s ability to manage the security of its\nCDR data environment in practice through the implementation and\noperation of processes and controls; and\n(b) includes the accredited data recipient being able to allocate adequate\nbudget and resources, and provide for management oversight.\nsenior management, of an accredited data recipient that is a body corporate,\nmeans:\n(a) the accredited data recipient’s directors; and\n(b) any person who is an associated person, within the meaning of paragraph\n(a) of the definition of that term, of the accredited data recipient.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Schedule:\nCDR data environment means the information technology systems used for, and\nprocesses that relate to, the management of CDR data.\ninformation security capability, of an accredited data recipient:\n(a) means the accredited data recipient’s ability to manage the security of its\nCDR data environment in practice through the implementation and\noperation of processes and controls; and\n(b) includes the accredited data recipient being able to allocate adequate\nbudget and resources, and provide for management oversight.\nsenior management, of an accredited data recipient that is a body corporate,\nmeans:\n(a) the accredited data recipient’s directors; and\n(b) any person who is an associated person, within the meaning of paragraph\n(a) of the definition of that term, of the accredited data recipient.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-9-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-9-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-9-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-9-logic-ltl-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-9-logic-deontic-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-9-logic-deontic-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b13ad6092d1242f82b89d8e922d5bb2f4c1b10f2c79ff81e8025af804ac04dc6",
      "skos:note": "Defines terms for CDR data environment and security capability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-2-sec-1-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 2  Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 167,
      "values:originalText": "In this Schedule:\nCDR data environment means the information technology systems used for, and\nprocesses that relate to, the management of CDR data.\ninformation security capability, of an accredited data recipient:\n(a) means the accredited data recipient’s ability to manage the security of its\nCDR data environment in practice through the implementation and\noperation of processes and controls; and\n(b) includes the accredited data recipient being able to allocate adequate\nbudget and resources, and provide for management oversight.\nsenior management, of an accredited data recipient that is a body corporate,\nmeans:\n(a) the accredited data recipient’s directors; and\n(b) any person who is an associated person, within the meaning of paragraph\n(a) of the definition of that term, of the accredited data recipient."
    },
