      "cml:conclusionText": "Senior management is an obligation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 3  Step 1—Define and implement security governance in relation to CDR data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-2-sec-1-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.167",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must establish a formal governance\nframework for managing information security risks relating to CDR data setting\nout the policies, processes, roles and responsibilities required to facilitate the\noversight and management of information security.\n(2) The accredited data recipient must clearly document its practices and procedures\nrelating to information security and management of CDR data, including the\nspecific responsibilities of senior management.\n(3) The accredited data recipient must have and maintain an information security\npolicy that details:\n\nSchedule 2  Steps for privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data held by accredited data recipients",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must establish a formal governance\nframework for managing information security risks relating to CDR data setting\nout the policies, processes, roles and responsibilities required to facilitate the\noversight and management of information security.\n(2) The accredited data recipient must clearly document its practices and procedures\nrelating to information security and management of CDR data, including the\nspecific responsibilities of senior management.\n(3) The accredited data recipient must have and maintain an information security\npolicy that details:\n\nSchedule 2  Steps for privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data held by accredited data recipients",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-10-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-10-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-10-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c43e2a849d1b06cce9533fb7e057faac084a85aa7e7b15d7bec99f4ec032da51"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-2-sec-1-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 3  Step 1—Define and implement security governance in relation to CDR data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 167,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must establish a formal governance\nframework for managing information security risks relating to CDR data setting\nout the policies, processes, roles and responsibilities required to facilitate the\noversight and management of information security.\n(2) The accredited data recipient must clearly document its practices and procedures\nrelating to information security and management of CDR data, including the\nspecific responsibilities of senior management.\n(3) The accredited data recipient must have and maintain an information security\npolicy that details:\n\nSchedule 2  Steps for privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data held by accredited data recipients"
    },
