    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 4  Step 2—Define the boundaries of the CDR data environment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-2-sec-1-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An accredited data recipient must assess, define and document the boundaries of\nits CDR data environment.\n(2) The accredited data recipient must review the boundaries of its CDR data\nenvironment for completeness and accuracy:\n(a) as soon as practicable when it becomes aware of material changes to the\nextent and nature of threats to its CDR data environment; or\n(b) where no such material changes occur—at least annually.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An accredited data recipient must assess, define and document the boundaries of\nits CDR data environment.\n(2) The accredited data recipient must review the boundaries of its CDR data\nenvironment for completeness and accuracy:\n(a) as soon as practicable when it becomes aware of material changes to the\nextent and nature of threats to its CDR data environment; or\n(b) where no such material changes occur—at least annually.",
