      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.169",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The accredited data recipient’s CDR data security response plans must include\nprocedures for:\n(a) managing all relevant stages of an incident, from detection to post-incident\nreview; and\n(b) notifying CDR data security breaches to the Information Commissioner\nand to CDR consumers as required under Part IIIC of the Privacy Act 1988;\nand\n(c) notifying information security incidents to the Australian Cyber Security\nCentre as soon as practicable and in any case no later than 30 days after the\naccredited data recipient becomes aware of the security incident.\n\nSchedule 2  Steps for privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data held by accredited data recipients",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The accredited data recipient’s CDR data security response plans must include\nprocedures for:\n(a) managing all relevant stages of an incident, from detection to post-incident\nreview; and\n(b) notifying CDR data security breaches to the Information Commissioner\nand to CDR consumers as required under Part IIIC of the Privacy Act 1988;\nand\n(c) notifying information security incidents to the Australian Cyber Security\nCentre as soon as practicable and in any case no later than 30 days after the\naccredited data recipient becomes aware of the security incident.\n\nSchedule 2  Steps for privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data held by accredited data recipients",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-14"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-14-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-1-14-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ba50a2fc6b090f6143b927cde737c6b64eb85e4bdf1e3a59fc5bd1cd614858bd",
      "skos:note": "Accredited data recipient must notify breaches and incidents to specified authorities.",
      "dc:description": "Notification of security incidents and breaches"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-2-sec-1-14-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1(3) 7  Step 5—Manage and report security incidents",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 169,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The accredited data recipient’s CDR data security response plans must include\nprocedures for:\n(a) managing all relevant stages of an incident, from detection to post-incident\nreview; and\n(b) notifying CDR data security breaches to the Information Commissioner\nand to CDR consumers as required under Part IIIC of the Privacy Act 1988;\nand\n(c) notifying information security incidents to the Australian Cyber Security\nCentre as soon as practicable and in any case no later than 30 days after the\naccredited data recipient becomes aware of the security incident.\n\nSchedule 2  Steps for privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data held by accredited data recipients"
    },
