    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-2-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 2  Information security controls",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-2-sec-2-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.171",
      "values:originalText": "The information security controls are set out in the following table:\nControl requirements\nMinimum controls\nDescription of minimum controls\n(a)\nMulti-factor authentication or equivalent control\nMulti-factor authentication or equivalent control is required for all\naccess to CDR data.\nNote:\nThis minimum control does not apply to access to CDR data by\nCDR consumers.\n(b)\nRestrict administrative privileges\nAdministrative privileges are granted only on an as needs basis for\nusers to perform their duties and only for the period they are\nrequired for.\nPrivileges granted on an ongoing basis are regularly reviewed to\nconfirm their ongoing need.\n(1)\nAn accredited data\nrecipient must have\nprocesses in place to\nlimit the risk of\ninappropriate or\nunauthorised access to its\nCDR data environment.\n(c)\nAudit logging and monitoring\nCritical events are identified, logged and retained to help ensure\ntraceability and accountability of actions. These logs are reviewed\nregularly to identify irregularities and deviations from expected\nprocessing.\nNote:\nIn relation to retention, see paragraph 9.3(2)(l) of these rules.\n\nSchedule 2  Steps for privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data held by accredited data recipients",
      "skos:definition": "The information security controls are set out in the following table:\nControl requirements\nMinimum controls\nDescription of minimum controls\n(a)\nMulti-factor authentication or equivalent control\nMulti-factor authentication or equivalent control is required for all\naccess to CDR data.\nNote:\nThis minimum control does not apply to access to CDR data by\nCDR consumers.\n(b)\nRestrict administrative privileges\nAdministrative privileges are granted only on an as needs basis for\nusers to perform their duties and only for the period they are\nrequired for.\nPrivileges granted on an ongoing basis are regularly reviewed to\nconfirm their ongoing need.\n(1)\nAn accredited data\nrecipient must have\nprocesses in place to\nlimit the risk of\ninappropriate or\nunauthorised access to its\nCDR data environment.\n(c)\nAudit logging and monitoring\nCritical events are identified, logged and retained to help ensure\ntraceability and accountability of actions. These logs are reviewed\nregularly to identify irregularities and deviations from expected\nprocessing.\nNote:\nIn relation to retention, see paragraph 9.3(2)(l) of these rules.\n\nSchedule 2  Steps for privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data held by accredited data recipients",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-2-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-2-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7f830d51e7cab7934cac8d3bc8ed213c1ba6f5f78d0d94cb7f9370dee74e3e8b",
      "skos:note": "Multi-factor authentication or equivalent control is required for all access to CDR data."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-2-sec-2-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 2  Information security controls",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 171,
      "values:originalText": "The information security controls are set out in the following table:\nControl requirements\nMinimum controls\nDescription of minimum controls\n(a)\nMulti-factor authentication or equivalent control\nMulti-factor authentication or equivalent control is required for all\naccess to CDR data.\nNote:\nThis minimum control does not apply to access to CDR data by\nCDR consumers.\n(b)\nRestrict administrative privileges\nAdministrative privileges are granted only on an as needs basis for\nusers to perform their duties and only for the period they are\nrequired for.\nPrivileges granted on an ongoing basis are regularly reviewed to\nconfirm their ongoing need.\n(1)\nAn accredited data\nrecipient must have\nprocesses in place to\nlimit the risk of\ninappropriate or\nunauthorised access to its\nCDR data environment.\n(c)\nAudit logging and monitoring\nCritical events are identified, logged and retained to help ensure\ntraceability and accountability of actions. These logs are reviewed\nregularly to identify irregularities and deviations from expected\nprocessing.\nNote:\nIn relation to retention, see paragraph 9.3(2)(l) of these rules.\n\nSchedule 2  Steps for privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data held by accredited data recipients"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-2-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
