    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 1  Simplified outline of this Schedule",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-1-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.177",
      "values:originalText": "This Schedule deals with how these rules apply in relation to the banking sector\nand non-bank lenders sector (NBL sector).\nPart 1 of this Schedule excludes certain data holders in the banking sector and\nNBL sector from the application of these rules, and defines certain terms relevant\nto those sectors.\nPart 2 of this Schedule deals with eligible CDR consumers in relation to the\nbanking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 3 of this Schedule deals with CDR data that may or must be disclosed when\nproduct data requests and consumer data requests are made in relation to the\nbanking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 5 of this Schedule deals with dispute resolution requirements in relation to\nthe banking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 6 of this Schedule deals with the staged application of these rules to the\nNBL sector. Over time, as set out in that Part, these rules will apply to a\nprogressively broader range of data holders and types of requests in relation to\nthat sector. Part 6 also affects the application of these rules to the banking sector\nin some respects.\nPart 7 of this Schedule sets out modifications of these rules, and also deals with\nother, miscellaneous matters, in relation to the banking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 8 of this Schedule makes certain modifications to the operation of these\nrules in cases where an entity moves from the NBL sector to the banking sector.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "skos:definition": "This Schedule deals with how these rules apply in relation to the banking sector\nand non-bank lenders sector (NBL sector).\nPart 1 of this Schedule excludes certain data holders in the banking sector and\nNBL sector from the application of these rules, and defines certain terms relevant\nto those sectors.\nPart 2 of this Schedule deals with eligible CDR consumers in relation to the\nbanking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 3 of this Schedule deals with CDR data that may or must be disclosed when\nproduct data requests and consumer data requests are made in relation to the\nbanking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 5 of this Schedule deals with dispute resolution requirements in relation to\nthe banking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 6 of this Schedule deals with the staged application of these rules to the\nNBL sector. Over time, as set out in that Part, these rules will apply to a\nprogressively broader range of data holders and types of requests in relation to\nthat sector. Part 6 also affects the application of these rules to the banking sector\nin some respects.\nPart 7 of this Schedule sets out modifications of these rules, and also deals with\nother, miscellaneous matters, in relation to the banking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 8 of this Schedule makes certain modifications to the operation of these\nrules in cases where an entity moves from the NBL sector to the banking sector.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-7-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "31097e68f8e0db079959bc3bf3e53577fb0e83cd77ef78ee8f1f0e4bbcdce000",
      "skos:note": "Simplified outline of this Schedule"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-1-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 1  Simplified outline of this Schedule",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 177,
      "values:originalText": "This Schedule deals with how these rules apply in relation to the banking sector\nand non-bank lenders sector (NBL sector).\nPart 1 of this Schedule excludes certain data holders in the banking sector and\nNBL sector from the application of these rules, and defines certain terms relevant\nto those sectors.\nPart 2 of this Schedule deals with eligible CDR consumers in relation to the\nbanking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 3 of this Schedule deals with CDR data that may or must be disclosed when\nproduct data requests and consumer data requests are made in relation to the\nbanking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 5 of this Schedule deals with dispute resolution requirements in relation to\nthe banking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 6 of this Schedule deals with the staged application of these rules to the\nNBL sector. Over time, as set out in that Part, these rules will apply to a\nprogressively broader range of data holders and types of requests in relation to\nthat sector. Part 6 also affects the application of these rules to the banking sector\nin some respects.\nPart 7 of this Schedule sets out modifications of these rules, and also deals with\nother, miscellaneous matters, in relation to the banking sector and NBL sector.\nPart 8 of this Schedule makes certain modifications to the operation of these\nrules in cases where an entity moves from the NBL sector to the banking sector.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-7-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-7"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 1A  Application of these rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-1-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.178",
      "values:originalText": "These rules do not apply in respect of any of the following kinds of data holder\nin the banking sector or the NBL sector (an excluded data holder):\n(a) a data holder that is a body corporate, if the body:\n(i) is a registered religious body; and\n(ii) offers a covered product or products in advancing its charitable\npurposes;\n(b) a data holder that is:\n(i) a foreign ADI for the purposes of the Banking Act 1959; or\n(ii) a foreign branch of an Australian ADI; or\n(iii) a restricted ADI.\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nPreliminary  Part 1\nClause 1.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "skos:definition": "These rules do not apply in respect of any of the following kinds of data holder\nin the banking sector or the NBL sector (an excluded data holder):\n(a) a data holder that is a body corporate, if the body:\n(i) is a registered religious body; and\n(ii) offers a covered product or products in advancing its charitable\npurposes;\n(b) a data holder that is:\n(i) a foreign ADI for the purposes of the Banking Act 1959; or\n(ii) a foreign branch of an Australian ADI; or\n(iii) a restricted ADI.\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nPreliminary  Part 1\nClause 1.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e304098049ee89c982cf9057bd2cd4ccd3148c653a252d872dfe24a673ad8707",
      "skos:note": "Excluded data holders in banking and non-bank lenders sectors"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-1-8",
