    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-11-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1(2) 4  Meaning of covered product",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-1-11-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.181",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A product need not be available to all members of the public in order to be\npublicly offered.\nNote:\nA product may be offered subject to eligibility requirements. For instance, it may be\navailable only to a person operating a particular type of business. This does not prevent\nit from being “publicly offered” if it would otherwise fall within the ordinary meaning\nof that term.\nProducts that may be covered products\nItem\nColumn 1: Sector\nColumn 2: Products\nBanking and NBL sectors\n(a) a personal credit or charge card account;\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A product need not be available to all members of the public in order to be\npublicly offered.\nNote:\nA product may be offered subject to eligibility requirements. For instance, it may be\navailable only to a person operating a particular type of business. This does not prevent\nit from being “publicly offered” if it would otherwise fall within the ordinary meaning\nof that term.\nProducts that may be covered products\nItem\nColumn 1: Sector\nColumn 2: Products\nBanking and NBL sectors\n(a) a personal credit or charge card account;\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-11"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-11-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7fb41a67d8fd2ec2fcf991d44301f187b0dc3ade68c7407374417612c14035d5",
      "skos:note": "A product need not be available to all members of the public in order to be publicly offered."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-1-11-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1(2) 4  Meaning of covered product",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 181,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A product need not be available to all members of the public in order to be\npublicly offered.\nNote:\nA product may be offered subject to eligibility requirements. For instance, it may be\navailable only to a person operating a particular type of business. This does not prevent\nit from being “publicly offered” if it would otherwise fall within the ordinary meaning\nof that term.\nProducts that may be covered products\nItem\nColumn 1: Sector\nColumn 2: Products\nBanking and NBL sectors\n(a) a personal credit or charge card account;\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-11-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-11-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 5  Meaning of trial product",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-1-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.182",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For these rules, in relation to the banking sector and NBL sector, a covered\nproduct is a trial product if the product is offered:\n(a) with the description “pilot” or “trial”; and\n(b) with a statement that it will operate as a pilot or trial for a period that ends\nno more than 6 months after the initial offering (the trial period); and\n(c) on the basis that the number of customers supplied with the product for the\npurposes of the trial will be no more than 1,000; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nPreliminary  Part 1\nClause 1.5\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(d) with a statement that the product may be terminated before the end of the\ntrial period and that, if it is, the CDR data in relation to the product may not\nbe available for data sharing under these rules.\n(2) A covered product will cease to be a trial product from the first time any of the\nfollowing occurs:\n(a) the product is supplied or offered after the end of the trial period;\n(b) the product begins to be supplied to more than 1,000 customers.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For these rules, in relation to the banking sector and NBL sector, a covered\nproduct is a trial product if the product is offered:\n(a) with the description “pilot” or “trial”; and\n(b) with a statement that it will operate as a pilot or trial for a period that ends\nno more than 6 months after the initial offering (the trial period); and\n(c) on the basis that the number of customers supplied with the product for the\npurposes of the trial will be no more than 1,000; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nPreliminary  Part 1\nClause 1.5\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(d) with a statement that the product may be terminated before the end of the\ntrial period and that, if it is, the CDR data in relation to the product may not\nbe available for data sharing under these rules.\n(2) A covered product will cease to be a trial product from the first time any of the\nfollowing occurs:\n(a) the product is supplied or offered after the end of the trial period;\n(b) the product begins to be supplied to more than 1,000 customers.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-12-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-1-12-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b52049faeb85574c10581ac2a763d3056041d9f3ad4ef239e3b1895fa991779"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-1-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 5  Meaning of trial product",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 182,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For these rules, in relation to the banking sector and NBL sector, a covered\nproduct is a trial product if the product is offered:\n(a) with the description “pilot” or “trial”; and\n(b) with a statement that it will operate as a pilot or trial for a period that ends\nno more than 6 months after the initial offering (the trial period); and\n(c) on the basis that the number of customers supplied with the product for the\npurposes of the trial will be no more than 1,000; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nPreliminary  Part 1\nClause 1.5\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(d) with a statement that the product may be terminated before the end of the\ntrial period and that, if it is, the CDR data in relation to the product may not\nbe available for data sharing under these rules.\n(2) A covered product will cease to be a trial product from the first time any of the\nfollowing occurs:\n(a) the product is supplied or offered after the end of the trial period;\n(b) the product begins to be supplied to more than 1,000 customers.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors"
    },
