    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 1  Additional criteria for eligibility—banking and NBL sectors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-2-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of subrules 1.10B(1) and (2), the additional criterion for a CDR\nconsumer to be eligible in relation to a particular data holder in the banking\nsector or the NBL sector at a particular time, is that the account mentioned in\nparagraph 1.10B(1)(b) or (2)(b) is set up in such a way that, at that time, it can be\naccessed online.\nNote:\nRule 1.10B provides, among other things, that a person is eligible in relation to a data\nholder if the person is:\n(a)\nan account holder or secondary user for an account with the data holder; or\n(b)\na partner in a partnership that has an account with the data holder (whether or not\nthe person is an account holder or secondary user).",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of subrules 1.10B(1) and (2), the additional criterion for a CDR\nconsumer to be eligible in relation to a particular data holder in the banking\nsector or the NBL sector at a particular time, is that the account mentioned in\nparagraph 1.10B(1)(b) or (2)(b) is set up in such a way that, at that time, it can be\naccessed online.\nNote:\nRule 1.10B provides, among other things, that a person is eligible in relation to a data\nholder if the person is:\n(a)\nan account holder or secondary user for an account with the data holder; or\n(b)\na partner in a partnership that has an account with the data holder (whether or not\nthe person is an account holder or secondary user).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2fddc099d2311b7fd0ba9b8f6e5361eefd8f48c416caae23691951c735cba75f",
      "skos:note": "Account must be accessible online for a CDR consumer to be eligible in relation to a data holder."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-2-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 1  Additional criteria for eligibility—banking and NBL sectors",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 184,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of subrules 1.10B(1) and (2), the additional criterion for a CDR\nconsumer to be eligible in relation to a particular data holder in the banking\nsector or the NBL sector at a particular time, is that the account mentioned in\nparagraph 1.10B(1)(b) or (2)(b) is set up in such a way that, at that time, it can be\naccessed online.\nNote:\nRule 1.10B provides, among other things, that a person is eligible in relation to a data\nholder if the person is:\n(a)\nan account holder or secondary user for an account with the data holder; or\n(b)\na partner in a partnership that has an account with the data holder (whether or not\nthe person is an account holder or secondary user)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Account must be accessible online.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 2  Meaning of account privileges—banking and NBL sectors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-2-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause is made for the purposes of the definition of account privileges in\nsubrule 1.7(1).\n(2) For the banking sector and NBL sector, a person has account privileges in\nrelation to an account the person holds with a data holder in either of those\nsectors if:\n(a) the account is, or is for, a covered product; and\n(b) the person is able to make transactions on the account.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This clause is made for the purposes of the definition of account privileges in\nsubrule 1.7(1).\n(2) For the banking sector and NBL sector, a person has account privileges in\nrelation to an account the person holds with a data holder in either of those\nsectors if:\n(a) the account is, or is for, a covered product; and\n(b) the person is able to make transactions on the account.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-5-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ddd9dc260aefe98a9f3c590c525a70f38244d6973f3a0d3c5cdd17e33d4c5374"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-2-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 2  Meaning of account privileges—banking and NBL sectors",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 184,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause is made for the purposes of the definition of account privileges in\nsubrule 1.7(1).\n(2) For the banking sector and NBL sector, a person has account privileges in\nrelation to an account the person holds with a data holder in either of those\nsectors if:\n(a) the account is, or is for, a covered product; and\n(b) the person is able to make transactions on the account."
    },
