        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-5-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-5-ss-2-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "549f354d2502af399ad11dc7043963fadead6f5b1f06c0754bd5eb023767de3e",
      "skos:note": "Person has account privileges in relation to an account held with a data holder in either sector if the account is for a covered product and the person can make transactions on the account."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-2-5-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2(2) 2  Meaning of account privileges—banking and NBL sectors",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 184,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the banking sector and NBL sector, a person has account privileges in\nrelation to an account the person holds with a data holder in either of those\nsectors if:\n(a) the account is, or is for, a covered product; and\n(b) the person is able to make transactions on the account."
    },
