    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 3  Consumer dashboard—application of rule 1.15",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-2-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of subrule 1.15(1), if a data holder in the banking sector or NBL\nsector receives a consumer data request from an accredited person on behalf of a\nCDR consumer who is eligible in relation to the data holder, the data holder must\nprovide the CDR consumer with a consumer dashboard.\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nCDR data that may be accessed under these rules in relation to the banking sector and NBL sector",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of subrule 1.15(1), if a data holder in the banking sector or NBL\nsector receives a consumer data request from an accredited person on behalf of a\nCDR consumer who is eligible in relation to the data holder, the data holder must\nprovide the CDR consumer with a consumer dashboard.\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nCDR data that may be accessed under these rules in relation to the banking sector and NBL sector",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9792cc722638face1e51de8108b2b6b21226bb7ce2aa86e58ecf87cbda11ed7b",
      "skos:note": "Data holder must provide CDR consumer with a consumer dashboard.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-2-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 3  Consumer dashboard—application of rule 1.15",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 184,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of subrule 1.15(1), if a data holder in the banking sector or NBL\nsector receives a consumer data request from an accredited person on behalf of a\nCDR consumer who is eligible in relation to the data holder, the data holder must\nprovide the CDR consumer with a consumer dashboard.\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nCDR data that may be accessed under these rules in relation to the banking sector and NBL sector"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-2-6-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 1  Meaning of required product data and voluntary product data—banking sector",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-3-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.185",
      "values:originalText": "and NBL sector\n(1) Required product data, in relation to the banking sector or the NBL sector,\nmeans CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers:\n(a) that is banking sector data or NBL sector data (as applicable); and\n(b) that is product specific data about a covered product (other than a covered\nproduct mentioned in subclause (2)); and\n(c) that is held by the data holder in a digital form.\nNote:\nProduct data can only be required to be disclosed if the data is about the eligibility\ncriteria, terms and conditions, price, availability or performance of a covered product,\nor if the data is about availability or performance and is publicly available (see section\n56BF of the Act).\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), the covered products mentioned in this\nsubclause are:\n(a) a foreign currency account; and\n(b) a consumer lease; and\n(c) a reverse mortgage; and\n(d) a margin loan; and\n(e) asset finance that is non-standard vehicle finance (for example, a novated\nlease).\n(3) Voluntary product data, in relation to the banking sector or the NBL sector,\nmeans CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers:\n(a) that is banking sector data or NBL sector data (as applicable); and\n(b) that is product specific data about a covered product; and\n(c) that is not required product data.",
      "skos:definition": "and NBL sector\n(1) Required product data, in relation to the banking sector or the NBL sector,\nmeans CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers:\n(a) that is banking sector data or NBL sector data (as applicable); and\n(b) that is product specific data about a covered product (other than a covered\nproduct mentioned in subclause (2)); and\n(c) that is held by the data holder in a digital form.\nNote:\nProduct data can only be required to be disclosed if the data is about the eligibility\ncriteria, terms and conditions, price, availability or performance of a covered product,\nor if the data is about availability or performance and is publicly available (see section\n56BF of the Act).\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), the covered products mentioned in this\nsubclause are:\n(a) a foreign currency account; and\n(b) a consumer lease; and\n(c) a reverse mortgage; and\n(d) a margin loan; and\n(e) asset finance that is non-standard vehicle finance (for example, a novated\nlease).\n(3) Voluntary product data, in relation to the banking sector or the NBL sector,\nmeans CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers:\n(a) that is banking sector data or NBL sector data (as applicable); and\n(b) that is product specific data about a covered product; and\n(c) that is not required product data.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-3-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-3-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-3-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "522c0d063f0106a34e2ab95a0457e3568cb43017bf684c96feca4dcf93e3b86e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-3-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 1  Meaning of required product data and voluntary product data—banking sector",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 185,
      "values:originalText": "and NBL sector\n(1) Required product data, in relation to the banking sector or the NBL sector,\nmeans CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers:\n(a) that is banking sector data or NBL sector data (as applicable); and\n(b) that is product specific data about a covered product (other than a covered\nproduct mentioned in subclause (2)); and\n(c) that is held by the data holder in a digital form.\nNote:\nProduct data can only be required to be disclosed if the data is about the eligibility\ncriteria, terms and conditions, price, availability or performance of a covered product,\nor if the data is about availability or performance and is publicly available (see section\n56BF of the Act).\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), the covered products mentioned in this\nsubclause are:\n(a) a foreign currency account; and\n(b) a consumer lease; and\n(c) a reverse mortgage; and\n(d) a margin loan; and\n(e) asset finance that is non-standard vehicle finance (for example, a novated\nlease).\n(3) Voluntary product data, in relation to the banking sector or the NBL sector,\nmeans CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers:\n(a) that is banking sector data or NBL sector data (as applicable); and\n(b) that is product specific data about a covered product; and\n(c) that is not required product data."
    },
