    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 2  Meaning of required consumer data and voluntary consumer data—banking",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-3-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.185",
      "values:originalText": "and NBL sectors\n(1) A relevant account, in relation to a CDR consumer, means an account that is\nheld with a data holder of banking sector data or NBL sector data and is, or is\nfor, a covered product, and that:\n(a) is held in the name of the CDR consumer alone; or\n(b) is a joint account of which the CDR consumer is one of the account\nholders; or\n(c) is a partnership account for a partnership in which the CDR consumer is a\npartner; or\n(d) is an account for which the CDR consumer is a secondary user;\nwhether or not the account can be accessed online, and, subject to subclauses (6)\nand (7), whether or not the account is open.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "skos:definition": "and NBL sectors\n(1) A relevant account, in relation to a CDR consumer, means an account that is\nheld with a data holder of banking sector data or NBL sector data and is, or is\nfor, a covered product, and that:\n(a) is held in the name of the CDR consumer alone; or\n(b) is a joint account of which the CDR consumer is one of the account\nholders; or\n(c) is a partnership account for a partnership in which the CDR consumer is a\npartner; or\n(d) is an account for which the CDR consumer is a secondary user;\nwhether or not the account can be accessed online, and, subject to subclauses (6)\nand (7), whether or not the account is open.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-4-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-4-logic-descriptionlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-4-logic-descriptionlogic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-3-4-logic-descriptionlogic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9bf50f68ff6d54edf588aa91044f3f8e41d8361d58e56ae2467ee35d94d0425f",
      "skos:note": "Defines a relevant account for CDR consumer purposes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-3-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 2  Meaning of required consumer data and voluntary consumer data—banking",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 185,
      "values:originalText": "and NBL sectors\n(1) A relevant account, in relation to a CDR consumer, means an account that is\nheld with a data holder of banking sector data or NBL sector data and is, or is\nfor, a covered product, and that:\n(a) is held in the name of the CDR consumer alone; or\n(b) is a joint account of which the CDR consumer is one of the account\nholders; or\n(c) is a partnership account for a partnership in which the CDR consumer is a\npartner; or\n(d) is an account for which the CDR consumer is a secondary user;\nwhether or not the account can be accessed online, and, subject to subclauses (6)\nand (7), whether or not the account is open.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors"
    },
