      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "824fdaf5b7082976313d97cbdb5b95217bf6d8edda8dd9ca6f884efd47e8da2d",
      "skos:note": "Lender must meet large provider qualification after first day of meeting the condition."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(2) 2  Meaning of initial provider and large provider",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subject to this clause, a relevant non-bank lender is a large provider on and after\nthe first day on which it meets the large provider qualification if, on that day, the\nlender:\n(a) is not an initial provider; and\n(b) meets the large provider qualification, as set out in subclause (3) or (4)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-2-norm",
