      "cml:premiseText": "(2) Subject to this clause, a relevant non-bank lender is a large provider on and after the first day on which it meets the large provider qualification if..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6(3) 2  Meaning of initial provider and large provider",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.190",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A relevant non-bank lender meets the large provider qualification on the\ncommencement day, or on a 1 July after that day (the relevant day), if:\n\n(a) each of the following is over $1 billion:\n(i) the total value of the resident loans and resident finance leases\nreported to the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority under the\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nApplication of these rules to the banking and NBL sectors  Part 6\nClause 6.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\napplicable standards by the lender and each of its associated non-bank\nlenders in relation to the most recent calendar month for which a\nreport was given to the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority\nbefore the relevant day;\n(ii) the total value of the resident loans and resident finance leases\nreported to the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority under the\napplicable standards by the lender and each of its associated non-bank\nlenders during the 12 months before the relevant day, averaged over\nthat period; and\n(b) the lender has more than 1,000 customers on that day.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A relevant non-bank lender meets the large provider qualification on the\ncommencement day, or on a 1 July after that day (the relevant day), if:\n\n(a) each of the following is over $1 billion:\n(i) the total value of the resident loans and resident finance leases\nreported to the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority under the\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nApplication of these rules to the banking and NBL sectors  Part 6\nClause 6.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\napplicable standards by the lender and each of its associated non-bank\nlenders in relation to the most recent calendar month for which a\nreport was given to the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority\nbefore the relevant day;\n(ii) the total value of the resident loans and resident finance leases\nreported to the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority under the\napplicable standards by the lender and each of its associated non-bank\nlenders during the 12 months before the relevant day, averaged over\nthat period; and\n(b) the lender has more than 1,000 customers on that day.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "183a505a1cf123259699d221c565febeb63035b2c5eb181d7b03444e1f759522",
      "skos:note": "Large provider qualification for non-bank lenders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(3) 2  Meaning of initial provider and large provider",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A relevant non-bank lender meets the large provider qualification on the\ncommencement day, or on a 1 July after that day (the relevant day), if:\n\n(a) each of the following is over $1 billion:\n(i) the total value of the resident loans and resident finance leases\nreported to the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority under the\n\nProvisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3\nApplication of these rules to the banking and NBL sectors  Part 6\nClause 6.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\napplicable standards by the lender and each of its associated non-bank\nlenders in relation to the most recent calendar month for which a\nreport was given to the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority\nbefore the relevant day;\n(ii) the total value of the resident loans and resident finance leases\nreported to the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority under the\napplicable standards by the lender and each of its associated non-bank\nlenders during the 12 months before the relevant day, averaged over\nthat period; and\n(b) the lender has more than 1,000 customers on that day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-3-norm",
