    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6(7) 2  Meaning of initial provider and large provider",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.190",
      "values:originalText": "(7) In this clause:\napplicable standards means the standards made by the Australian Prudential\nRegulation Authority under the Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001\ndealing with the provision of information to the Authority relating to the loans\nand finance leases of an ADI or registered financial corporation.\nNote:\nThe applicable standards were, in 2025, set out in the Financial Sector (Collection of\nData) (reporting standard) determination No. 9 of 2022 [F2022L00212].\nassociated non-bank lender: a relevant non-bank lender (the first lender) is an\nassociated non-bank lender of another relevant non-bank lender (the second\nlender) if any of the following apply:\n(a) the first lender is a related body corporate of the second lender for the\npurposes of the Act (see subsection 4A(5) of the Act);\n(b) the first lender has an arrangement with the second lender in relation to the\nadministration, offering, provision or underwriting of resident loans or\nresident finance leases;\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "skos:definition": "(7) In this clause:\napplicable standards means the standards made by the Australian Prudential\nRegulation Authority under the Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001\ndealing with the provision of information to the Authority relating to the loans\nand finance leases of an ADI or registered financial corporation.\nNote:\nThe applicable standards were, in 2025, set out in the Financial Sector (Collection of\nData) (reporting standard) determination No. 9 of 2022 [F2022L00212].\nassociated non-bank lender: a relevant non-bank lender (the first lender) is an\nassociated non-bank lender of another relevant non-bank lender (the second\nlender) if any of the following apply:\n(a) the first lender is a related body corporate of the second lender for the\npurposes of the Act (see subsection 4A(5) of the Act);\n(b) the first lender has an arrangement with the second lender in relation to the\nadministration, offering, provision or underwriting of resident loans or\nresident finance leases;\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-7-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-7-logic-descriptionlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-7-logic-alleninterval-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7f2346015a289fa914dc749f91f6c8a3bd8da13e950d52c2270e365cb24ad4e1",
      "skos:note": "Defines applicable standards and associated non-bank lenders."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-6-14-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(7) 2  Meaning of initial provider and large provider",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "(7) In this clause:\napplicable standards means the standards made by the Australian Prudential\nRegulation Authority under the Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001\ndealing with the provision of information to the Authority relating to the loans\nand finance leases of an ADI or registered financial corporation.\nNote:\nThe applicable standards were, in 2025, set out in the Financial Sector (Collection of\nData) (reporting standard) determination No. 9 of 2022 [F2022L00212].\nassociated non-bank lender: a relevant non-bank lender (the first lender) is an\nassociated non-bank lender of another relevant non-bank lender (the second\nlender) if any of the following apply:\n(a) the first lender is a related body corporate of the second lender for the\npurposes of the Act (see subsection 4A(5) of the Act);\n(b) the first lender has an arrangement with the second lender in relation to the\nadministration, offering, provision or underwriting of resident loans or\nresident finance leases;\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors"
    },
