    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 11  Disclosure of CDR data voluntarily",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-6-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.197",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A data holder in the banking sector or NBL sector, other than an excluded data\nholder, may notify the Commission that it wishes Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules\nto apply to it from a specified date.\n(2) The data holder, from that specified date, may:\n(a) receive a request under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules from a CDR\nconsumer who is eligible in relation to that data holder; and\n(b) disclose required or voluntary product or consumer data in response to the\nrequest.\n(3) These rules apply to the data holder in respect of that request, and all subsequent\nrequests under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules by consumers who are eligible in\nrelation to that data holder.\nNote:\nThis clause means that, among other things, a data holder who elects to receive and\nrespond to such a request must comply with all aspects of these rules relevant to\nhandling it (and all future requests by eligible consumers). For instance, the data holder\nwould need to provide the consumer dashboard in accordance with subrule 1.15(1)\nupon receiving a request under Part 4, and would need to meet the internal and external\ndispute resolution requirements.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A data holder in the banking sector or NBL sector, other than an excluded data\nholder, may notify the Commission that it wishes Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules\nto apply to it from a specified date.\n(2) The data holder, from that specified date, may:\n(a) receive a request under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules from a CDR\nconsumer who is eligible in relation to that data holder; and\n(b) disclose required or voluntary product or consumer data in response to the\nrequest.\n(3) These rules apply to the data holder in respect of that request, and all subsequent\nrequests under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules by consumers who are eligible in\nrelation to that data holder.\nNote:\nThis clause means that, among other things, a data holder who elects to receive and\nrespond to such a request must comply with all aspects of these rules relevant to\nhandling it (and all future requests by eligible consumers). For instance, the data holder\nwould need to provide the consumer dashboard in accordance with subrule 1.15(1)\nupon receiving a request under Part 4, and would need to meet the internal and external\ndispute resolution requirements.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-24-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-24-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-24-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1e477fda8bfc78b752604af19eb6a440615c1da21e27c3cf4712f7c6ad990d93"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-6-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 11  Disclosure of CDR data voluntarily",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 197,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A data holder in the banking sector or NBL sector, other than an excluded data\nholder, may notify the Commission that it wishes Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules\nto apply to it from a specified date.\n(2) The data holder, from that specified date, may:\n(a) receive a request under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules from a CDR\nconsumer who is eligible in relation to that data holder; and\n(b) disclose required or voluntary product or consumer data in response to the\nrequest.\n(3) These rules apply to the data holder in respect of that request, and all subsequent\nrequests under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules by consumers who are eligible in\nrelation to that data holder.\nNote:\nThis clause means that, among other things, a data holder who elects to receive and\nrespond to such a request must comply with all aspects of these rules relevant to\nhandling it (and all future requests by eligible consumers). For instance, the data holder\nwould need to provide the consumer dashboard in accordance with subrule 1.15(1)\nupon receiving a request under Part 4, and would need to meet the internal and external\ndispute resolution requirements.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors"
    },
