          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-24-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-24-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "70ebb1cb55660a6de57e9cd67ad74519575d8aacabe17713ab251508c6ee1c8c",
      "skos:note": "Comply with all aspects of these rules relevant to handling a request and future requests by eligible consumers.",
      "dc:description": "comply with all aspects of these rules"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-3-sec-6-24-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(3) 11  Disclosure of CDR data voluntarily",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 197,
      "values:originalText": "(3) These rules apply to the data holder in respect of that request, and all subsequent\nrequests under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules by consumers who are eligible in\nrelation to that data holder.\nNote:\nThis clause means that, among other things, a data holder who elects to receive and\nrespond to such a request must comply with all aspects of these rules relevant to\nhandling it (and all future requests by eligible consumers). For instance, the data holder\nwould need to provide the consumer dashboard in accordance with subrule 1.15(1)\nupon receiving a request under Part 4, and would need to meet the internal and external\ndispute resolution requirements.\n\nSchedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors"
    },
