        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Retailer must retail electricity during connection points",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Connection points are relevant for retailers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-43",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 5  Meaning of trial product",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-43"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.208",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For these rules, in relation to the energy sector, a plan is a trial product if the\nplan is offered:\n(a) with the description “pilot” or “trial”; and\n(b) with a statement that it will operate as a pilot or trial for a period that ends\nno more than 24 months after the initial offering (the trial period); and\n(c) on the basis that the number of customers to be supplied with the plan for\nthe purposes of the trial will be limited to no more than 2,000; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nPreliminary  Part 1\nClause 1.5\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(d) with a statement that the plan may be terminated before the end of the trial\nperiod and that, if it is, the CDR data in relation to the plan may not be\navailable for data sharing under these rules.\n(2) A plan will cease to be a trial product from the time any of the following occurs:\n(a) the plan is supplied or offered after the end of the trial period;\n(b) the plan begins to be supplied to more than 2,000 customers.\n\nSchedule 4  Provisions relevant to the energy sector",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For these rules, in relation to the energy sector, a plan is a trial product if the\nplan is offered:\n(a) with the description “pilot” or “trial”; and\n(b) with a statement that it will operate as a pilot or trial for a period that ends\nno more than 24 months after the initial offering (the trial period); and\n(c) on the basis that the number of customers to be supplied with the plan for\nthe purposes of the trial will be limited to no more than 2,000; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nPreliminary  Part 1\nClause 1.5\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(d) with a statement that the plan may be terminated before the end of the trial\nperiod and that, if it is, the CDR data in relation to the plan may not be\navailable for data sharing under these rules.\n(2) A plan will cease to be a trial product from the time any of the following occurs:\n(a) the plan is supplied or offered after the end of the trial period;\n(b) the plan begins to be supplied to more than 2,000 customers.\n\nSchedule 4  Provisions relevant to the energy sector",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-43-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-43-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3474acf7430a05f7ddd1aa5139c2ddb635d92723c9378e6ae1b7a235fd6d5e43"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-1-43",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 5  Meaning of trial product",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 208,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For these rules, in relation to the energy sector, a plan is a trial product if the\nplan is offered:\n(a) with the description “pilot” or “trial”; and\n(b) with a statement that it will operate as a pilot or trial for a period that ends\nno more than 24 months after the initial offering (the trial period); and\n(c) on the basis that the number of customers to be supplied with the plan for\nthe purposes of the trial will be limited to no more than 2,000; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nPreliminary  Part 1\nClause 1.5\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(d) with a statement that the plan may be terminated before the end of the trial\nperiod and that, if it is, the CDR data in relation to the plan may not be\navailable for data sharing under these rules.\n(2) A plan will cease to be a trial product from the time any of the following occurs:\n(a) the plan is supplied or offered after the end of the trial period;\n(b) the plan begins to be supplied to more than 2,000 customers.\n\nSchedule 4  Provisions relevant to the energy sector"
    },
