    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 2  Meaning of account privileges—energy sector",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-2-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.210",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause is made for the purposes of the definition of account privileges in\nsubrule 1.7(1) of these rules.\n(2) For the energy sector, a person has account privileges in relation to an account\nwith a retailer if the person is a customer authorised representative of the account\nholder for the purposes of:\n(a) rule 56A of the National Energy Retail Rules; or\n(b) Chapter 7 of the National Electricity Rules.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This clause is made for the purposes of the definition of account privileges in\nsubrule 1.7(1) of these rules.\n(2) For the energy sector, a person has account privileges in relation to an account\nwith a retailer if the person is a customer authorised representative of the account\nholder for the purposes of:\n(a) rule 56A of the National Energy Retail Rules; or\n(b) Chapter 7 of the National Electricity Rules.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-11-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-11-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b3fde3627a3985e732871fe5790e5cfb483843b5839a07324bb3bcd490e2b082"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-2-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 2  Meaning of account privileges—energy sector",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 210,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause is made for the purposes of the definition of account privileges in\nsubrule 1.7(1) of these rules.\n(2) For the energy sector, a person has account privileges in relation to an account\nwith a retailer if the person is a customer authorised representative of the account\nholder for the purposes of:\n(a) rule 56A of the National Energy Retail Rules; or\n(b) Chapter 7 of the National Electricity Rules."
    },
