    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 3  Consumer dashboard—application of rule 1.15",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-2-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.210",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For subrule 1.15(1), if a retailer receives a consumer data request from an\naccredited person on behalf of a CDR consumer who has online access to the\nrelevant account, the retailer must provide the CDR consumer with the consumer\ndashboard.\n(2) For subrule 1.15(1), if a retailer receives a consumer data request from an\naccredited person on behalf of a CDR consumer who does not have a consumer\ndashboard, the retailer must:\n(a) offer the CDR consumer a consumer dashboard; and\n(b) provide it if the CDR consumer accepts.\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nCDR data that may be accessed under these rules—energy sector  Part 3\nClause 3.1A\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For subrule 1.15(1), if a retailer receives a consumer data request from an\naccredited person on behalf of a CDR consumer who has online access to the\nrelevant account, the retailer must provide the CDR consumer with the consumer\ndashboard.\n(2) For subrule 1.15(1), if a retailer receives a consumer data request from an\naccredited person on behalf of a CDR consumer who does not have a consumer\ndashboard, the retailer must:\n(a) offer the CDR consumer a consumer dashboard; and\n(b) provide it if the CDR consumer accepts.\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nCDR data that may be accessed under these rules—energy sector  Part 3\nClause 3.1A\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-12-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-12-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6125972a4ebee94e2219d0cc76e283451a898fdcffa01928af0f5a0fdb308716"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-2-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 3  Consumer dashboard—application of rule 1.15",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 210,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For subrule 1.15(1), if a retailer receives a consumer data request from an\naccredited person on behalf of a CDR consumer who has online access to the\nrelevant account, the retailer must provide the CDR consumer with the consumer\ndashboard.\n(2) For subrule 1.15(1), if a retailer receives a consumer data request from an\naccredited person on behalf of a CDR consumer who does not have a consumer\ndashboard, the retailer must:\n(a) offer the CDR consumer a consumer dashboard; and\n(b) provide it if the CDR consumer accepts.\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nCDR data that may be accessed under these rules—energy sector  Part 3\nClause 3.1A\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020"
    },
