    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 2  Meeting external dispute resolution requirements—energy sector",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-43"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.216",
      "values:originalText": "Note:\nSchemes operated by the Australian Financial Complaints Authority Limited and the energy and water\nombudsman of each State and Territory are recognised as external dispute resolution schemes for section\n56DA of the Act.\nHow accredited persons and retailers meet the external dispute resolution\nrequirements\n(1) For the energy sector, persons of the following kinds meet the external dispute\nresolution requirements in the circumstances indicated:\n(a) an accredited person that is not a retailer—if it is an AFCA member;\n(b) a retailer that is not an accredited person—if it is an EWO member;\n(c) an accredited person that is also a retailer, but not a limited retailer—if it is\nboth an AFCA member and an EWO member;\n(d) an accredited person that is also a limited retailer—if it is an EWO\nmember.\nMeaning of AFCA member\n(2) In this clause, a retailer or an accredited person is an AFCA member if it is a\nmember of the recognised external dispute resolution scheme operated by the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority Limited for the energy sector.\nMeaning of EWO member\n(3) In this clause, a retailer or accredited person is an EWO member if, in each\nrelevant jurisdiction:\n(a) if the jurisdiction has an energy and water ombudsman recognised in\naccordance with section 56DA of the Act—the retailer is a member of the\nexternal dispute resolution scheme operated by that ombudsman in relation\nto CDR consumer complaints; and\n(b) otherwise—the retailer has taken the necessary steps to participate in the\ndispute resolution process provided by the jurisdiction that is appropriate\nfor CDR consumer complaints.\nMeaning of limited retailer\n(4) A retailer is a limited retailer if:\n(a) it uses any energy sector CDR data that it collects only in order to provide\ngoods or services within the energy sector; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nDispute resolution—energy sector  Part 5\nClause 5.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(b) it does not use non-energy sector CDR data that it collects in order to\nprovide goods or services outside the energy sector.\n\nSchedule 4  Provisions relevant to the energy sector",
      "skos:definition": "Note:\nSchemes operated by the Australian Financial Complaints Authority Limited and the energy and water\nombudsman of each State and Territory are recognised as external dispute resolution schemes for section\n56DA of the Act.\nHow accredited persons and retailers meet the external dispute resolution\nrequirements\n(1) For the energy sector, persons of the following kinds meet the external dispute\nresolution requirements in the circumstances indicated:\n(a) an accredited person that is not a retailer—if it is an AFCA member;\n(b) a retailer that is not an accredited person—if it is an EWO member;\n(c) an accredited person that is also a retailer, but not a limited retailer—if it is\nboth an AFCA member and an EWO member;\n(d) an accredited person that is also a limited retailer—if it is an EWO\nmember.\nMeaning of AFCA member\n(2) In this clause, a retailer or an accredited person is an AFCA member if it is a\nmember of the recognised external dispute resolution scheme operated by the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority Limited for the energy sector.\nMeaning of EWO member\n(3) In this clause, a retailer or accredited person is an EWO member if, in each\nrelevant jurisdiction:\n(a) if the jurisdiction has an energy and water ombudsman recognised in\naccordance with section 56DA of the Act—the retailer is a member of the\nexternal dispute resolution scheme operated by that ombudsman in relation\nto CDR consumer complaints; and\n(b) otherwise—the retailer has taken the necessary steps to participate in the\ndispute resolution process provided by the jurisdiction that is appropriate\nfor CDR consumer complaints.\nMeaning of limited retailer\n(4) A retailer is a limited retailer if:\n(a) it uses any energy sector CDR data that it collects only in order to provide\ngoods or services within the energy sector; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nDispute resolution—energy sector  Part 5\nClause 5.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(b) it does not us",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "677ce5ce418bd9ce28c6938662eb1bd107191427091bc2b1a06fc043176a01c9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-43",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 2  Meeting external dispute resolution requirements—energy sector",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 216,
      "values:originalText": "Note:\nSchemes operated by the Australian Financial Complaints Authority Limited and the energy and water\nombudsman of each State and Territory are recognised as external dispute resolution schemes for section\n56DA of the Act.\nHow accredited persons and retailers meet the external dispute resolution\nrequirements\n(1) For the energy sector, persons of the following kinds meet the external dispute\nresolution requirements in the circumstances indicated:\n(a) an accredited person that is not a retailer—if it is an AFCA member;\n(b) a retailer that is not an accredited person—if it is an EWO member;\n(c) an accredited person that is also a retailer, but not a limited retailer—if it is\nboth an AFCA member and an EWO member;\n(d) an accredited person that is also a limited retailer—if it is an EWO\nmember.\nMeaning of AFCA member\n(2) In this clause, a retailer or an accredited person is an AFCA member if it is a\nmember of the recognised external dispute resolution scheme operated by the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority Limited for the energy sector.\nMeaning of EWO member\n(3) In this clause, a retailer or accredited person is an EWO member if, in each\nrelevant jurisdiction:\n(a) if the jurisdiction has an energy and water ombudsman recognised in\naccordance with section 56DA of the Act—the retailer is a member of the\nexternal dispute resolution scheme operated by that ombudsman in relation\nto CDR consumer complaints; and\n(b) otherwise—the retailer has taken the necessary steps to participate in the\ndispute resolution process provided by the jurisdiction that is appropriate\nfor CDR consumer complaints.\nMeaning of limited retailer\n(4) A retailer is a limited retailer if:\n(a) it uses any energy sector CDR data that it collects only in order to provide\ngoods or services within the energy sector; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nDispute resolution—energy sector  Part 5\nClause 5.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(b) it does not use non-energy sector CDR data that it collects in order to\nprovide goods or services outside the energy sector.\n\nSchedule 4  Provisions relevant to the energy sector"
    },
