        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5(3) 2  Meeting external dispute resolution requirements—energy sector",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.216",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In this clause, a retailer or accredited person is an EWO member if, in each\nrelevant jurisdiction:\n(a) if the jurisdiction has an energy and water ombudsman recognised in\naccordance with section 56DA of the Act—the retailer is a member of the\nexternal dispute resolution scheme operated by that ombudsman in relation\nto CDR consumer complaints; and\n(b) otherwise—the retailer has taken the necessary steps to participate in the\ndispute resolution process provided by the jurisdiction that is appropriate\nfor CDR consumer complaints.\nMeaning of limited retailer",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In this clause, a retailer or accredited person is an EWO member if, in each\nrelevant jurisdiction:\n(a) if the jurisdiction has an energy and water ombudsman recognised in\naccordance with section 56DA of the Act—the retailer is a member of the\nexternal dispute resolution scheme operated by that ombudsman in relation\nto CDR consumer complaints; and\n(b) otherwise—the retailer has taken the necessary steps to participate in the\ndispute resolution process provided by the jurisdiction that is appropriate\nfor CDR consumer complaints.\nMeaning of limited retailer",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3-logic-argumentation-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "540bae4629a39e4c18173f5e53636f6552c6f88b97fc0af73db1e3b1d4e32534",
      "skos:note": "Retailer must participate in external dispute resolution process."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(3) 2  Meeting external dispute resolution requirements—energy sector",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 216,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In this clause, a retailer or accredited person is an EWO member if, in each\nrelevant jurisdiction:\n(a) if the jurisdiction has an energy and water ombudsman recognised in\naccordance with section 56DA of the Act—the retailer is a member of the\nexternal dispute resolution scheme operated by that ombudsman in relation\nto CDR consumer complaints; and\n(b) otherwise—the retailer has taken the necessary steps to participate in the\ndispute resolution process provided by the jurisdiction that is appropriate\nfor CDR consumer complaints.\nMeaning of limited retailer"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must participate",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Retailer is an EWO member if necessary steps are taken.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Participation in dispute resolution process is obligatory."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "BETWEEN",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal interval for participation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Participation in dispute resolution process must occur within relevant jurisdiction.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Temporal interval for participation is between relevant jurisdiction and retailer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-3-logic-argumentation-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "IMPLIES",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Implication of membership",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Membership in external dispute resolution scheme implies participation.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Participation in dispute resolution process is implied by membership."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5(4) 2  Meeting external dispute resolution requirements—energy sector",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.216",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A retailer is a limited retailer if:\n(a) it uses any energy sector CDR data that it collects only in order to provide\ngoods or services within the energy sector; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nDispute resolution—energy sector  Part 5\nClause 5.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(b) it does not use non-energy sector CDR data that it collects in order to\nprovide goods or services outside the energy sector.\n\nSchedule 4  Provisions relevant to the energy sector",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A retailer is a limited retailer if:\n(a) it uses any energy sector CDR data that it collects only in order to provide\ngoods or services within the energy sector; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nDispute resolution—energy sector  Part 5\nClause 5.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(b) it does not use non-energy sector CDR data that it collects in order to\nprovide goods or services outside the energy sector.\n\nSchedule 4  Provisions relevant to the energy sector",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-4-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-4-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-4-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5ee125783051f077ee273b7f9a5f46d41c61f61eb23433e9c40641d46339cd16",
      "skos:note": "Retailer must use energy sector CDR data only for energy sector purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-5-43-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5(4) 2  Meeting external dispute resolution requirements—energy sector",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 216,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A retailer is a limited retailer if:\n(a) it uses any energy sector CDR data that it collects only in order to provide\ngoods or services within the energy sector; and\n\nProvisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4\nDispute resolution—energy sector  Part 5\nClause 5.2\nCompetition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020\n(b) it does not use non-energy sector CDR data that it collects in order to\nprovide goods or services outside the energy sector.\n\nSchedule 4  Provisions relevant to the energy sector"
    },
