    {
      "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-8-22",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 3  Meaning of larger retailer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-8-22"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.221",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part:\n(a) a retailer that had 10,000 or more small customers on the amendment day\nis a larger retailer; and\n(b) a retailer that had 10,000 or more small customers at all times during a\nfinancial year that begins on or after the amendment day is also a larger\nretailer on and from the day 12 months after the end of that financial year.\n(2) In this clause:\n(a) a person is a small customer of a retailer if the person is:\n(i) a domestic or small business customer of the retailer within the\nmeaning given in section 3 of the Electricity Industry Act 2000 (Vic);\nor\n(ii) a small customer of the retailer within the meaning of section 5 of the\nNational Energy Retail Law; and\n(b) the amendment day is the day on which Schedule 1 to the Competition and\nConsumer (Consumer Data Right) Amendment Rules (No. 2) 2021\ncommenced.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Part:\n(a) a retailer that had 10,000 or more small customers on the amendment day\nis a larger retailer; and\n(b) a retailer that had 10,000 or more small customers at all times during a\nfinancial year that begins on or after the amendment day is also a larger\nretailer on and from the day 12 months after the end of that financial year.\n(2) In this clause:\n(a) a person is a small customer of a retailer if the person is:\n(i) a domestic or small business customer of the retailer within the\nmeaning given in section 3 of the Electricity Industry Act 2000 (Vic);\nor\n(ii) a small customer of the retailer within the meaning of section 5 of the\nNational Energy Retail Law; and\n(b) the amendment day is the day on which Schedule 1 to the Competition and\nConsumer (Consumer Data Right) Amendment Rules (No. 2) 2021\ncommenced.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-8-22-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-8-22-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9488c79faccdea33c08504f30010b5a3985406be84c5021e2ff35ddce1299239"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sch-4-sec-8-22",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 3  Meaning of larger retailer",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 221,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part:\n(a) a retailer that had 10,000 or more small customers on the amendment day\nis a larger retailer; and\n(b) a retailer that had 10,000 or more small customers at all times during a\nfinancial year that begins on or after the amendment day is also a larger\nretailer on and from the day 12 months after the end of that financial year.\n(2) In this clause:\n(a) a person is a small customer of a retailer if the person is:\n(i) a domestic or small business customer of the retailer within the\nmeaning given in section 3 of the Electricity Industry Act 2000 (Vic);\nor\n(ii) a small customer of the retailer within the meaning of section 5 of the\nNational Energy Retail Law; and\n(b) the amendment day is the day on which Schedule 1 to the Competition and\nConsumer (Consumer Data Right) Amendment Rules (No. 2) 2021\ncommenced."
    },
